window.TP_SEARCH = [{"t":"Where to go next","u":"index.html#next","x":"Server admin? Install & requirements, then Jev connection for the key and the costs, and Commands & permissions. Mob author? Quick start, then Profiles, tactics & contexts, Skills & intents and MythicMobs vocabulary. Looking for one key? Press / and search, or open the Profile reference and the config.yml reference.","k":"section","p":"ThePredict docs"},{"t":"What it never does","u":"index.html#never","x":"No effects. ThePredict never adds particles, sounds, glow, animations or markers, and never edits your skills or MythicMobs files. Tells and stances are signals (~onSignal:PREDICTOR_*) and placeholders that your own skills can react to. No hidden reads. It decides with what the mob could perceive: participants in range, visible details only with line of sight. A player's movement is read from what they actually do, never from raw keyboard input. No names to Jev. Jev receives bands and facts in English with aliases (player_1, entity_1 plus its species), never names, UUIDs, coordinates, Display names or MythicMobs IDs. No surprise costs. Without a key nothing leaves your server. With a key, every request fits the budgets you set in config.yml.","k":"section","p":"ThePredict docs"},{"t":"The fallback chain","u":"index.html#fallback-chain","x":"If Jev is slow, unsure or unreachable, the mob never freezes. It drops down a four-level chain and climbs back up on the next good answer. Level Shown as Who decides 1 JEV Jev's answer. 2 ALTERNATIVE The next valid option, or a contingency, of that same answer. 3 LOCAL The profile itself: active context and tactic priority, no network, no cost. 4 BASE The mob's base AI (its BaseAI or AIGoalSelectors). ThePredict does not control it. /thepredict inspect nearest tells you the current level and the last reason for a drop. The reasons are listed in Troubleshooting.","k":"section","p":"ThePredict docs"},{"t":"How it decides","u":"index.html#how-it-decides","x":"A deterministic engine does the heavy work every tick; Jev only makes the final pick among a few candidates it has prepared. 1 · ReadEvery 2 ticksTarget, distance band, health bands, shields, drawn bows, cooldowns, terrain. 2 · PrepareCandidate tacticsContexts filter, reach and readiness checks, duplicates merged, each option described in plain English. 3 · AskOne request per fightEvery 20 ticks or sooner when something changes. Jev returns a probability per option, plus \"what if\" contingencies. 4 · ActWithin ticksFires ready skills on their own cooldown, reacts to openings, re-checks reach and conditions before every cast. The mobs that fight the same players share one encounter and one request: a boss and its adds cost one request per heartbeat, with a question per mob. Requests never block the server.","k":"section","p":"ThePredict docs"},{"t":"Who does what","u":"index.html#who-does-what","x":"ThePredict does not replace MythicMobs. It sits on top of it and only takes the decisions. Who What it does MythicMobs Defines the mob, its skills, conditions, targeters, cooldowns, effects and projectiles. Picks the target with its threat table. Moves the mob with its goals and the native navigator. ThePredict Generates the mob's movement goals from the profile (they replace its AIGoalSelectors), picks the tactic, publishes the current intent through predictor* conditions, placeholders and signals, fires the skills at the right tick and adds threat for things MythicMobs does not measure. Jev (TypeSafe's decision model) Picks among the tactics that are valid right now and returns probabilities. It never executes anything. Optional: without a key, ThePredict decides locally, at no cost.","k":"section","p":"ThePredict docs"},{"t":"ThePredict docs","u":"index.html","x":"ThePredict (tP) is an addon for MythicMobs Premium 5.13.1 on Paper 26.2 with Java 25. Bind a mob to a short profile and it stops spamming skills on timers: it reads the fight every couple of ticks, keeps its spacing, backs off, flanks a raised shield, punishes a target that drinks, and fires each skill the moment it makes sense. Info Release candidate ThePredict 0.0.1 is a release candidate. These pages describe what this build does, checked against its source code, but it has not been verified on a live Paper server yet. A key marked no effect yet is accepted but not used by this build. If your server behaves differently from what you read here, that is a bug worth reporting (see Troubleshooting & status). Quick startYour first smart mob in three lines, then the bundled example boss. InstallRequirements, first start, where files live, migrating old configs. Skills & intentsThe one-line Intention that tells ThePredict what a skill is for. Profile referenceEvery profile key with type, default and range. config.yml referenceEvery global key, read straight from the plugin's sources. TroubleshootingStatus lines, fallback reasons and common mistakes.","k":"page","p":"ThePredict docs"},{"t":"Turning it off","u":"install.html#disable","x":"One mob: set Predictor: false in its MythicMobs file and run /mm reload. ThePredict closes the session, removes its goals and MythicMobs puts the mob's own AIGoalSelectors back. Removing the mob's profile from Profiles/ and running /mm reload does the same. The whole plugin: remove the JAR and restart. On shutdown ThePredict stops its task, cancels requests in flight, sets every predictor* condition to false, releases the goals of its sessions, stops a duel recording, flushes records and aggregates, and closes the Jev client last. It can take a couple of seconds longer while scenario recording or the records writer is flushing. No key: nothing leaves the server, and bound mobs fight with their profile's local planner.","k":"section","p":"Install & requirements"},{"t":"Migrating from schema 1","u":"install.html#schema-1","x":"There is no migration command: ThePredict never changes your files. When it finds schema 1 files (a master file with a provider section or other old keys, or profiles with Behaviors, Operations or no Tactics), it does not load them and writes the same kind of proposal as above, already converted to schema 2 and to the new paths. How to apply a proposal: Stop the server and keep a copy of plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/ and of any old plugins/ThePredict/config.yml and AI/ files. Read every decision in report.md and fix what it lists under manual review. Copy each .proposed file into plugins/MythicMobs/ and remove the .proposed extension (AIConfig/config.yml.proposed becomes plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.yml). Set TYPESAFE_API_KEY yourself. A key from the old provider is never copied, because it is not a TypeSafe key. Start the server and run /thepredict status. Keep the old files until status no longer asks for the proposal. What the converter does: the provider section becomes jev with the tested model and an empty key; limits with an equivalent move over when they fit the new ranges (for example decision.maxConcurrentRequests becomes decision.maxInFlightRequests, profileDefaults.decisionIntervalTicks becomes minimumDecisionIntervalTicks, profileDefaults.lowHealthRatio becomes criticalHealthRatio); keys without an equivalent are listed with the reason; each old choice becomes a tactic without movement; each Operation becomes the matching shortcut context; DirectChoice becomes DirectTactic. After migrating, give your tactics a movement (see Movement & goals).","k":"section","p":"Install & requirements"},{"t":"Moving from the old location","u":"install.html#old-location","x":"Older builds kept their files in plugins/ThePredict/config.yml and plugins/ThePredict/AI/. ThePredict never moves or deletes them; what happens depends on where your files are: Only the old location has content (the master file, or a .yml in AI/): ThePredict loads nothing from it, enables no requests and writes a proposal in plugins/ThePredict/migration/<yyyyMMdd-HHmmss>/ with AIConfig/config.yml.proposed, one AIConfig/Profiles/<file>.proposed per profile and a report.md. The console says Migration proposal: review <report> and the .proposed files next to it, then copy them into plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/ by hand. No file was changed and no query was enabled. The same proposal is reused on every start while your files do not change. Both locations have content: AIConfig/ wins. The console, /thepredict status and the join notice say Old files in plugins/ThePredict/config.yml and plugins/ThePredict/AI/ are ignored because plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/ already has configuration. Nothing was moved or deleted. Only the new location has content: no notice. README.txt and example.yml.example do not count as content.","k":"section","p":"Install & requirements"},{"t":"Reloads and restarts","u":"install.html#reloads","x":"You changed Do this config.yml or the key Restart the server. Both are read only at startup. /thepredict check re-checks the service with the key already loaded; it does not read a new one. A profile /mm reload. It re-reads MythicMobs mobs and skills, then re-reads and re-binds every profile. A mob or a skill /mm reload. A datapack tag used in a selector /minecraft:reload, then /mm reload. There is no /thepredict reload. Watch out A broken config.yml keeps ThePredict off An unknown key, a key from the old schema or a value out of range keeps ThePredict inactive, and the console names the problem: Invalid configuration: AIConfig/config.yml: <path>: <reason>. ThePredict stays inactive and /thepredict status still works. MythicMobs keeps working, and storage is not opened (no records/, no aggregates.db). Fix the file and restart.","k":"section","p":"Install & requirements"},{"t":"Where things live","u":"install.html#files","x":"People edit files in the MythicMobs data folder; ThePredict keeps everything it generates in its own folder. Outside AIConfig/, ThePredict writes nothing inside plugins/MythicMobs/. What Where Master configuration plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.yml Profiles (.yml and .yaml) plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/ Profile template Profiles/README.txt and Profiles/example.yml.example (not loaded) Example boss plugins/ThePredict/examples/ Records, backups, exports plugins/ThePredict/records/ (with backups/, exports/ and a .lock) Aggregates database plugins/ThePredict/aggregates.db, beside records/, not inside Duels, scenarios, migration proposals plugins/ThePredict/duels/, scenarios/, migration/ Learning and overlays plugins/ThePredict/learn/, plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/","k":"section","p":"Install & requirements"},{"t":"Install","u":"install.html#install-steps","x":"Put the ThePredict JAR (for example ThePredict-{{fact:plugin.version}}.jar) in plugins/, next to MythicMobs Premium. Start the server. The first start creates only the files that are missing and never replaces one that exists: plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.yml: the master file (schema 2, empty key, tested model). plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/README.txt and Profiles/example.yml.example: a profile template, ignored until you copy it to a .yml file. plugins/ThePredict/examples/: the example boss (a mob, its skills and its profile), inactive where it is. examples/README.txt explains how to try it. Read the console. A fresh install is not an error; each line says what to do next: Console Jev not configured: set TYPESAFE_API_KEY or jev.apiKey. MythicMobs works normally. Next: set the key and restart the server, then run /thepredict status. No profiles: copy examples/ or create a .yml file in plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/. Next: read plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/README.txt. With profiles but no mob set to Predictor: true yet, it says <n> profiles read, but no mob targeted by a profile has Predictor: true. Next: set Predictor: true on the MythicMobs mob and run /mm reload. Optional: set the Jev key and restart (see Jev connection). With a key, ThePredict checks the service without spending tokens and reports, for example: Jev check: READY (credential valid; model unverified until first inference). Decisions are enabled. Continue with the Quick start. An administrator with thepredict.admin who joins gets one line when something needs attention, for examp","k":"section","p":"Install & requirements"},{"t":"Requirements","u":"install.html#requirements","x":"Component Version Notes Java 25 or newer Checked at startup. Paper 26.2 Folia is not supported. MythicMobs Premium 5.13.1 or newer Required dependency (depend: [MythicMobs]). A TypeSafe key — Optional. Only needed for Jev to decide; without it mobs fight with their profile's local planner, at no cost. See Jev connection. The combination tested while building this release is Java 25, Paper 26.2 (build 129), MythicMobs Premium 5.13.1 and the Jev model jev-1.13.0. Any other combination is untested. A wrong version disables the plugin at startup with one of these lines: Console Startup prerequisite failed: Java <n> is unsupported; ThePredict requires Java 25 or newer Startup prerequisite failed: Minecraft <version> is unsupported; this Paper build requires 26.2 or newer Startup prerequisite failed: MythicMobs <version> is unsupported; minimum version is 5.13.1","k":"section","p":"Install & requirements"},{"t":"Next steps","u":"quick-start.html#next","x":"Profiles, tactics & contexts: tactics, contexts and how Jev sees each option. Movement & goals: what each movement does and the goals it generates. Skills & intents: the full Intention vocabulary and how ThePredict casts. MythicMobs vocabulary: conditions, placeholders and signals for your own skills.","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"Remove the example","u":"quick-start.html#remove-example","x":"Delete the three copied files and run /mm reload.","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"Force a tactic","u":"quick-start.html#debug-intent","x":"To try one tactic without Jev, a player with thepredict.debug (or the console, with the mob's UUID) can pin it and release it: Console /thepredict debug intent nearest keep_distance /thepredict debug release nearest A debug intent is local and never sends a request to Jev. thepredict.debug is not given to operators by default; see Commands & permissions.","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"What to read in inspect","u":"quick-start.html#inspect","x":"Line What it tells you Goals The goal set ThePredict generated from the profile: float, fleeConditional, moveWithinConditional, moveTowardsTargetConditional, goToSpawnLocation, meleeAttack, randomStroll, lookAtTarget and the goals thepredict:flank, thepredict:hold and thepredict:owner. Session The control level: LOCAL without a key, JEV with one. Intent The tactic, its movement, the ticks left and whether its skill was tried. Why The last fallback reason and the last cast result: they explain a LOCAL or BASE level. Threat The MythicMobs threat table and the threat ThePredict added for assists, blocked hits and ranged harass.","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"The files","u":"quick-start.html#guardian-files","x":"plugins/MythicMobs/Mobs/ThePredictGuardian.ymlYAML # ThePredict 0.0.1 example boss. Predictor starts false: the mob fights as a plain MythicMobs zombie. # ThePredict generates its movement goals when Predictor is true; do not add AIGoalSelectors here. ThePredictGuardian: Type: ZOMBIE Display: 'ThePredict Guardian' Health: 100 Damage: 3 Predictor: false Options: FollowRange: 32 PreventOtherDrops: true Modules: ThreatTable: true ThreatTable: UseDamageTaken: true DecayUnreachable: false Skills: - damage{a=2} @target ~onAttack - setstance{stance=pressing} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_STANCE_PRESSING - setstance{stance=guarded} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_STANCE_GUARDED - setstance{stance=evasive} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_STANCE_EVASIVE plugins/MythicMobs/Skills/ThePredictGuardianSkills.ymlYAML # Skills of the ThePredict Guardian. ThePredict casts them with its own trigger; the mob never casts them # with a normal trigger. Each skill declares its Intention. PredictValues stay as history and are not read. # Cooldown is the native one, in seconds. The slam hits players only (@PlayersInRadius). ThePredictGuardianMelee: Intention: DAMAGE, MELEE, DAMAGE_MEDIUM, WHEN_TARGET_IN_MELEE PredictValues: [MELEE_ATTACK, SINGLE_TARGET, MEDIUM_DAMAGE] Cooldown: 2 Skills: - effect:particles{p=crit;a=12;hs=0.4;vs=0.4;y=1} @self - delay 5 - damage{a=6} @target ThePredictGuardianRanged: Intention: DAMAGE, HITSCAN, DAMAGE_LOW, WHEN_TARGET_FLEEING, WHEN_TARGET_AT_RANGE, RISK_NEEDS_LINE_OF_SIGHT PredictValues: [RANGED_ATTACK, SINGLE_TARGET, LOW_DAMAGE] Cooldown: 3 Conditions: - targetwithin{d=16} true Tar","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"Try it","u":"quick-start.html#try-it","x":"Copy the three files: MythicMobs/Mobs/ThePredictGuardian.yml into plugins/MythicMobs/Mobs/, MythicMobs/Skills/ThePredictGuardianSkills.yml into plugins/MythicMobs/Skills/, and AI/ThePredictGuardian.yml into plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/. Run /mm reload, then /thepredict status. The mob still has Predictor: false, so the profile is read but not active. On a fresh install the Catalog section shows (the revision number varies): Console Profiles: SETUP_PENDING (revision N, 1 profiles read, 0 active, 0 errors, 0 warnings): no mob targeted by a profile has Predictor: true; set it in MythicMobs and reload MythicMobs Spawn it with /mm m spawn ThePredictGuardian 1. With Predictor: false it is a plain MythicMobs zombie: it chases you and hits with its own attack. Set Predictor: true in the copied mob file, run /mm reload and /thepredict status: Console Profiles: LOADED (revision N, 1 profiles read, 1 active, 0 errors, 0 warnings) Fight it in survival and run /thepredict inspect nearest (it looks for the closest bound mob within 16 blocks).","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"The example boss","u":"quick-start.html#example-boss","x":"ThePredict ships a complete example, the ThePredict Guardian: a zombie with four skills (a melee strike, a ranged bolt, a self-heal and an area slam) and a profile with eight tactics. The first start writes it to plugins/ThePredict/examples/, where it stays inactive.","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"Your first smart mob","u":"quick-start.html#first-mob","x":"You add three things on your side: one key in the mob, one line in each skill, and a short profile. That is it: no timers, no AIGoalSelectors, no extra skills. 1. In the mob file, turn ThePredict on: plugins/MythicMobs/Mobs/Brute.ymlYAML Brute: Type: ZOMBIE Display: 'Brute' Health: 80 Predictor: true Modules: ThreatTable: true 2. In each skill, say what it is for with one Intention line, and keep its native Cooldown: plugins/MythicMobs/Skills/Brute.ymlYAML BruteSmash: Intention: DAMAGE, MELEE, DAMAGE_MEDIUM Cooldown: 2 Skills: - delay 4 - damage{a=7} @target 3. A profile tells ThePredict which mob it drives and which tactics it may pick: plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/brute.ymlYAML schemaVersion: 2 brute_ai: MythicID: Brute Objective: Defeat the current target Choices: smash: { MythicID: BruteSmash } Tactics: press_and_smash: { Movement: APPROACH, Choice: smash } hold: { Movement: HOLD } Then run /mm reload and /thepredict status. The Catalog section should report the profile as LOADED with one profile active and no errors. Spawn the mob, fight it in survival and run /thepredict inspect nearest. Tip Why these three pieces Predictor: true binds the mob. Without it the mob is a plain MythicMobs mob, even with a profile. The Intention line tells ThePredict what the skill does (hit, reach, risks) without numbers: reach, radius and wind-up are read from the skill itself. A skill without it still works, but only fires as its own tactic's choice. See Skills & intents. Tactic IDs such as press_and_smash are the option names Jev reads, so make them describe the action in Engli","k":"section","p":"Quick start"},{"t":"How Jev sees each option","u":"profiles.html#question-detail","x":"ThePredict never sends Jev two options that read the same, the name of a choice, or numbers. What it says about each tactic depends on Timing.QuestionDetail (default full): Detail Each option Instruction compact A text of at most 120 characters: short movement and short skill, plus at most one poor fit now: … phrase computed in code (for example shield would block it). The Description only appears as a note: excerpt when two options would read the same. Short text: Which tactic best serves mob_1's objective now? standard An object with the same keys for every option, empty ones left out: movement, skill, best_when, risks and note (your Description). The question, the assumption of a contingency and the parts of the state Jev should look at. full (default) standard plus fits_now and poor_fit_now: up to 3 phrases each about what in the current moment favors or hurts the option, computed in code. standard plus a fixed focus sentence. In compact, for the example boss with its target blocking at melee distance, press_and_strike reads close in; melee hit, medium damage; poor fit now: shield would block it, and retreat_and_defend reads retreat; self heal. With standard and full, put the essential first in each Description: a long one is sent whole. Options Jev cannot tell apart. Two tactics with the same movement, the same Description and the same skill purpose (or no skill) are identical to Jev: only the higher-priority one is sent, and the binder warns Tactics.<a> and Tactics.<b> describe the same option to Jev; Jev only sees '<a>'. Give them different descriptions or purposes. ","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Objective and descriptions in English","u":"profiles.html#english","x":"Jev was trained mostly on English, and other languages decide less accurately. ThePredict sends Jev the profile's Objective, each tactic's name, Description and movement, and what its skill is for (from the Intention line, as fixed English phrases without numbers). It never sends player names or UUIDs. Write Objective and Description in short, clear English. The catalog warns, without blocking, when a text may not be English: may not be in English (contains the word 'objetivo', which is common in other languages); Jev reads English, or (contains the non-ASCII character 'ñ'). Request size is estimated at 1.5 characters per token, calibrated on English text. Text in other scripts, such as CJK, can use fewer characters per token and the estimate would fall short: one more reason to write in English.","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Native conditions","u":"profiles.html#native-conditions","x":"ThePredict evaluates a context's conditions on the mob itself, outside any skill. That has consequences: Entity conditions work, for example healthpercent{p=<30%}. For health in percent use healthpercent{p=<N%} or {p=>N%}: health{h=…} compares absolute health and rejects %. Conditions that only exist in a skill's context (trigger, skill target or metadata) are always false here. Put those in the skill's own Conditions. A line MythicMobs rejects disables only that context, with a catalog error: MythicMobs rejected the condition '…'; context '…' is disabled. A condition from another plugin that nobody resolves is disabled a tick later: no plugin resolved the condition '…'.","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Shortcut contexts","u":"profiles.html#shortcut-contexts","x":"These four names are computed by ThePredict and take no Conditions: Name Active when idle The mob has no perceived target. attacking_phase The target is in the MELEE band (Movement.MeleeReach or closer). tracking_enemy The target is farther than MeleeReach. low_health_phase The mob's health is in the CRITICAL band (Health.Critical).","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Contexts","u":"profiles.html#contexts","x":"A context limits which tactics are eligible while it is active. When several are active, the highest Priority decides; with equal priorities the one declared first wins and the catalog warns (has the same Priority 50 as context '…'; the one declared first wins when both are active). With no active context, every tactic is eligible. Key Rule Conditions MythicMobs condition lines, at least one. Not allowed in shortcut contexts. Priority 0 to 100; default 50. Tactics At least one tactic of the profile, no repeats. DirectTactic Optional; must be in Tactics. In local mode it is picked directly. A profile holds up to 16 contexts.","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Naming tactics","u":"profiles.html#tactic-names","x":"The tactic ID is the name Jev reads, so it should describe the action in plain English. Format: snake_case, [a-z][a-z0-9_]{2,39} (3 to 40 characters, starting with a letter). none and the prefixes debug_, tell_ and stance_ are reserved. Good Bad Why press_and_strike t1, option_a Jev only sees the name: without meaning there is no useful decision. keep_distance_and_shoot KeepDistance, keep-distance Does not match the pattern (capitals, dash). retreat_and_defend retirarse Jev reasons in English. flank_and_strike debug_flank, none Reserved.","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Tactics","u":"profiles.html#tactics","x":"A tactic is one option the mob can pick: a movement, optionally a skill, and a priority. Key Default What it does Movement required APPROACH, KEEP_DISTANCE, RETREAT, HOLD, FLANK or NONE (see Movement & goals). FLANK requires a Choice. Choice none The choice it casts. Description none What it does, in English, for Jev. Priority 50 0 to 100. In local mode the highest priority among the eligible tactics wins. Stance from its movement Base stance while it runs (see Stances, tells & poise). A profile holds 1 to 255 tactics.","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Choices","u":"profiles.html#choices","x":"A choice is something a tactic can cast: a MythicMobs skill, or a plain vanilla hit. Key Default What it does Kind MYTHIC_SKILL MYTHIC_SKILL casts a skill; VANILLA_MELEE deals a vanilla hit and takes no MythicID. MythicID required for skills Exact skill ID. The skill should carry an Intention line (Skills & intents). RequiresTarget true Whether the choice needs a target. A self-heal is usually false. CD 0 Extra cooldown in ticks, for compatibility only. Use the skill's native Cooldown. Choice IDs (melee, ranged) are local to the profile and never reach Jev: [a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}. Note The vanilla hit while ThePredict controls While ThePredict controls a mob, its base melee goal does not hit. A vanilla hit only comes as a VANILLA_MELEE choice, which takes the tactic like any skill, at most one hit every 20 ticks (the vanilla rhythm) and never farther than Movement.MeleeReach. A classic MythicMobs boss adds that passive melee hit to the skills it casts on triggers, so a ThePredict boss loses that passive damage against the same classic boss: put melee damage in a skill of the tactic, or use a VANILLA_MELEE choice, and size its Cooldown and damage accordingly.","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Profile files","u":"profiles.html#files","x":"A profile file is a .yml or .yaml file in AIConfig/Profiles/ that starts with schemaVersion: 2 and holds one or more profiles. Each profile is keyed by its ID; snake_case is recommended. Files ending in .yml.example are ignored. AIConfig/Profiles/example.ymlYAML schemaVersion: 2 example_ai: MythicID: ReplaceWithYourMythicMobId Objective: Survive while defeating the current target Choices: melee: { MythicID: ReplaceWithYourMeleeSkillId } ranged: { MythicID: ReplaceWithYourRangedSkillId } punch: { Kind: VANILLA_MELEE } Tactics: press_and_strike: { Movement: APPROACH, Choice: melee, Priority: 70 } keep_distance_and_shoot: Movement: KEEP_DISTANCE Choice: ranged Description: Stay outside melee reach and shoot while the target approaches Priority: 60 brawl: { Movement: APPROACH, Choice: punch } hold: { Movement: HOLD, Priority: 10 } Contexts: wounded: Conditions: - healthpercent{p=<30%} Priority: 90 Tactics: [keep_distance_and_shoot, hold] idle: Priority: 10 Tactics: [hold] DirectTactic: hold Loading is strict: An unknown key is an error with the file and the path: is not a known field. A key from the old schema says is a schema 1 field; review the migration proposal under migration/. A profile with an error is skipped; the other profiles keep loading. Two profiles with the same ID, or two profiles for the same mob, are all excluded with an error. Values follow this precedence: built-in defaults, then profileDefaults in config.yml, then the profile. The global decision.* limits are never widened by a profile. Every key, with its type, default and range, is in the Profile referenc","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Turning a mob on","u":"profiles.html#binding","x":"A mob is driven by ThePredict when all three hold: Its MythicMobs file has Predictor: true. Any value other than true or false is a catalog error: <Mob>.Predictor: must be true or false. A profile in plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/ has MythicID equal to the mob's exact ID. IDs are case-sensitive; when only the case differs, the error suggests the right one: unknown mob 'guardian'; IDs are case-sensitive, did you mean 'Guardian'? The profile has no errors. A mob with Predictor: true and no valid profile is reported as <Mob>.Predictor: is true but no valid AI profile targets this mob. The mob file can also carry PredictorTraining, PredictorDifficulty and PredictorEntropy (see Mob file keys). After a change, run /mm reload and check the Profiles: line of /thepredict status. Mob tips: Options.FollowRange is how far the mob perceives participants (capped by decision.searchRadiusBlocks, 48 by default) and the maximum range of its APPROACH goal. The example uses 32. Modules.ThreatTable: true is needed for the enriched threat; without it the mob still works, but ThePredict cannot steer its target (see Targets, participants & threat). No AIGoalSelectors needed. With Predictor: true, ThePredict generates the movement goals. The mob's own AIGoalSelectors are only used as its base AI when the profile has no BaseAI. Triggered skills keep running. Skills on ~onAttack or ~onTimer still fire while ThePredict controls the mob. If you do not want their damage on top of the tactics, gate them with predictorcontrol false (see MythicMobs vocabulary). The catalog warns when the mob also ca","k":"section","p":"Profiles, tactics & contexts"},{"t":"Mobs that do not take goals","u":"movement.html#no-goals","x":"Species with a Brain. Their vanilla AI is a brain, not a goal selector, so goals do not drive them. A profile for one of these species only accepts tactics with Movement: NONE; any other movement is an error such as species PIGLIN uses a Brain; only Movement: NONE is allowed. ThePredict installs no goals and inspect says Goals: not installed (MythicMobs keeps its AI). The species are: allay, armadillo, axolotl, camel, frog, tadpole, goat, copper_golem, happy_ghast, nautilus, zombie_nautilus, sniffer, zoglin, breeze, creaking, hoglin, piglin, piglin_brute, warden, villager A piglin guard: tactics without movementYAML schemaVersion: 2 guard_piglin: MythicID: GuardPiglin Objective: Guard the gate and strike whoever comes close Choices: strike: { MythicID: GuardPiglinStrike } Tactics: strike_in_place: { Movement: NONE, Choice: strike } wait: { Movement: NONE } Mobs that are not Creature (slime, magma cube, ghast, phantom, bat): MythicMobs gives them no movement goals, so ThePredict installs none either. inspect says Goals: not installed (MythicMobs keeps its AI) and the mob keeps its own AI. Flyers and swimmers that are Creature do get goals, but their movement has not been tested and is not recommended in this release: ThePredict targets land mobs.","k":"section","p":"Movement & goals"},{"t":"Base AI","u":"movement.html#base-ai","x":"The base AI is what the mob does at level 4, when ThePredict does not control it. ThePredict uses, in this order: the profile's BaseAI; otherwise the mob's AIGoalSelectors; otherwise 0 meleeAttack and 1 randomStroll. A clear line is dropped. If a line names a goal MythicMobs does not know, the installation is refused and the mob keeps its MythicMobs AI (install incomplete: 1 MythicMobs goals missing). YAML BaseAI: - 1 meleeAttack - 2 randomStroll","k":"section","p":"Movement & goals"},{"t":"The goals ThePredict installs","u":"movement.html#goals","x":"With Predictor: true, ThePredict replaces the mob's movement goals with a set generated from the profile and installs it through the MythicMobs AI API (/thepredict inspect shows Goals: installed for revision <n>). Each tactical goal only runs while the current intent asks for its movement, through the predictormove condition. Only the movements some tactic uses get goals. Priority Generated goal For 0 clear — 1 float always 2 goToSpawnLocation{maxrange=<Arena.Radius>;speed=<Approach.Speed>} only with an arena 3 fleeConditional{distance=<Retreat.Distance>;speed=<Retreat.Speed>;mc=[ - predictormove{m=RETREAT} true ];targetconditions=[ - isTarget true ]} RETREAT 4 fleeConditional{distance=<Band.Inner>;speed=<Approach.Speed>;mc=[ - predictormove{m=KEEP_DISTANCE} true ];targetconditions=[ - isTarget true ]} KEEP_DISTANCE (inner edge) 5 moveWithinConditional{range=<Band.Outer>;speed=<Approach.Speed>;mc=[ - predictormove{m=KEEP_DISTANCE} true ]} KEEP_DISTANCE (outer edge) 6 moveTowardsTargetConditional{speed=<Approach.Speed>;minrange=<MeleeReach>;maxrange=<FollowRange>;mc=[ - predictormove{m=APPROACH} true ]} APPROACH 7 thepredict:flank (Paper goal) FLANK 8 thepredict:hold (Paper goal) HOLD, whenever any movement is used base + 10 your base AI, without clear level 4 (BASE) next lookAtTarget, if the base AI lacks it always last thepredict:owner (ownership marker) — The two flee goals carry targetconditions=[ - isTarget true ]: the mob only flees from its own target, never from the nearest living entity (which could be an ally). With Timing.TickLayer full, the Paper goal thepredict:","k":"section","p":"Movement & goals"},{"t":"Movements","u":"movement.html#movements","x":"Movement What the mob does APPROACH Closes in with the native navigator and stops at MeleeReach. KEEP_DISTANCE Backs away when the target is closer than Band.Inner, closes in when it is farther than Band.Outer, and stays put in between. RETREAT Moves away over walkable ground until it has opened Retreat.Distance; with an arena, it stays inside it. HOLD Does not walk; keeps looking at the target and floating in water. FLANK Circles a target that raises a shield until it is out of the blocking angle, and strikes from there. Only eligible against a raised shield, and it needs a Choice. NONE Leaves movement alone: the tactic only casts its skill. The only movement species with a Brain accept. If a movement makes no progress for two decisions in a row (no movement goal running, or not getting closer or farther as it should), the intent is dropped with the reason NO_PROGRESS, typically when the target stands on a pillar, behind a wall or in water.","k":"section","p":"Movement & goals"},{"t":"Distances","u":"movement.html#distances","x":"Every movement works with the distance to the target, in blocks, and a few lines you set in the profile's Movement section (or inherit from profileDefaults). MELEE RANGED BEYOND KEEP_DISTANCE 02.55916 mobMeleeReachBand.InnerBand.OuterRangedReach Default distances, in blocks. The distance bands are what Jev reads; the keep-distance band is where KEEP_DISTANCE stops moving. Key Default Rule Used for MeleeReach 2.5 greater than 0 The MELEE band, where APPROACH stops, and the reach of melee skills. Band.Inner 5.0 greater than MeleeReach KEEP_DISTANCE backs away when closer. Band.Outer 9.0 greater than Band.Inner KEEP_DISTANCE closes in when farther. RangedReach 16.0 at least Band.Outer Up to here the target is RANGED; farther, BEYOND. Retreat.Distance 10.0 greater than 0 Distance a RETREAT tries to open. Retreat.Speed 1.2 0.1 to 3 Speed multiplier while retreating. Approach.Speed 1.15 0.1 to 3 Speed while approaching, keeping distance and walking back to the arena. Arena.Radius no arena greater than Band.Outer The mob walks back to its spawn point when it gets farther. Health works the same way: at or below Health.Critical (0.3) a creature is CRITICAL, at or below Health.Wounded (0.6) it is WOUNDED, above that HEALTHY. The ratio counts health plus absorption, for the mob and for players.","k":"section","p":"Movement & goals"},{"t":"Purpose override (administrators)","u":"skills.html#purpose-override","x":"Choices.<id>.Purpose is internal data and an administrator override for tuning one mob, not something authors write. It replaces the skill's Intention line for that choice (the binder warns Choices.<id>.Purpose overrides the Intention of skill '<S>') and is the only form that takes numbers (Reach, Radius, WindUp). Its keys are in the profile reference. To move a profile that still has Purpose sections to Intention lines: Run /thepredict intention suggest <profile> and copy each line into its skill, under Intention. Run /mm reload. /thepredict inspect should show origin=skill with the same roles, delivery and conditions. Remove Purpose from the profile; while it stays, the profile wins and the warning says so. Removing PredictValues is optional; they are no longer read. To go back, put the Purpose back in the profile: it wins over the skill's line.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Suggesting a line","u":"skills.html#suggest","x":"/thepredict intention suggest [profile] prints, for each bound choice, the canonical Intention line of its current purpose, and what the line cannot carry (for example a reach that needs targetwithin). It never writes MythicMobs files. Without a profile ID it covers every bound profile. Permission: thepredict.admin.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Rhythm","u":"skills.html#rhythm","x":"A skill fires on its own Cooldown. Tune the Cooldown to control spam. With Timing.CastMode any_ready (the default), every skill with a valid Intention fires on the first tick it is ready, using its Cooldown and Charges, besides the tactic's own choice. GAP_CLOSE and ESCAPE skills only fire in a direction that makes sense (closing in, or getting away). Exceptions: a gap closer that deals damage may also hit in melee, and the PUNISH_CONSUMING and EVADE_CRITICAL reactions lift the rule (see reactions). With intent_only, only the tactic's choice fires. A skill without Cooldown spams under any_ready: it fires every time it can. That rhythm is yours to set. The only guards ThePredict adds: one cast start per tick, and the mob stays busy until the skill's wind-up is over. There is no extra minimum gap. A vanilla hit (Kind: VANILLA_MELEE) has no Cooldown: it keeps the vanilla attack rhythm, one hit every 20 ticks, even when the target's invulnerability is shorter. The PREDICTOR_<TACTIC> signal is not repeated when the same tactic is renewed. Skills already running (delay lines, projectiles in flight) are not cancelled when the tactic changes. With decision.castThread same_tick (the default), delay 10 waits exactly 10 server ticks. ThePredict sorts each skill into a cooldown class from its native Cooldown (plus CD): NONE (0 s), SHORT (up to 3 s), MEDIUM (up to 10 s), LONG (more) or UNKNOWN (no fixed readable value, for example a placeholder). A vanilla hit is SHORT (MEDIUM with a CD of 60 ticks or more). /thepredict inspect shows each class on its Skills line. Tip Gating classic ski","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"How ThePredict casts","u":"skills.html#casting","x":"ThePredict casts with its own MythicMobs trigger (THEPREDICT; you never write it). @target and @trigger are the mob's target. Right before casting, it checks, in order: The target is the expected one: the leader of the threat table, otherwise Mob.getTarget(). A skill with a native targetwithin also waits until Mob.getTarget() is that same target. The native Cooldown and charges. The reach of the delivery, and line of sight when the line says RISK_NEEDS_LINE_OF_SIGHT or the skill checks lineofsight. The target's invulnerability frames and shield. The skill's own Conditions. Outcome What happened CAST The skill was cast. NOT_ELIGIBLE Not ready yet (cooldown, reach, a condition): it waits without being consumed and retries. DEFERRED_INVULNERABLE The target was just hit and vanilla would ignore the hit: it waits, unless every damaging mechanic has ignoreinvulnerability=true. SKIPPED_SHIELD A damaging skill is not cast into a raised shield that would block it, unless the line has IGNORES_SHIELD or the damage has ignoreshield=true. REJECTED_BY_MYTHICMOBS MythicMobs refused it: a failed chance (rolled once, at cast time, never checked in advance), a cancelled event or no charges left.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Untyped skills and PredictValues","u":"skills.html#untyped","x":"A skill without a valid Intention line (and without an administrator Purpose) is untyped: it only fires as the choice of its own tactic (decision.untypedCast tactic_only), and Jev learns nothing about it beyond the tactic's description. PredictValues no longer give a skill a purpose. The binder says which case applies: Console skill '<S>' has no Intention; the choice is untyped and only casts with its own tactic PredictValues of skill '<S>' are no longer read; write an Intention Old files may keep their PredictValues: with a valid Intention they are kept as history and cause no warning. Every new line needs at least a role and a delivery: Old PredictValues entry Write instead MELEE_ATTACK DAMAGE, MELEE RANGED_ATTACK DAMAGE, PROJECTILE or DAMAGE, HITSCAN DEFENSE DEFENSE, SELF SINGLE_TARGET / AREA_TARGET a delivery: MELEE, PROJECTILE, AREA_AT_TARGET… LOW_DAMAGE / MEDIUM_DAMAGE / HIGH_DAMAGE DAMAGE_LOW / DAMAGE_MEDIUM / DAMAGE_HIGH APPLIES_POISON / APPLIES_BAD_OMEN DEBUFF plus a delivery HEALS_CASTER SUSTAIN, SELF SUMMONS_ALLY SUMMON plus a delivery IGNORES_SHIELD IGNORES_SHIELD, or ignoreshield=true on the damage mechanic The binder also checks that the line and the skill agree, in English, without excluding the profile: skill '<S>' checks lineofsight but its purpose has no NEEDS_LINE_OF_SIGHT risk, purpose deals damage but skill '<S>' has no damage mechanic, skill '<S>' ignores shields but the purpose says BLOCKED_BY_SHIELD, and the reverse cases. A tactic whose movement can never let its skill land is flagged too: Tactics.keep_distance_and_strike: Movement KEEP_DISTANCE kee","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Skills that run other skills","u":"skills.html#nested","x":"ThePredict does not follow what a skill runs inside another skill (skill{s=…}, randomskill), a projectile (projectile) or an aura (aura). A skill with any of those lines counts as a skill that can deal damage, with an assumed knockback, and the binder warns once per skill: Console skill '<S>': it runs nested skills, projectiles or auras that ThePredict does not follow; it may deal damage and a knockback is assumed If that skill does not push, set Displacement: NONE on its choice. If it is not a damaging skill, say so in its Intention line.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"What ThePredict reads from the skill","u":"skills.html#native-facts","x":"Everything that MythicMobs already enforces is read from the skill, once, when the profile binds: Fact Read from Reach targetwithin{d=N} in the skill's Conditions (a number only). Otherwise a melee skill uses Movement.MeleeReach. Area radius The r of a radius targeter (@PlayersInRadius, @MobsInRadius, @EntitiesInRadius); 5 when unset, as in MythicMobs. Cone length The range of @EntitiesInCone (16 when unset), or targetwithin. Wind-up The ticks of each delay, plus the delay= option of cosmetic mechanics (effect:*, particles, sound, message), up to the first mechanic that is not cosmetic. Capped at 100 ticks; unknown when a delay is a placeholder or a range. Recovery The trailing delay lines after the hit. Cooldown and charges The native Cooldown (seconds) and Charges. Shield and invulnerability ignoreshield=true and ignoreinvulnerability=true on the damaging mechanics. Line of sight A lineofsight condition in Conditions or TargetConditions. Push damage knockback (unless preventknockback), throw, leap, explosions and pulls. Override with Choices.<id>.Displacement. Allies Targeters such as @MobsInRadius, @Parent, @Children or @Owner. Override with Choices.<id>.TargetsAllies. An AREA_AROUND_SELF without a radius targeter, or a CONE without range or targetwithin, cannot be completed: the choice becomes untyped and the warning says why. Watch out targetwithin changes MythicMobs too Adding targetwithin{d=N} to a skill's Conditions makes MythicMobs refuse the skill beyond N blocks of Mob.getTarget() for every trigger, not only for ThePredict. Add it only when that is what you want.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Tell answers","u":"skills.html#answers","x":"Changing soon Tells and telegraphing will be redefined in an upcoming release. At most one. It sets how the target should answer this skill's tell, and so which PREDICTOR_TELL_* signal is sent, unless the profile's Choices.<id>.Telegraph.Answer names another. Without either, the answer follows the delivery (see Stances, tells & poise). Primitive Means How ThePredict uses it ANSWER_BLOCK The tell asks for a shield. The skill's tell asks the target to block: PREDICTOR_TELL_BLOCK. A Choices.<id>.Telegraph.Answer in the profile wins over it. ANSWER_DODGE The tell asks for a sidestep. Asks to sidestep: PREDICTOR_TELL_DODGE. ANSWER_BACK_OFF The tell asks the target to leave reach. Asks to leave its reach: PREDICTOR_TELL_BACK_OFF. ANSWER_BREAK_SIGHT The tell asks the target to break line of sight. Asks to break line of sight: PREDICTOR_TELL_BREAK_SIGHT. ANSWER_INTERRUPT The tell asks the target to hit during the wind-up. Asks to hit the caster during the wind-up: PREDICTOR_TELL_INTERRUPT.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Shield","u":"skills.html#shield","x":"Primitive Means How ThePredict uses it IGNORES_SHIELD Goes through shields. The skill is cast even against a raised shield. Also read from ignoreshield=true on the damage mechanic.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Risks","u":"skills.html#risks","x":"0 to 4 per line. Primitive Means How ThePredict uses it RISK_LEAVES_CASTER_EXPOSED Leaves the caster exposed afterwards. A poor fit at critical health; gets a recovery after the hit. RISK_ROOTS_CASTER The caster cannot move while it uses it. Same; Jev weighs it against fleeing. RISK_SELF_DAMAGE Hurts the caster. Weighed against the caster's own health. RISK_NEEDS_LINE_OF_SIGHT Needs a line of sight. Turns on the line-of-sight check before the cast. The binder suggests it when the skill checks lineofsight. RISK_SLOW_PROJECTILE A moving target may dodge it. A poor fit when the target is moving away. RISK_BLOCKED_BY_SHIELD A raised shield blocks it. Makes explicit what damage already does by default. RISK_HITS_ALLIES May hurt allies. Matters in fights with several mobs.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Best when","u":"skills.html#best-when","x":"0 to 4 per line. Primitive Means How ThePredict uses it WHEN_TARGET_LOW_HEALTH Works best when the target's health is critical. Finishers; a local tie-break bonus. WHEN_TARGET_SHIELDING Works best when the target blocks or raises a shield. Skills that break or go around a shield. WHEN_TARGET_FLEEING Works best when the target moves away. Ranged punishment or gap closers. WHEN_SELF_LOW_HEALTH Works best when the caster's health is critical. Heals and defenses. WHEN_ENEMIES_GROUPED Works best when the target has another enemy close by. Area skills. WHEN_TARGET_AT_RANGE Works best when the target is beyond melee. Ranged attacks. WHEN_TARGET_IN_MELEE Works best when the target is in melee. Hits and short areas.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Damage tier","u":"skills.html#damage","x":"At most one. Without a tier, the skill counts as \"deals damage, tier unknown\" when it has the DAMAGE or FINISHER role or a damaging mechanic (for example a CONTROL skill that also runs damage), and as \"no damage\" otherwise. So the shortest valid line, DAMAGE, MELEE, works. Primitive Means How ThePredict uses it DAMAGE_LOW Deals little damage. Jev compares damaging options by tier; exact numbers do not help it. DAMAGE_MEDIUM Deals medium damage. Same. DAMAGE_HIGH Deals a lot of damage. Same; also orders the ready skills of any_ready.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Delivery","u":"skills.html#delivery","x":"Exactly one per line. Primitive Means How ThePredict uses it MELEE A hit on a target within arm's reach. Reach is Movement.MeleeReach, or targetwithin when the skill has it. PROJECTILE A projectile that travels and may miss. Dodgeable; pair it with RISK_SLOW_PROJECTILE when it is slow. HITSCAN An effect at range that lands at once. Not dodgeable; its reach is the skill's targetwithin. AREA_AROUND_SELF An area centred on the caster. Its radius is the r of the skill's radius targeter (@PlayersInRadius, @MobsInRadius, @EntitiesInRadius; 5 when unset). AREA_AT_TARGET An area centred on the target. Aim matters less; punishes grouped enemies. CONE A sweep in front of the caster. Its length is the range of @EntitiesInCone (16 when unset) or targetwithin. SELF Affects only the caster. Needs no reach and no target.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Roles","u":"skills.html#roles","x":"1 to 3 per line. The first one is the primary role. Primitive Means How ThePredict uses it DAMAGE Its main end is to take health. Separates hits from everything else and turns on the damage checks before a cast (shield, invulnerability frames). CONTROL Stuns, slows, pushes or roots the target. Jev favors it to cut an escape or split a target; preferred against a raised shield. GAP_CLOSE Closes the distance at once. Makes an approach useful even when the target is far. With any_ready it fires while approaching, flanking, or keeping distance from beyond the band. It may also fire in melee when it deals damage and the target is in reach, or to punish an eating or drinking target; never during a retreat. ESCAPE Gets the caster away from danger at once. Fits only while moving away: with any_ready it fires on a retreat or while keeping distance inside the band. While evading at critical health it may fire with any movement except an approach. DEFENSE Reduces the damage the caster takes. Protecting rather than healing; fits low health or heavy pressure. SUSTAIN Restores the caster's health. Fits low health. With decision.pruning: safe, a sustain option is dropped from the question while the caster is healthy. BUFF Improves the caster or its allies. An action without a target that does not compete with hits. DEBUFF Weakens the target. Weakening rather than damaging. SUMMON Creates allies. Changes how many fight on each side; Jev weighs it differently. ZONE Denies an area for a while. Cutting paths or punishing kiting. INTERRUPT Cuts what the target is doing. Fits a target that drin","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Writing rules","u":"skills.html#rules","x":"Write a YAML list or a comma-separated text. Primitives are read without regard to case, and - or inner spaces count as _. A line holds at most 16 raw primitives and 400 characters. A valid line has 1 to 3 roles (the first is the primary one), exactly one delivery, at most one damage tier, up to 4 WHEN_ and 4 RISK_ primitives, optionally IGNORES_SHIELD, and at most one ANSWER_ primitive. An unknown or repeated primitive is ignored with a warning; the rest of the line still counts. An unknown primitive that starts with WHEN_, RISK_, DAMAGE_ or ANSWER_ warns that it may need a newer ThePredict (FUTURE_TOKEN); any other is UNKNOWN_TOKEN. An invalid line (no role, no delivery, too many of one family, or IGNORES_SHIELD together with RISK_BLOCKED_BY_SHIELD) is never used halfway: the choice becomes untyped (see untyped skills). When ThePredict prints a line (/thepredict intention suggest), it uses the canonical order: roles (primary first), delivery, damage, WHEN_ and RISK_ in the order of the tables below, then IGNORES_SHIELD. That is why the example bolt reads WHEN_TARGET_FLEEING before WHEN_TARGET_AT_RANGE. The vocabulary is versioned (currently v2). A primitive never changes its meaning or family, and no version is written in the line. These warnings come from ThePredict when the profile binds. MythicMobs itself has no reason to reject the file because of this line.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"The Intention line","u":"skills.html#the-intention-line","x":"Each skill a choice points at says what it is for with one Intention line, next to its Cooldown. ThePredict reads it when the profile binds; MythicMobs ignores it. plugins/MythicMobs/Skills/Guardian.ymlYAML ThePredictGuardianMelee: Intention: DAMAGE, MELEE, DAMAGE_MEDIUM, WHEN_TARGET_IN_MELEE Cooldown: 2 Skills: - delay 5 - damage{a=6} @target The line names what the skill does, never numbers. Reach, radius and wind-up come from the skill itself (see below). Jev never sees the primitive names either: it reads fixed English phrases built from them.","k":"section","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"DAMAGE","u":"skills.html#intention-DAMAGE","x":"Its main end is to take health.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"CONTROL","u":"skills.html#intention-CONTROL","x":"Stuns, slows, pushes or roots the target.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"GAP_CLOSE","u":"skills.html#intention-GAP_CLOSE","x":"Closes the distance at once.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"ESCAPE","u":"skills.html#intention-ESCAPE","x":"Gets the caster away from danger at once.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"DEFENSE","u":"skills.html#intention-DEFENSE","x":"Reduces the damage the caster takes.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"SUSTAIN","u":"skills.html#intention-SUSTAIN","x":"Restores the caster's health.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"BUFF","u":"skills.html#intention-BUFF","x":"Improves the caster or its allies.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"DEBUFF","u":"skills.html#intention-DEBUFF","x":"Weakens the target.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"SUMMON","u":"skills.html#intention-SUMMON","x":"Creates allies.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"ZONE","u":"skills.html#intention-ZONE","x":"Denies an area for a while.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"INTERRUPT","u":"skills.html#intention-INTERRUPT","x":"Cuts what the target is doing.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"FINISHER","u":"skills.html#intention-FINISHER","x":"Finishes off a weakened target.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"OPENER","u":"skills.html#intention-OPENER","x":"Opens the fight with an advantage.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"MELEE","u":"skills.html#intention-MELEE","x":"A hit on a target within arm's reach.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"PROJECTILE","u":"skills.html#intention-PROJECTILE","x":"A projectile that travels and may miss.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"HITSCAN","u":"skills.html#intention-HITSCAN","x":"An effect at range that lands at once.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"AREA_AROUND_SELF","u":"skills.html#intention-AREA_AROUND_SELF","x":"An area centred on the caster.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"AREA_AT_TARGET","u":"skills.html#intention-AREA_AT_TARGET","x":"An area centred on the target.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"CONE","u":"skills.html#intention-CONE","x":"A sweep in front of the caster.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"SELF","u":"skills.html#intention-SELF","x":"Affects only the caster.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"DAMAGE_LOW","u":"skills.html#intention-DAMAGE_LOW","x":"Deals little damage.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"DAMAGE_MEDIUM","u":"skills.html#intention-DAMAGE_MEDIUM","x":"Deals medium damage.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"DAMAGE_HIGH","u":"skills.html#intention-DAMAGE_HIGH","x":"Deals a lot of damage.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"WHEN_TARGET_LOW_HEALTH","u":"skills.html#intention-WHEN_TARGET_LOW_HEALTH","x":"Works best when the target's health is critical.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"WHEN_TARGET_SHIELDING","u":"skills.html#intention-WHEN_TARGET_SHIELDING","x":"Works best when the target blocks or raises a shield.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"WHEN_TARGET_FLEEING","u":"skills.html#intention-WHEN_TARGET_FLEEING","x":"Works best when the target moves away.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"WHEN_SELF_LOW_HEALTH","u":"skills.html#intention-WHEN_SELF_LOW_HEALTH","x":"Works best when the caster's health is critical.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"WHEN_ENEMIES_GROUPED","u":"skills.html#intention-WHEN_ENEMIES_GROUPED","x":"Works best when the target has another enemy close by.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"WHEN_TARGET_AT_RANGE","u":"skills.html#intention-WHEN_TARGET_AT_RANGE","x":"Works best when the target is beyond melee.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"WHEN_TARGET_IN_MELEE","u":"skills.html#intention-WHEN_TARGET_IN_MELEE","x":"Works best when the target is in melee.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"RISK_LEAVES_CASTER_EXPOSED","u":"skills.html#intention-RISK_LEAVES_CASTER_EXPOSED","x":"Leaves the caster exposed afterwards.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"RISK_ROOTS_CASTER","u":"skills.html#intention-RISK_ROOTS_CASTER","x":"The caster cannot move while it uses it.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"RISK_SELF_DAMAGE","u":"skills.html#intention-RISK_SELF_DAMAGE","x":"Hurts the caster.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"RISK_NEEDS_LINE_OF_SIGHT","u":"skills.html#intention-RISK_NEEDS_LINE_OF_SIGHT","x":"Needs a line of sight.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"RISK_SLOW_PROJECTILE","u":"skills.html#intention-RISK_SLOW_PROJECTILE","x":"A moving target may dodge it.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"RISK_BLOCKED_BY_SHIELD","u":"skills.html#intention-RISK_BLOCKED_BY_SHIELD","x":"A raised shield blocks it.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"RISK_HITS_ALLIES","u":"skills.html#intention-RISK_HITS_ALLIES","x":"May hurt allies.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"IGNORES_SHIELD","u":"skills.html#intention-IGNORES_SHIELD","x":"Goes through shields.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"ANSWER_BLOCK","u":"skills.html#intention-ANSWER_BLOCK","x":"The tell asks for a shield.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"ANSWER_DODGE","u":"skills.html#intention-ANSWER_DODGE","x":"The tell asks for a sidestep.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"ANSWER_BACK_OFF","u":"skills.html#intention-ANSWER_BACK_OFF","x":"The tell asks the target to leave reach.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"ANSWER_BREAK_SIGHT","u":"skills.html#intention-ANSWER_BREAK_SIGHT","x":"The tell asks the target to break line of sight.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"ANSWER_INTERRUPT","u":"skills.html#intention-ANSWER_INTERRUPT","x":"The tell asks the target to hit during the wind-up.","k":"value","p":"Skills & intents"},{"t":"Editor support","u":"vocabulary.html#editor","x":"Editors that check MythicMobs names may flag predictor* as unknown. With the MythicScribe extension for VS Code, declare these files under MythicScribe.customDatasets in your settings.json (\"source\": \"File\", one entry with \"elementType\": \"Condition\" and one with \"elementType\": \"Mechanic\"). Placeholders need no entry. thepredict-conditions.jsonJSON [ {\"name\": [\"predictorcontrol\"], \"description\": \"True while ThePredict controls the mob (level JEV, ALTERNATIVE or LOCAL, not expired).\", \"attributes\": []}, {\"name\": [\"predictormove\"], \"description\": \"True while ThePredict controls the mob and asks for this movement: APPROACH, KEEP_DISTANCE, RETREAT, HOLD, FLANK or NONE, any case.\", \"attributes\": [{\"name\": [\"m\", \"movement\"], \"type\": \"String\", \"description\": \"\", \"default_value\": \"\"}]}, {\"name\": [\"predictortactic\"], \"description\": \"True while ThePredict controls the mob with this tactic.\", \"attributes\": [{\"name\": [\"t\", \"tactic\"], \"type\": \"String\", \"description\": \"\", \"default_value\": \"\"}]}, {\"name\": [\"predictorstance\"], \"description\": \"True when the mob's published stance is one of the listed names (neutral, pressing, guarded, evasive, windup, recovery, staggered; comma-separated, any case), or when the list includes enraged and the mob is enraged.\", \"attributes\": [{\"name\": [\"s\", \"stance\"], \"type\": \"String\", \"description\": \"\", \"default_value\": \"\"}]}, {\"name\": [\"predictorzone\", \"predictorzonefact\"], \"description\": \"True while ThePredict controls the mob and the zone publishes this terrain fact (see Zones & terrain).\", \"attributes\": [{\"name\": [\"fact\", \"f\"], \"type\": \"String\", \"descripti","k":"section","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"Example","u":"vocabulary.html#example","x":"A boss that keeps its classic slam only while ThePredict is not in control, shows an aura during one tactic, re-decides when it is hit and roars when it starts retreating. plugins/MythicMobs/Mobs/VocabularyGuardian.ymlYAML VocabularyGuardian: Type: ZOMBIE Display: 'Vocabulary Guardian' Health: 100 Predictor: true Options: FollowRange: 32 Despawn: false Skills: - skill{s=GuardianSlam} @target ~onTimer:60 - skill{s=GuardianDefendAura} @self ~onTimer:20 - predictordecide @self ~onDamaged - sound{s=entity.warden.roar} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_RETREAT_AND_DEFEND - message{m=\"<caster.predictor.tactic> (<caster.predictor.confidence>)\"} @PlayersInRadius{r=16} ~onTimer:40 plugins/MythicMobs/Skills/VocabularyGuardian.ymlYAML GuardianSlam: Conditions: - predictorcontrol false Skills: - damage{a=6} @target GuardianDefendAura: Conditions: - predictortactic{t=retreat_and_defend} true Skills: - effect:particles{p=crit;a=10} @self GuardianShield: Intention: SUSTAIN, SELF, WHEN_SELF_LOW_HEALTH Cooldown: 5 Skills: - heal{a=6} @self plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/vocabulary_guardian.ymlYAML schemaVersion: 2 vocabulary_guardian: MythicID: VocabularyGuardian Objective: Survive while defeating the current target Choices: shield: { MythicID: GuardianShield, RequiresTarget: false } Tactics: approach: { Movement: APPROACH, Priority: 60 } retreat_and_defend: { Movement: RETREAT, Choice: shield, Priority: 90 } hold: { Movement: HOLD, Priority: 10 } Contexts: low_health_phase: { Priority: 90, Tactics: [retreat_and_defend] } GuardianSlam only hits while ThePredict is not in control, so its damag","k":"section","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"Signals","u":"vocabulary.html#signals","x":"ThePredict talks to your skills with native MythicMobs signals. React to one with ~onSignal:<NAME> in the mob's Skills: YAML Skills: - sound{s=entity.warden.roar} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_RETREAT_AND_DEFEND - setstance{stance=guarded} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_STANCE_GUARDED How a signal reaches a mob: A signal is only sent when the mob listens for it: a line with ~onSignal:<NAME>, or a bare ~onSignal (which MythicMobs runs for any signal without its own handler), in the Skills of the mob or of its Template. A handler written inside another skill does not count, because MythicMobs does not register it either. Write the name in upper case, exactly. Whether MythicMobs compares signal names without case is not confirmed. A signal is not a paid call: it never sends anything to Jev. Signal Sent when PREDICTOR_<TACTIC> A new tactic starts at level JEV, ALTERNATIVE or LOCAL. PREDICTOR_ plus the tactic ID in upper case, for example PREDICTOR_RETREAT_AND_DEFEND. Never when the same tactic is renewed, never when control drops to BASE. PREDICTOR_TELL_<ANSWER> A telegraphed hit starts its tell (see Stances, tells & poise). Changing soon. PREDICTOR_STANCE_<STANCE> The visible stance changes. PREDICTOR_STANCE_ENRAGED, PREDICTOR_STANCE_CALM An enraging context starts or ends. PREDICTOR_ROLE_<ROLE> The group gives the mob a new role; at most once every 5 seconds. PREDICTOR_PLAN_<PLAN> The group adopts a new plan. PREDICTOR_PATTERN_<PATTERN> A habit of the mob's target becomes active, or comes back active after a rest (see Patterns). Once per activation, and only in the bias and full patte","k":"section","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"Placeholders","u":"vocabulary.html#placeholders","x":"Use them in any MythicMobs text, for example message{m=\"<caster.predictor.tactic>\"}. The caster is the bound mob. On a mob without a session every placeholder shows none, so you can tell an unbound mob (none) from a bound one playing its base AI (base). Placeholder Shows <caster.predictor.tactic> Current tactic ID; none without a session. <caster.predictor.movement> Current movement in lower case (approach, keep_distance, ...); none without a session. <caster.predictor.level> Control level: jev, alternative, local or base; none without a session. <caster.predictor.confidence> Confidence of the current decision with two decimals (0.73); 0.00 before the first decision, none without a session. <caster.predictor.state> controlled while ThePredict controls the mob, base otherwise, none without a session. <caster.predictor.pressure> changing soon Pressure rung 0–8 while the difficulty controller plays; none otherwise. <caster.predictor.stance> Visible stance in lower case: neutral, pressing, guarded, evasive, windup, recovery or staggered; none without a session. <caster.predictor.poise> Poise left, 0–100; none when the profile has no Poise section. <caster.predictor.answer> changing soon What the open tell asks of the target (block, dodge, back_off, break_sight, interrupt); none without a tell. <caster.predictor.telegraph> changing soon Ticks until the telegraphed hit lands; none without a tell. <caster.predictor.zone> Published terrain facts, comma-separated (cover_near,narrow_ground); none without facts (they need zone mode full). <caster.predictor.pushdanger> What a push woul","k":"section","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"Conditions and mechanic","u":"vocabulary.html#conditions","x":"Names work in any case, like every MythicMobs component. Each condition works both in a skill's Conditions and in a goal's mobconditions. Control conditions are false without a live intent. predictorcontrol, predictormove, predictortactic, predictorrole, predictorplan, predictortoken, predictorzone and predictorpattern are false without a session, at level BASE, when the intent expires and when the plugin stops. So when ThePredict lets go, the mob returns to its base goals on the next cycle. predictorstance is the exception: it is true while the mob has a session and its published stance matches, also at BASE. An invalid argument (an unknown movement, tactic, fact or pattern) makes the condition always false, and the console warns once per load.","k":"section","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"MythicMobs vocabulary","u":"vocabulary.html","x":"ThePredict publishes what each bound mob is doing, and your skills decide what to show. It never adds a particle, a sound or an animation by itself: every visible or audible cue comes from your own skills, triggered by the conditions, placeholders and signals on this page.","k":"page","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictorcontrol","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictorcontrol","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob (level JEV, ALTERNATIVE or LOCAL, not expired). False without a session, at BASE, when the intent expires and when the plugin stops. Use predictorcontrol false to silence classic timer skills while ThePredict fights.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictormove","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictormove","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob and asks for this movement: APPROACH, KEEP_DISTANCE, RETREAT, HOLD, FLANK or NONE, any case. An unknown movement makes it always false and warns once per load. The generated movement goals use it.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictortactic","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictortactic","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob with this tactic. Write the tactic ID exactly, in lower case; an invalid value (or none) is always false and warns, suggesting the lower-case form when that is the only difference.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictorstance","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictorstance","x":"True when the mob's published stance is one of the listed names (neutral, pressing, guarded, evasive, windup, recovery, staggered; comma-separated, any case), or when the list includes enraged and the mob is enraged. Unlike the other conditions it does not need control: it also works at BASE while the mob has a session.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictorzone","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictorzone","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob and the zone publishes this terrain fact (see Zones & terrain). Facts exist only with an effective zone mode of full and Zone.Facts: true. target_near_drop is not accepted; an unknown fact is always false and warns at load.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictorrole","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictorrole","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob and the group gave it this role (pressure, flank, ranged, support, control, guard, reserve). False at BASE or after the intent expires, even if the mob keeps its role.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictorplan","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictorplan","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob and its group follows this plan (press_main_target, surround_target, split_targets, screen_the_leader, harass_from_range, fall_back_and_regroup, search_last_known).","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictortoken","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictortoken","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob and it holds an attack token of this pool (melee or ranged) on its target.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictorpattern","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictorpattern","x":"True while ThePredict controls the mob and its current target has this pattern active (see Patterns). Names are lower case; an unknown name is always false and warns at load. Patterns are published only in the bias and full modes, so with the shipped observe mode this condition is always false.","k":"condition","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"predictordecide","u":"vocabulary.html#voc-predictordecide","x":"A mechanic, not a condition. Asks ThePredict to bring the next decision of the mob's encounter forward, for example when the mob takes damage. It never waits or fails; a mob without an encounter changes nothing, and a mob already marked is not marked twice.","k":"mechanic","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.tactic>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-tactic","x":"Current tactic ID; `none` without a session.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.movement>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-movement","x":"Current movement in lower case (`approach`, `keep_distance`, ...); `none` without a session.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.level>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-level","x":"Control level: `jev`, `alternative`, `local` or `base`; `none` without a session.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.confidence>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-confidence","x":"Confidence of the current decision with two decimals (`0.73`); `0.00` before the first decision, `none` without a session.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.state>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-state","x":"`controlled` while ThePredict controls the mob, `base` otherwise, `none` without a session.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.pressure>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-pressure","x":"Pressure rung `0`–`8` while the difficulty controller plays; `none` otherwise.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.stance>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-stance","x":"Visible stance in lower case: `neutral`, `pressing`, `guarded`, `evasive`, `windup`, `recovery` or `staggered`; `none` without a session.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.poise>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-poise","x":"Poise left, `0`–`100`; `none` when the profile has no `Poise` section.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.answer>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-answer","x":"What the open tell asks of the target (`block`, `dodge`, `back_off`, `break_sight`, `interrupt`); `none` without a tell.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.telegraph>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-telegraph","x":"Ticks until the telegraphed hit lands; `none` without a tell.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.zone>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-zone","x":"Published terrain facts, comma-separated (`cover_near,narrow_ground`); `none` without facts (they need zone mode `full`).","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.pushdanger>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-pushdanger","x":"What a push would do to the mob where it stands: `none`, `harm`, `lethal` or `unknown`. `none` also without a zone.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.role>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-role","x":"Group role in lower case; `none` when the group assigned none.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.plan>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-plan","x":"Group plan in lower case; `none` when the group has none.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.token>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-token","x":"Attack token held: `melee`, `ranged`, `both` or `none`.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.slot>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-slot","x":"Position slot the group gave the mob around its target; `none` when it has none.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.squad>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-squad","x":"Size of the mob's squad; `none` without a squad.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.pattern>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-pattern","x":"The target's most confident active pattern in lower case; `none` otherwise. Published only in the `bias` and `full` pattern modes (always `none` with the shipped `observe`).","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"<caster.predictor.forecast>","u":"vocabulary.html#ph-forecast","x":"The target's forecast next action, shown only while the forecast is accurate enough ({{key:patterns.forecastMinAccuracy}}) and the pattern mode is `bias` or `full`; `none` otherwise.","k":"placeholder","p":"MythicMobs vocabulary"},{"t":"Enriched threat","u":"targets.html#enriched-threat","x":"The MythicMobs threat table still picks the target. ThePredict adds (or removes) threat for facts MythicMobs does not measure, with the weights of the profile's Threat section. It works with and without Jev. Threat key Default Effect AssistsOthers 1.5 When a player heals or buffs other participants with a splash or lingering potion: weight × participants reached, added to that player in the table of every active member of the encounter. RangedHarass 1.0 Multiplies the final damage of each projectile from a player who is not the mob's target, in that mob's table. BlockedHits 0.25 Points per mob hit the player blocks with a shield, in that mob's table. UnreachableDecayPerSecond 2.0 Points per second the target loses while the mob cannot reach it on foot: after two decisions following a path that does not reach the target, it is removed at each decision. Nothing is removed while the mob stands still without a path. No window cap. MaxPerWindow 20.0 Cap of points added per mob table, player and fact in each 100-tick (5 s) window. Must be above 0. Units and limits: With ThreatTable.UseDamageTaken: true, the native table adds one point per point of damage, so the weights are in points of final damage. Ranged harass uses the final Bukkit damage, after armor, resistance and absorption. MythicMobs switches target when another entity passes the current target's threat by 10 %. ThePredict never forces that switch. With ThreatTable.DecayUnreachable: true on the mob, MythicMobs already lowers the unreachable target's threat: ThePredict ignores UnreachableDecayPerSecond so it is not remov","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"Safe mob-versus-mob duels","u":"targets.html#safe-duels","x":"To pit two mobs against each other without ever touching players or other mobs, combine four independent safeguards: Native targeting of the rival only: AITargetSelectors with - 0 clear and - 1 nearestSpecificFaction{faction=<rival>}. A player only counts as part of a faction with the permission faction.<name in lower case> and without mythicmobs.nofaction; operators and * have both, so they stay out. Never give faction.<rival> to a player. No threat from players: Modules: ThreatTable: false, so a player's hit never changes the target. Profiles that only admit the rival: Participants: PlayerGameModes: [] and Entities: Allow: ['faction:<rival>']. ThePredict then never perceives, targets or casts against anything else. Single-target damage: every damaging skill targets @target, never an area. For a fair comparison with a classic boss, give both sides the same stats, base goals and skills (a shared MythicMobs Template helps), set Damage: 0 on both and put all damage in skills, gate the classic timer skills with predictorcontrol false, and make every round end (for example a delay 1800 then remove @self on spawn). Run the arena in its own world with natural spawning off. /thepredict duel records everything both mobs decide and do (see Storage & records).","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"Example: a two-faction duel","u":"targets.html#duel-example","x":"The mob of the other faction uses the same profile with faction:duel_red swapped for its rival: AIConfig/Profiles/duel_blue.ymlYAML schemaVersion: 2 duel_blue_ai: MythicID: ThePredictGuardian Objective: Defeat the red duelist in front of you Choices: punch: { Kind: VANILLA_MELEE } Tactics: press: { Movement: APPROACH, Choice: punch, Description: Close in and hit the rival } hold: { Movement: HOLD, Description: Wait for the rival to come closer } Participants: PlayerGameModes: [] Entities: Allow: ['faction:duel_red']","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"What Jev reads about other entities","u":"targets.html#entities-to-jev","x":"An entity reaches Jev as entity_N plus its species, the key of its type without namespace: entity_1 is a zombie, entity_2 is a wither skeleton, target is a zombie. Its custom name, Display, MythicMobs ID, faction and UUID never travel. Local outputs (inspect, records) do show the species: Target: entity_1 (zombie) …. Jev gets fewer facts about an entity than about a player, never invented ones: Fact Player Mob with items (skeleton, pillager, piglin, witch, armed zombie) Other living entity Health and armor yes yes yes Raising a shield, blocking yes from the item in use (BLOCKS_ATTACKS), with the vanilla block delay same Shield disabled, attack recharging, pearl on cooldown yes — — Drawing a bow, bow fully drawn yes from the item in use — Crossbow loaded, holds a totem yes from equipment — Eating or drinking yes from the item in use — Gliding, invisible, mace dive yes yes or equivalent yes or equivalent Long-reach weapon yes from the weapon in hand — Tendency from movement and distance from velocity and distance same Reachable on foot, visible, flankable yes yes yes Out of the target's reach yes from its ThePredict profile, or the vanilla melee check of a Mob the vanilla check if it is a Mob Threat yes yes yes Species — yes yes","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"How the policy decides","u":"targets.html#policy-order","x":"The first rule that applies wins: An invalid or dead entity never takes part. The mob itself and the members of its own encounter (its allies) never do. A player takes part when their game mode is listed, and nothing else applies to players. An armor stand never does. Anything matching a Deny selector never does. Anything on the same side as the mob never does. Anything matching an Allow selector does. Everything else does not. Sides. Two entities are on the same side when both are MythicMobs mobs with the same faction (any case), or else when they share a main scoreboard team. Sides never apply to players, even in a team. An encounter is a side: its members are allies and its participants are rivals. Two ThePredict mobs fighting each other form two encounters, each with its own request and its own point of view. Watch out ThePredict mobs without a faction are rivals A broad allow (kind:MONSTER, kind:MOB, predictor) also admits other ThePredict mobs. Without a Faction or a team, they are rivals: two of them fighting the same player form separate encounters (more requests), and if their AITargetSelectors pick each other (for example - 1 monsters), they fight each other. For a group that should fight together, give them the same Faction: in MythicMobs and target with - 1 nearestOtherFactionMonsters instead of - 1 monsters, or add their faction to the deny list. A player the policy does not admit at the top of the threat table leaves the mob without a target for ThePredict (it does not fall back to Mob#getTarget()): safe, since nothing is cast against that player. With an enti","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"Selectors","u":"targets.html#selectors","x":"A selector is prefix:value text; each list holds up to 16. Loading only checks the shape; values are resolved when profiles bind (on every /mm reload), and an unknown value warns with its path (for example Participants.Entities.Allow[0]) and is ignored. Selector Matches when type:<key> The entity type is that one: type:minecraft:zombie (without a namespace, minecraft). tag:<key> The type is in that entity-type tag, vanilla or from a datapack: tag:minecraft:undead. Tags are read when profiles bind: after /minecraft:reload, run /mm reload. category:<SpawnCategory> Its spawn category: MONSTER, ANIMAL, WATER_ANIMAL, WATER_AMBIENT, WATER_UNDERGROUND_CREATURE, AMBIENT, AXOLOTL, MISC. kind:<KIND> It is a LIVING entity, a MOB, an ENEMY (wider than monster: includes slime, ghast, phantom, hoglin and shulker), a MONSTER or an ANIMAL. mythic:* or mythic:<MobId> It is a MythicMobs mob, or one of that exact type (case-sensitive). faction:<name> Its MythicMobs faction, any case. team:<name> Its main scoreboard team, any case. tagged:<tag> It has that /tag scoreboard tag, exactly. predictor It is a mob bound to ThePredict.","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"Who can take part","u":"targets.html#participants","x":"A participant is anything a mob perceives, targets and fights. It can be any living entity, not only a player. A small policy built from native Minecraft, Paper and MythicMobs distinctions decides who qualifies. Without configuration, only players in SURVIVAL or ADVENTURE take part, and requests to Jev are exactly the same as without the feature. The global policy is the participants section of config.yml (participants.playerGameModes, participants.entities.allow, participants.entities.deny, participants.entities.profilesMayAllow, participants.entities.perceiveNonTargets). Each profile can refine it with an optional Participants section: Profile key Default Rule PlayerGameModes the global list A subset of the global list; a mode outside it is an error. []: these mobs never perceive or attack players. Entities.Allow [] Selectors added to the global allow list. Ignored with a warning when the admin set profilesMayAllow: false. Entities.Deny [] Selectors added to the global deny list; they never take part. Entities.PerceiveNonTargets the global value true only if the global key allows it. With false, the mob only perceives its own target among entities; with true it also perceives allowed entities nearby (at most participants.entities.maxCandidatesPerMember per mob).","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"What a mob perceives","u":"targets.html#perception","x":"ThePredict decides only with what the mob could perceive, so its behavior stays believable: Who: the participants the policy below admits, within the mob's Options.FollowRange (never more than decision.searchRadiusBlocks). By default that means living players in SURVIVAL or ADVENTURE; a player in CREATIVE or SPECTATOR does not exist for ThePredict. What: visible details of a player (a raised shield, a drawn bow, the item in hand, effects) only with line of sight and when the player is not invisible. A player's tendency (closing in, backing off, strafing) comes from how they actually move, never from raw keyboard input. What Jev reads: bands and facts (MELEE, RANGED, CRITICAL, RAISING_SHIELD…), never coordinates, names or UUIDs. Inside each encounter, players are player_1, player_2… and other entities entity_1, entity_2… with their species. No double hits: one cast per choice and per cooldown, one vanilla hit per 20 ticks, no hits during the target's invulnerability frames and no hits into a blocking shield (unless the skill ignores shields). The threat ThePredict adds is capped per window. The history of an encounter is discarded when it ends.","k":"section","p":"Targets, participants & threat"},{"t":"Micro-movements","u":"combat-loop.html#micro","x":"Only with full. The Paper goal thepredict:micro (priority 3) circles, steps aside, steps in or steps back toward short destinations computed with the pathfinder. It hovers around players only, and never asks for a path against air or after a hit it just took. Paper evaluates goals every 2 ticks, so a reaction can reach the legs 0 to 2 ticks later. Impulses are yours. Leaps, dashes and knockbacks are your skills (leap, velocity and the other MythicMobs mechanics). ThePredict never calls setVelocity or applies knockback itself.","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"Reactions","u":"combat-loop.html#reactions","x":"A reaction arms a preference for a few ticks: the next skill fired is one that suits the moment. Timing.Reactions picks the bands that are evaluated (all, survival or none), Reactions.Ahead the bands tried before the tactic's own skill (survival and opportunity by default), and Timing.ReactionDelay how long a trigger must hold first. Reaction Band Triggers when What it prefers EVADE_CRITICAL survival Health is critical and the target is in melee. Survival preference and, in FULL, a backstep. A skill whose role is ESCAPE, DEFENSE or SUSTAIN. An ESCAPE skill may fire with any movement except APPROACH. DODGE_SHOT survival A shot is incoming or drawn. Movement only; not evaluated in REACTIONS. Movement only (no cast); needs TickLayer: full. PUNISH_CONSUMING opportunity The target is consuming. Opportunity preference and, in FULL, an enter. INTERRUPT, GAP_CLOSE or DAMAGE. A GAP_CLOSE may also fire with HOLD or NONE. PUNISH_RECHARGE opportunity A player is recharging an attack inside the inner band. A MELEE damage or finisher skill. Players only: theirs is the only attack recharge that can be read. RESPECT_SHIELD opportunity The target is blocking and the movement is not a flank. CONTROL, or a skill that ignores shields, instead of hitting a raised shield. FINISH opportunity The target is critical. A finisher is preferred. A FINISHER. SPACE_OUT spacing Open space after a cast. Movement only; not evaluated in REACTIONS. Movement only; needs TickLayer: full. EDGE_DANGER survival The mob stands on a lethal edge. Movement only; not evaluated in REACTIONS. Movement only (a step away f","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"The per-tick layer","u":"combat-loop.html#tick-layer","x":"Between two decisions, the per-tick layer carries out the intent Jev chose. It never changes the tactic, the level or the deadline, except to extend a reactive intent (same tactic, longer deadline, no new question). Mode What it adds casts Fires skills the moment they are ready. reactions (default) Also reacts within ticks to openings and danger (table below), and times hits so they land. full Also short micro-movements (circle, step aside, step in, back off). The global mode is decision.tickLayer.mode; a profile's Timing.TickLayer may ask for less, never more (it warns and uses the global one, and so does an overlay). The layer has its own budgets under decision.tickLayer.*, and casting is never delayed when it degrades under load.","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"Cadence","u":"combat-loop.html#cadence","x":"Timing.Cadence sets how often the mob asks: Cadence Intent length Cost reactive (default) Short (Timing.IntentHorizon, 10 ticks), extended while nothing changes; reactive questions at most every Timing.ReactiveInterval (6 ticks). More questions. With the shipped request caps, the worst case is about one such encounter per world and up to about 0.95 USD per mob-hour. standard The usual intent length. IntentHorizon is ignored with a warning. The saving mode: about five encounters per world fit the same caps. These are ceilings set by the request caps, not server measurements. See Jev connection for the budget keys.","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"The fallback chain","u":"combat-loop.html#fallback","x":"Level Shown as Who decides Typical cause of a drop 1 JEV Jev's answer. — 2 ALTERNATIVE The next valid option, or a contingency, of the same answer. The chosen tactic stopped being valid. 3 LOCAL The profile: active context, DirectTactic, priority. No network, no cost. No key, service paused, no budget, low confidence. 4 BASE The mob's base AI. ThePredict does not control it. No eligible tactic, no progress, session reloaded, internal error. Placeholders show the level as jev, alternative, local or base (<caster.predictor.level>). Every drop has a reason, listed in Troubleshooting.","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"The life of an intent","u":"combat-loop.html#intents","x":"Adopted. An answer is adopted when its confidence reaches Timing.MinimumConfidence (0.45 by default) and, to replace the current tactic, beats it by Timing.SwitchMargin (0.15). After decision.lowConfidenceStreakForLocal low-confidence answers in a row the mob drops to its local planner (LOW_CONFIDENCE). Held. An adopted tactic is kept at least profileDefaults.minimumDecisionIntervalTicks (20 ticks). Renewed or expired. An intent is valid for profileDefaults.maximumIntentDurationTicks (40 ticks) unless renewed. Without a replacement it expires (EXPIRED). Each request can also carry decision.contingenciesPerMob \"what if\" questions per mob (for example \"if your health becomes critical\"). If that situation happens, the mob switches to the stored answer without waiting for a new request. An answer that arrives too late (decision.maxDecisionAgeMillis), after the mob changed target, after a reload, or from another model is discarded; /thepredict status counts each reason under discards. Target changes. When MythicMobs changes the mob's target, the decision in flight is dropped and the mob plays at level 4 until the next capture of its encounter: 2 to 4 ticks usually, about 22 at most. Retreats are shared. An encounter allows max(1, members / 3) simultaneous retreats; another mob asked to retreat falls back with RETREAT_LIMIT.","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"Two layers","u":"combat-loop.html#layers","x":"Layer Rhythm What it does Reactive, local every observationIntervalTicks (2 ticks), plus the per-tick layer Keeps the current intent, re-checks reach and conditions before each skill, fires skills as they become ready, and switches at once to an alternative or a contingency it already received. Deliberative, Jev once per encounter heartbeat, or sooner Picks the tactic among the candidates the engine prepared. Never blocks the server.","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"Encounters","u":"combat-loop.html#encounters","x":"Bound mobs that fight the same targets form one encounter. An encounter sends at most one request per heartbeat (decision.encounterHeartbeatTicks, 20 ticks), with one question per mob, or sooner when something relevant happens: a contingency fires, the situation changes, or a skill runs predictordecide. A boss with three adds costs one request per heartbeat, not four. A mob never joins an encounter that lists it as a participant: two ThePredict mobs fighting each other form two encounters, each with its own point of view. Two groups that start fighting apart and later meet stay two encounters, with two requests. An encounter carries at most 16 participants per capture, players and entities together.","k":"section","p":"How a fight runs"},{"t":"The example boss, all together","u":"stances.html#example","x":"From AIConfig/Profiles/ThePredictGuardian.ymlYAML Stances: Native: hybrid Describe: false ByMovement: APPROACH: PRESSING HOLD: GUARDED RETREAT: EVASIVE Telegraph: AgainstPlayers: enforce AgainstEntities: off Commitment: 100 EntropyCommitment: 25 ShortWindUp: lead DefaultRecoveryTicks: 20 Poise: Max: 0.15 RegenDelayTicks: 60 RegenPerSecond: 0.05 WindUpMultiplier: 1.5 BlockedHitPoise: 0.05 StaggerTicks: 30 ImmunityTicks: 100","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Poise","u":"stances.html#poise","x":"Poise lets players break a boss's rhythm. It exists only when the profile has a Poise section (there are no global keys): Key Default Effect Max 0.15 Share of max health that must be dealt to break poise. RegenDelayTicks 60 Without damage for this long, poise starts to recover. RegenPerSecond 0.05 Share recovered per second after the delay. WindUpMultiplier 1.5 Damage taken during a wind-up counts this much more. BlockedHitPoise 0.05 Poise the mob loses when the target blocks one of its HEAVY or SEVERE hits. StaggerTicks 30 Stagger length: the mob casts nothing, does not react, and ThePredict does not move it. A break during a wind-up interrupts the hit. ImmunityTicks 100 After a stagger, poise does not fill for this long. <caster.predictor.poise> shows the poise left (0–100) and the stance turns staggered during a stagger.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"What your skills can use","u":"stances.html#tell-signals","x":"You get Meaning PREDICTOR_TELL_BLOCK, PREDICTOR_TELL_DODGE, PREDICTOR_TELL_BACK_OFF, PREDICTOR_TELL_BREAK_SIGHT, PREDICTOR_TELL_INTERRUPT Signals sent when a tell starts, only to mobs with the matching handler. <caster.predictor.answer> The answer of the open tell, in lower case; none without one. <caster.predictor.telegraph> Ticks until the hit lands; none without a tell. predictorstance{s=windup} True during the wind-up; recovery right after the hit. Your tell, your styleYAML Skills: - sound{s=item.shield.block;p=0.6} @PlayersInRadius{r=16} ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_TELL_BLOCK - effect:particles{p=cloud;a=30;hs=1.5;vs=0.1} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_TELL_BACK_OFF When a tell has no cue a player could notice, the binder warns: skill '<S>' telegraph has no visual (or audio) cue; ThePredict adds none: add a ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_TELL_<ANSWER> handler. It also warns when two skills ask for different answers but start with the same effects, and when a delayed hit on @target cannot be avoided by moving away. In groups, the number of open MEDIUM tells on one player and the spacing around big impacts are capped too (see Groups).","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Feints and recovery","u":"stances.html#feints","x":"Telegraph.Commitment (50 to 100, default 100) is the chance a tell is real. Below 100 the mob may feint: start a tell and not follow through. Telegraph.EntropyCommitment (0 to 50, default 25) applies while Entropy is on. A skill with RISK_LEAVES_CASTER_EXPOSED or RISK_ROOTS_CASTER leaves the mob in recovery after the hit: Choices.<id>.Telegraph.RecoveryTicks, or the skill's trailing delay lines, or Telegraph.DefaultRecoveryTicks (20). After a whiff, a lost target or a rejection, the mob recovers for telegraph.whiffRecoveryTicks and that skill cools down for telegraph.whiffCooldownTicks.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Minimum length","u":"stances.html#minimum","x":"With enforcement on (Telegraph.AgainstPlayers enforce by default; Telegraph.AgainstEntities off), every MEDIUM, HEAVY or SEVERE hit is announced for at least: minimum of its class + answer time + delivery margin Class Minimum (telegraph.minTicks) LIGHT 0 (not enforced) MEDIUM 8 ticks HEAVY 16 ticks SEVERE 24 ticks The answer adds telegraph.answerTicks ticks (0 to block or dodge, 3 to back off, break sight or interrupt) and the delivery margin 1 tick. A HEAVY melee hit therefore gets at least 16 + 0 + 1 = 17 ticks. While Entropy is on, minimums do not apply. When the skill's own wind-up is shorter than its minimum, Telegraph.ShortWindUp decides: lead (default) starts the tell first and casts when the minimum is met; immediate casts at once with your wind-up (the binder warns, and /thepredict status counts those hits).","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Danger and answer","u":"stances.html#danger","x":"Each choice gets a danger class and an answer: Danger: NONE, LIGHT, MEDIUM, HEAVY or SEVERE, deduced from the skill's purpose (damage tier, area or single target, control, finisher, shield-piercing) or set with Choices.<id>.Telegraph.Danger. High damage, or medium damage that also controls, finishes or ignores shields, is SEVERE; medium damage in an area, or control, is HEAVY; medium single-target damage, low damage in an area or a debuff is MEDIUM; low single-target damage is LIGHT. An untyped skill is MEDIUM. Answer: BLOCK, DODGE, BACK_OFF, BREAK_SIGHT or INTERRUPT. It comes, in this order, from Choices.<id>.Telegraph.Answer in the profile, from the ANSWER_* primitive of the skill's Intention line, or else from the delivery: melee and cones ask to block, areas around the caster and shield-piercing hits ask to back off, projectiles and areas at the target ask to dodge, and an instant ranged hit asks to break line of sight when it needs one (otherwise to back off). An untyped skill asks to back off. A Choices.<id>.Purpose in the profile replaces the whole Intention line, its ANSWER_* included.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Tells","u":"stances.html#tells","x":"Changing soon Tells and telegraphing will be redefined in an upcoming release. This section documents how the current build works. A tell is the window between \"this hit is coming\" and the hit. ThePredict decides when a dangerous hit needs one, how long it lasts and what the target should do; your skills decide how it looks and sounds.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Which skills fit a stance","u":"stances.html#casts","x":"Stances.Casts maps a base stance to the roles that CastMode: any_ready may fire in it. The tactic's own choice is never filtered. YAML Stances: Native: hybrid Casts: GUARDED: [DEFENSE, SUSTAIN] PRESSING: [DAMAGE, CONTROL, GAP_CLOSE] Stances.Describe is accepted but has no effect in this build; with true the profile logs a warning when it loads.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Enraged","u":"stances.html#enraged","x":"Stances.EnragedContexts lists contexts of the profile that enrage the mob while they are active: predictorstance{s=enraged} becomes true, and the mob receives PREDICTOR_STANCE_ENRAGED on entering and PREDICTOR_STANCE_CALM on leaving. Stances.EnragedNative adds values of the mob's own MythicMobs stance that also count as enraged (only with hybrid or write). Being enraged never shortens a tell or a recovery below its minimum.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Sharing the stance with MythicMobs","u":"stances.html#native","x":"Stances.Native (global stance.nativeMode) decides how the stance meets MythicMobs' own stance: Mode What ThePredict does hybrid (default) Writes the variable predictor_stance (lower case) and reads the mob's own stance. Never calls setStance. read Only reads the mob's stance. write Calls setStance; a stance your skills set wins a conflict until the next action change. The binder warns when the mob already sets its own stance. off Neither reads nor writes. When the visible stance changes, the mob receives PREDICTOR_STANCE_<STANCE> (if it has the handler). The example boss uses it to mirror the stance natively: YAML Skills: - setstance{stance=pressing} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_STANCE_PRESSING - setstance{stance=guarded} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_STANCE_GUARDED - setstance{stance=evasive} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_STANCE_EVASIVE Read it in skills with predictorstance{s=guarded,evasive} or the placeholder <caster.predictor.stance>.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Stances","u":"stances.html#stances","x":"Every bound mob has a visible stance: Stance Kind When neutral base KEEP_DISTANCE and NONE tactics, and at level BASE. pressing base APPROACH and FLANK tactics. guarded base HOLD tactics. evasive base RETREAT tactics. windup action While a telegraphed hit is winding up. recovery action Right after such a hit. staggered action After its poise breaks. The base stance of a tactic comes from Stances.ByMovement (the table above by default) unless the tactic sets its own Tactics.<id>.Stance. A new base stance must be asked for Stances.HysteresisCycles reactive cycles in a row (2 by default, 2 ticks each) and holds at least Stances.MinDwellTicks (20 ticks); the survival reaction EVADE_CRITICAL skips both waits.","k":"section","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Stances, tells & poise","u":"stances.html","x":"ThePredict never adds a particle, a sound or an animation. Everything on this page is published as signals, a variable and placeholders; your own skills decide what the player sees and hears.","k":"page","p":"Stances, tells & poise"},{"t":"Checking difficulty in game","u":"difficulty.html#eval","x":"Command What it does /thepredict eval status The difficulty block of the nearest bound mob (for a player), or the default preset at full power. /thepredict eval difficulty <nearest|uuid> The block of one mob: preset <name> entropy <true|false>, then r <reaction ticks> c <adaptation seconds> pressure <rung|bench>. /thepredict eval pressure <nearest|uuid> <0-8|auto> Pins a mob's rung for testing; auto releases it. Not stored. Also needs thepredict.debug. /thepredict eval verdict list / verdict import <file> Lists or imports evaluation verdicts, which unlock modes that wait for one (such as pattern bias). /thepredict eval report Not available on the server in this release. All of them need thepredict.eval (operators by default). See Commands & permissions.","k":"section","p":"Difficulty"},{"t":"MythicMobs level","u":"difficulty.html#native-level","x":"With difficulty.nativeLevelAllowed true, a profile with Difficulty.NativeLevel spawn lets five fights in a row at an extreme move the MythicMobs level of the next spawn by ±1, within the mob's level ±2. Never during a fight.","k":"section","p":"Difficulty"},{"t":"Entropy","u":"difficulty.html#entropy","x":"PredictorEntropy: true (with Predictor: true) turns on an opt-in lethal mode, against players: The mob always plays at the highest rung, without the controller, and no stat is ever changed. Its reaction delay starts at the preset's reaction floor and shrinks in a straight line over the target time down to entropyReactionFloorTicks; its adaptation time (how long before it asks again or replans) starts at entropyAdaptStartSeconds and shrinks toward zero. Tell minimums do not apply, feints use Telegraph.EntropyCommitment, and the group's fairness limits only record. It never reads hidden player input. An administrator can force Entropy on or off per world with difficulty.worlds.<world>.entropy. A value other than true or false in the mob file is a catalog error: <Mob>.PredictorEntropy: must be true or false.","k":"section","p":"Difficulty"},{"t":"Pressure","u":"difficulty.html#pressure","x":"The controller moves a pressure rung from 0 (gentlest) to 8 (full power). Each rung sets how quickly the mob may react, how eagerly it fires damage, and how much it may exploit enemy patterns: Rung 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Reaction delay (ticks) 20 18 16 14 12 10 8 6 the preset's floor Share of casts that may exploit a pattern 0 0 0 0.10 0.20 0.30 0.40 0.50 0.50 Against players the reaction delay never goes below the preset's reaction floor (reactionFloorTicks); against entities the floor is 0. A profile's Timing.ReactionDelay can only raise it. Higher rungs also prefer damaging skills and give damaging casts less slack; in a group, lower rungs allow fewer melee attackers at once and wider gaps between impacts. How the rung moves: In the fight, every difficulty.adjustIntervalTicks, the controller projects how long the fight will last from the damage dealt so far. Outside the difficulty.toleranceRatio band around the target it moves the rung (a profile can turn this off with Difficulty.InFight). Estimates count only after difficulty.minEvidenceTicks; a fight closes after difficulty.disengageTicks without the mob dealing damage. Between fights, the starting rung learns from how fights ended (difficulty.learningGain, difficulty.deadbandRatio, difficulty.dampingReversals); a profile can turn this off with Difficulty.Learn or fix the start with Difficulty.StartRung. A profile can bound the rung with Difficulty.MinRung and Difficulty.MaxRung, and set its own target with Difficulty.TargetSeconds (5 to 3600 seconds). <caster.predictor.pressure> shows the rung while the controller plays (n","k":"section","p":"Difficulty"},{"t":"Modes","u":"difficulty.html#modes","x":"difficulty.defaultMode (or a profile's Difficulty.Mode) decides how a mob picks its pressure: Mode Behavior auto (default) player against players, bench against everything else. player A controller aims the whole fight at the preset's target length. bench Full power, fixed rung, no controller.","k":"section","p":"Difficulty"},{"t":"Presets","u":"difficulty.html#presets","x":"Today a preset sets the target length of a whole fight against players, plus how quickly the mob may react to them. Against other entities the mob simply plays at full power. Mob file name config.yml key Target fight length Reaction floor (ticks) Entropy floor (ticks) Entropy start Fácil facil 45 min 5 4 7 s Normal normal 30 min 5 3 5 s Difícil dificil 15 min 3 0 3.5 s Caos caos 10 min 1 0 1.5 s Vacío vacio 5 min 0 0 0 s Choosing a preset: Per mob, in the MythicMobs mob file (with Predictor: true): PredictorDifficulty, one of Fácil, Normal, Difícil, Caos, Vacío (case and accents ignored). Without it, difficulty.defaultPreset applies (normal). Another value is a catalog error: <Mob>.PredictorDifficulty: must be one of Fácil, Normal, Difícil, Caos, Vacío, and the mob stays unbound. Per world, by the administrator: difficulty.worlds.<world>.preset and .entropy in config.yml beat the mob file. Players never choose the difficulty. Mob fileYAML MyBoss: Type: WITHER_SKELETON Predictor: true PredictorDifficulty: Difícil PredictorEntropy: false config.ymlYAML difficulty: worlds: arena_nether: preset: dificil entropy: false The numbers of each preset live under difficulty.presets.<name> (see the config.yml reference).","k":"section","p":"Difficulty"},{"t":"Difficulty","u":"difficulty.html","x":"Changing soon This whole page will change In an upcoming release, difficulty becomes a level of intelligence and aggression (Fácil, Normal, Difícil, Entropía, Absolute Void) instead of a target fight length, and the \"fair player\" rules around it will be redefined. This page documents how the current build works, so you can use it today.","k":"page","p":"Difficulty"},{"t":"Inspect a member","u":"groups.html#inspect","x":"/thepredict inspect <nearest|uuid> group adds one line per field: membershipEpoch, planEpoch, stale, state (the group mode in use), leader, squad, role, slot, plan, origin (jev, local or none), seesTarget, tokens, player and table. The exact in-game text has not been verified on a live server yet.","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"The Group section of a profile","u":"groups.html#profile","x":"AIConfig/Profiles/warden_squad.yml (excerpt)YAML Group: Mode: full Squad: wardens LeaderPriority: 80 Weight: 2 Questions: plan_and_leader OnLeaderDeath: succeed AgainstEntities: free Group.Mode: full only takes effect when the global group.mode is full too. Every key is listed with its default and range in the Profile reference, and the global limits in the config.yml reference. Note Global keys not read yet group.idleWarnTicks, group.maxFacts, group.factOnTicks and group.factOffTicks are accepted and validated, but this build does not read them: no group fact is sent to Jev yet. A value other than the shipped one logs a warning at startup.","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Vocabulary","u":"groups.html#vocabulary","x":"Your skills can react to the group's decisions. Like every control condition, these are false at BASE and when the intent expires, even if the mob still holds its role, plan or token. Condition Arguments True while predictorrole role or r: pressure, flank, ranged, support, control, guard, reserve ThePredict controls the mob and the group gave it that role predictorplan plan or p: a plan name from the table above ThePredict controls the mob and its group follows that plan predictortoken pool: melee or ranged ThePredict controls the mob and it holds a token of that pool Placeholders: <caster.predictor.role>, <caster.predictor.plan>, <caster.predictor.token> (melee, ranged, both or none), <caster.predictor.slot> and <caster.predictor.squad> (squad size). Each shows none when there is nothing to show. See MythicMobs vocabulary for the full list. Signals are sent only to a mob that has a matching ~onSignal:<NAME> handler (or a generic ~onSignal). ThePredict adds no effect of its own: what happens is up to your skills. Role signals. PREDICTOR_ROLE_<ROLE> when the mob's role changes, at most once every 5 seconds per mob: PREDICTOR_ROLE_PRESSURE PREDICTOR_ROLE_FLANK PREDICTOR_ROLE_RANGED PREDICTOR_ROLE_SUPPORT PREDICTOR_ROLE_CONTROL PREDICTOR_ROLE_GUARD PREDICTOR_ROLE_RESERVE Plan signals. PREDICTOR_PLAN_<PLAN> to every member when the group adopts a new plan: PREDICTOR_PLAN_PRESS_MAIN_TARGET PREDICTOR_PLAN_SURROUND_TARGET PREDICTOR_PLAN_SPLIT_TARGETS PREDICTOR_PLAN_SCREEN_THE_LEADER PREDICTOR_PLAN_HARASS_FROM_RANGE PREDICTOR_PLAN_FALL_BACK_AND_REGROUP PREDICTOR_PLAN_SEARCH_LAST_KN","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Questions to Jev","u":"groups.html#questions","x":"In full mode, with a leader, the leader's profile decides with Group.Questions which questions the encounter's request carries: Value The request carries plan_and_leader The group plan question and the leader's own tactic question. The default for the leader in full. plan_only Only the group plan question. leader_only Only the leader's tactic question, and no plan. members One tactic question per member and no plan question, as in fair and coordinate. A member that is not asked still appears in the fight state Jev reads, and plays locally (following its role when the group has a plan). Without a leader there is no plan question and every member is asked. Tip Mind the budget One question per member adds up quickly. For five members the local encoder measured about 22 200 characters per request with members, and about 7 000 with plan_and_leader (roughly 2 700 to 4 700 tokens). Prefer Timing.Cadence: standard on group bosses that run in full. See Jev connection for costs and limits.","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Plans, roles and slots","u":"groups.html#plans","x":"When the leader's request carries the group plan question, the group follows a plan. The question offers up to group.maxPlanCandidates of the plans the group can follow, at most one per family (attack, protect, retreat, search), and the first candidate is always the local plan, press_main_target. The group adopts that local plan at once and switches to Jev's pick when the answer arrives. A plan holds at least group.minPlanTicks and expires after group.planHorizonTicks. /thepredict inspect <mob> group shows whether the plan came from Jev or was chosen locally. Plan What the group does Offered when press_main_target Everyone presses the main target. Always (two or more members). surround_target Members take position slots around the target. Always (two or more members). split_targets Members split between targets. Three or more members. screen_the_leader The squad screens the leader. The group has a leader. harass_from_range Ranged members harass while the others hold. A member has a ranged damaging skill. fall_back_and_regroup The group falls back toward the leader in two waves. The group has a leader or a member with a support skill. search_last_known Look for a lost target at its last known position. ThePredict moves nobody for it: your skills react to predictorplan{p=search_last_known} or PREDICTOR_PLAN_SEARCH_LAST_KNOWN. No member sees its target now, and one saw it at most group.lkpForgetTicks ago. While there is a plan, each member gets a role. ThePredict reads what a profile can do from its choices and their Intention lines, and gives each member the role that suits i","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Leader and squads","u":"groups.html#leader","x":"A group has a leader only when at least one member's profile sets Group.LeaderPriority above 0 or names a Group.Squad. The leader is chosen in this order: The highest LeaderPriority. Then the member whose squad has the most members in the encounter. Then the healthiest member. Squads come from the declared Group.Squad names first; then a member whose summons fight in the same encounter heads a squad with them. At most group.maxSquads squads are kept per encounter; the members of any further squad count as having no squad. When the leader dies, Group.OnLeaderDeath decides: succeed elects a new leader at once; break breaks the group for group.brokenTicks, with no plan and no roles until it reforms. The leader's own impact slot is reserved group.leaderReserveTicks ahead, so its big hit is not crowded out.","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Fairness limits","u":"groups.html#fairness","x":"Changing soon The fairness rules toward players will be replaced by intelligence levels in an upcoming release. This section documents how the current build works. In every mode except off, a damaging cast must hold an attack token on its target before it fires. Only damaging casts ask: a heal, an escape or a defense without damage never waits. Two pools. Melee, cone, area-around-self and self deliveries (and the vanilla hit) use the melee pool. Projectile, hitscan and area-at-target deliveries use the ranged pool. A skill without an Intention line counts as ranged. Caps per target. At most group.maxMeleeAttackersPerPlayer melee weight and group.maxRangedAttackersPerPlayer ranged weight hold tokens on one target at the same time. Each member uses its Group.Weight (1 by default; give a big boss 2 or more so it fills the cap alone). Impact spacing. Two impacts on the same target land at least group.minImpactGapTicks apart (never below 4 ticks). Heavy and severe impacts keep group.bigImpactSpacingTicks of space around them (never below 8). Tells. At most group.maxMediumTellsPerPlayer MEDIUM tells are open on one target, a second medium tell cannot ask for a different answer, and nothing medium or harder opens while a heavy tell is open. First-hand sight. A member that does not see the target itself (it only knows where the target is through its allies) cannot land a MEDIUM or harder hit. An exit. Position slots never fill the group.exitSectorDegrees sector behind the target (never below 60°), so there is always a way out. Pressure. Against players, the difficulty controller's ","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Modes","u":"groups.html#modes","x":"Mode What it adds off No group step and no attack limits. fair Attack tokens and impact spacing on each target (the shipped default). coordinate Meant to add a group plan, roles and position slots. In this build a plan is only adopted together with the group plan question of full, so coordinate works like fair. full fair, plus the group plan question: the leader's request asks Jev to choose a plan, and with the plan come roles and position slots. group.mode in config.yml sets the ceiling for the whole server. A profile's Group.Mode can only lower it: a higher value loads with the warning is above Group.Mode and uses the minimum and uses the global mode. plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.ymlYAML group: mode: full Note What needs full A group gets a plan, roles and position slots only in full, with a leader, and when the leader's Group.Questions asks the plan question (plan_and_leader, the default, or plan_only). Everything else on this page that mentions a plan, a role or a slot depends on that.","k":"section","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Groups","u":"groups.html","x":"When two or more bound mobs fight the same targets, they form one encounter: one request to Jev per heartbeat for the whole group. Group coordination sits on top of that encounter. It spaces out the hits on each player and, in the top mode, lets Jev pick a plan for the whole squad, with roles and positions for its members. A lone mob has no group step: everything on this page needs at least two members in the encounter. Note Encounters are sides Mobs of the same side join one encounter; their participants are the other side. Two ThePredict mobs that fight each other form two encounters, each with its own request. Two groups that start fighting far apart and later meet stay two encounters. See Targets, participants & threat for how sides are decided.","k":"page","p":"Groups"},{"t":"press_main_target","u":"groups.html#GroupPlan-PRESS_MAIN_TARGET","x":"Everyone presses the main target.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"surround_target","u":"groups.html#GroupPlan-SURROUND_TARGET","x":"Members take position slots around the target.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"split_targets","u":"groups.html#GroupPlan-SPLIT_TARGETS","x":"Members split between targets.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"screen_the_leader","u":"groups.html#GroupPlan-SCREEN_THE_LEADER","x":"The squad screens the leader.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"harass_from_range","u":"groups.html#GroupPlan-HARASS_FROM_RANGE","x":"Ranged members harass while the others hold.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"fall_back_and_regroup","u":"groups.html#GroupPlan-FALL_BACK_AND_REGROUP","x":"The group falls back toward the leader in two waves.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"search_last_known","u":"groups.html#GroupPlan-SEARCH_LAST_KNOWN","x":"Look for a lost target at its last known position. ThePredict moves nobody for it: your skills react to predictorplan{p=search_last_known} or PREDICTOR_PLAN_SEARCH_LAST_KNOWN.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"pressure","u":"groups.html#GroupRole-PRESSURE","x":"Closes to melee and keeps the target busy.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"flank","u":"groups.html#GroupRole-FLANK","x":"Takes a position outside the target's shield and strikes from the side.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"ranged","u":"groups.html#GroupRole-RANGED","x":"Stays in the distance band and shoots.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"support","u":"groups.html#GroupRole-SUPPORT","x":"Prefers a skill that can help an ally.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"control","u":"groups.html#GroupRole-CONTROL","x":"Prefers control while another member holds melee.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"guard","u":"groups.html#GroupRole-GUARD","x":"Stands between the leader and the biggest threat.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"reserve","u":"groups.html#GroupRole-RESERVE","x":"Holds no job and waits for an opening.","k":"value","p":"Groups"},{"t":"Commands and limits","u":"zones.html#commands","x":"/thepredict zone (permission thepredict.admin) prints one fixed line in this release: No ready zone. Effective mode is the minimum of zone.mode and Zone.Mode. Permission: thepredict.admin. Neither this command nor inspect shows a mob's zone yet. While records.level is not off, the records add a hazard line when hazard damage follows a mob's push (within zone.pushAttributionTicks) or when a mob hurts itself on a hazard (see Storage & records). ThePredict never changes pathfinding costs: it does not call setPathfindingMalus and writes no zone variables. MythicMobs' own AIPathfindingMalus option and setpathfindingmalus mechanic are untested with ThePredict on a live server. Nothing on this page has been verified on a live server yet.","k":"section","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"The Zone section of a profile","u":"zones.html#profile","x":"AIConfig/Profiles/warden.yml (excerpt)YAML Zone: Mode: full Radius: 32 Facts: true HazardPush: \"off\" Mode and HazardPush accept a bare off too, but quoting it is always safe. Each key is listed with its default and range in the Profile reference.","k":"section","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"Pushes, edges and hazards","u":"zones.html#pushes","x":"Changing soon Environment exploitation (pushing into lava or off edges, fighting around water and height) will be redefined in an upcoming release. This section documents how the current build works. Edges. An edge is a drop bigger than zone.maxSafeDropBlocks (with the default of 3, a drop of 4 blocks or more). A push is lethal when it would land in the void, in lava, or in a fall that meets the victim's current health. ThePredict checks where a knockback (zone.knockbackDepthBlocks) or a strong push such as a throw or a leap (zone.strongPushDepthBlocks) would land, reading each skill's push from the skill itself (see Choices.<id>.Displacement). Pushes against players. From observe up, a lethal push against a player does not fire on sight. It waits, zone.pushDeferTicks at a time, and is skipped after zone.pushDeferMaxTicks, unless it comes behind a HEAVY or SEVERE tell that shows its full minimum and whose answer fits the ground. Pulls, self-moves and pushes that are not lethal always go through. A push stays attributed to the mob that caused it for zone.pushAttributionTicks. Tells that cannot be answered. Against a player, a tell whose answer does not fit the ground (for example, no room to back off) is not opened. ThePredict retries every zone.answerRetryTicks and drops it after zone.answerMaxWaitTicks. Guarding the mob (guard and full). The mob refuses unsafe ground: a micro-movement whose destination fails a safe-cell check changes side, a backstep becomes a sidestep, the mob will not step into a lethal push, and with Timing.TickLayer: full it steps away from a lethal ed","k":"section","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"Vocabulary","u":"zones.html#vocabulary","x":"Element What it does predictorzone{fact=<fact>} (alias predictorzonefact, key fact or f) True while ThePredict controls the mob and the zone publishes that fact. Use the lower-case names from the table above. target_near_drop is not accepted; an unknown name is always false and the load warns predictorzone: fact is not an exposed zone fact; the condition is always false. <caster.predictor.zone> The published facts, comma-separated (cover_near,narrow_ground), or none. <caster.predictor.pushdanger> What a push would do to the mob where it stands: none, harm, lethal or unknown. none also when there is no zone. plugins/MythicMobs/Skills/WardenSkills.yml (excerpt)YAML WardenBraceSkill: Conditions: - predictorzone{fact=edge_behind} true Skills: - setvariable{var=caster.braced;value=1;type=INTEGER} @self Like the other control conditions, predictorzone is false at BASE and when the intent expires.","k":"section","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"Terrain facts","u":"zones.html#facts","x":"From the zone, ThePredict derives short facts about each mob. They are sampled every zone.factPeriodTicks, a fact must hold zone.factOnTicks before it turns on and be gone zone.factOffTicks before it turns off, and at most zone.maxFactsPerMob per mob are sent to Jev. Fact True when Phrase Jev reads edge_behind A lethal push sits behind the mob. “…has a deadly drop or hazard close behind it” no_safe_retreat The raw retreat query found nothing. “…has no safe ground to retreat to” target_high_ground The target's floor is at least two above the mob. “…stands on higher ground” high_ground The mob's floor is at least two above the target. “…stands on higher ground than its target” cover_near Cover exists within four blocks. “…has cover from its target close by” narrow_ground Clearance at the mob is at most one block. “…is fighting in a narrow passage” hazard_underfoot The mob's cell is harmful and is not lava. “…stands on harmful ground” internal only The target stands next to a lethal push. Entities only. “…stands next to a deadly drop or hazard” enclosed Less than a quarter of the walkable columns see the sky. “…the fight takes place indoors or underground” hazardous_arena At least five percent of the columns are a hazard, a pit or void. “…the arena has hazards such as lava or deadly drops” Watch out Facts need full Facts are published only while the effective zone mode is full and the profile keeps Zone.Facts at true. With the shipped observe mode, the predictorzone condition is always false and <caster.predictor.zone> shows none.","k":"section","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"What the zone reads","u":"zones.html#reading","x":"Size. A square around the fight with a radius of Zone.Radius, or zone.defaultRadiusBlocks when the profile sets none. A mob with an arena (Movement.Arena.Radius) uses the arena radius plus 4 instead. Nothing goes past zone.maxRadiusBlocks. Vertically it reads zone.bandBlocks above and below. Ground. Walkable columns, headroom and drops; a drop is followed down to zone.maxDropScanBlocks. Hazards. Void, lava, fire, campfires and magma, cactus, sweet berry bushes, wither roses, powder snow, pointed dripstone and cobwebs. Water, slime and hay blocks count as soft landings. Shape of the arena. Cover close to the mob, narrow passages, higher ground, how much of the arena sees the sky. The zone opens with the encounter, is patched as blocks change, and is dropped after zone.idleDropTicks without use. The remaining zone.* keys are budgets that keep the work bounded per tick; see the config.yml reference.","k":"section","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"Modes","u":"zones.html#modes","x":"Mode What it does off No zone is built and no decision reads terrain. observe The zone is built. Against a player, the push policy and the tell checks apply (see below). The shipped default. guard observe, plus the mob refuses unsafe ground. full guard, plus terrain facts reach Jev, the predictorzone condition and the <caster.predictor.zone> placeholder. zone.mode in config.yml sets the ceiling. A profile's Zone.Mode can only lower it: a higher value loads with a warning naming the file and Zone.Mode, and uses the global mode. The effective mode of a mob is the lower of the two. plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.ymlYAML zone: mode: full","k":"section","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"Zones & terrain","u":"zones.html","x":"A zone is ThePredict's map of the ground around one encounter: where the floor is, where a fall or a push would be deadly, where the cover is and who stands higher. It is built off the server thread from chunk snapshots and kept up to date while the fight lasts. What the mob does with it depends on the zone mode.","k":"page","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"edge_behind","u":"zones.html#fact-edge_behind","x":"A lethal push sits behind the mob.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"no_safe_retreat","u":"zones.html#fact-no_safe_retreat","x":"The raw retreat query found nothing.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"target_high_ground","u":"zones.html#fact-target_high_ground","x":"The target's floor is at least two above the mob.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"high_ground","u":"zones.html#fact-high_ground","x":"The mob's floor is at least two above the target.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"cover_near","u":"zones.html#fact-cover_near","x":"Cover exists within four blocks.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"narrow_ground","u":"zones.html#fact-narrow_ground","x":"Clearance at the mob is at most one block.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"hazard_underfoot","u":"zones.html#fact-hazard_underfoot","x":"The mob's cell is harmful and is not lava.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"target_near_drop","u":"zones.html#fact-target_near_drop","x":"The target stands next to a lethal push. Entities only.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"enclosed","u":"zones.html#fact-enclosed","x":"Less than a quarter of the walkable columns see the sky.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"hazardous_arena","u":"zones.html#fact-hazardous_arena","x":"At least five percent of the columns are a hazard, a pit or void.","k":"zone fact","p":"Zones & terrain"},{"t":"Inspect a target's patterns","u":"patterns.html#inspect","x":"/thepredict inspect <nearest|uuid> patterns reads the live model of the mob's current target: the actions of the last 40 ticks, the forecast and its accuracy (in thousandths), and for a pattern its state (inactive, active or resting), confidence, trials, success streak, rest, the quota used and the facts sent. Without a session, a target or a model it prints nothing. The exact in-game text has not been verified on a live server yet.","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"The Patterns section of a profile","u":"patterns.html#profile","x":"AIConfig/Profiles/duelist.yml (excerpt)YAML Patterns: Mode: observe AgainstEntities: free Facts: true Keys, defaults and ranges are in the Profile reference and the config.yml reference. Note Global keys not read yet patterns.hearingBlocks, patterns.maxWatchedPerEncounter and patterns.maxCounterDelayTicks are accepted and validated, but this build does not read them. A value other than the shipped one logs a warning at startup.","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Example: with and without ThePredict","u":"patterns.html#example","x":"A classic MythicMobs boss can only hard-code one habit check per skill line: Without ThePredictYAML Skills: - variableAdd{var=caster.tp_spam;amount=1} @self ~onDamaged ?varInRange{var=skill.hit-attack-cooldown;value=0to0.5} - shieldbreak{d=100} @trigger ~onAttack ?~blocking With ThePredict, the detector decides when a habit is real and when it changed, and your skill simply asks, or listens for the moment it is spotted: With ThePredict (patterns.mode bias, with a verdict)YAML Skills: - skill{s=Boss_ShieldBreaker} @target ~onTimer:10 ?predictorpattern{p=shield_turtle} - skill{s=Boss_TurtleTaunt} @self ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_PATTERN_SHIELD_TURTLE The shield breaker and the taunt are still your skills, with your effects; ThePredict only tells them when the target turtles. The signal fires once per activation, so the taunt plays when the habit is first spotted, not on every tick.","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Exploiting a pattern","u":"patterns.html#exploit","x":"Changing soon How far a boss may exploit a player's habits is part of the fairness rules that will be replaced by intelligence levels in an upcoming release. This section documents how the current build works. In bias and full, an active pattern leans the mob toward its counter: the EXPLOIT_PATTERN reaction prefers the matching skill, and with decision.candidateScoring set to utility the score of a tactic that fits the counter rises by 10 %. Counters never shorten a tell, a cooldown or a wind-up. The movement part needs Timing.TickLayer: full. Pattern Preferred counter Movement Group plan hint spams_clicks medium-damage skills step in crit_jumper DAMAGE or CONTROL skills step back wtap_pressure CONTROL or a skill that pushes the target sidestep predictable_strafe_left, predictable_strafe_right AREA_AT_TARGET or CONE skills orbit chases_retreat AREA_AT_TARGET or CONTROL skills step back shield_turtle skills that ignore shields orbit shield_late skills whose tell asks to block overextends_after_block INTERRUPT or medium damage step back fails_answer_block … fails_answer_interrupt skills whose tell asks for that answer fails_dodge_projectile PROJECTILE skills weak_to_area AREA_AT_TARGET or CONE skills heals_at_low_hp INTERRUPT, saved for the moment press_main_target pearls_when_low PROJECTILE or GAP_CLOSE, saved for the moment retreats_when_low GAP_CLOSE or PROJECTILE harass_from_range relies_on_totem FINISHER, saved for the moment kites_at_range GAP_CLOSE surround_target seeks_high_ground PROJECTILE stand still harass_from_range mace_diver medium-damage skills sidestep no_shi","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Vocabulary","u":"patterns.html#vocabulary","x":"Element What it does predictorpattern{pattern=<name>} (key pattern or p) True while ThePredict controls the mob and its current target has that pattern active. Names are the lower-case names above; an unknown name is always false and the load warns predictorpattern: pattern is not an enemy pattern; the condition is always false. <caster.predictor.pattern> The target's most confident active pattern, or none. <caster.predictor.forecast> The target's forecast next action (an action name from the list above), or none. PREDICTOR_PATTERN_<PATTERN> Signal sent once each time a pattern becomes active (also when it comes back after a rest), to each mob of the encounter whose target is that enemy and that has a handler: ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_PATTERN_SHIELD_TURTLE, or a bare ~onSignal. It says what was read, not what the mob will do. Watch out Only in bias and full The condition, the placeholders and the signal act only in the bias and full modes. With the shipped observe mode, predictorpattern is always false, both placeholders show none and no signal is sent: a mode that does not change decisions does not move your skills either.","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Forecast","u":"patterns.html#forecast","x":"ThePredict also predicts the enemy's next action from the last two. The forecast is shown only while its running accuracy is at least patterns.forecastMinAccuracy.","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Patterns","u":"patterns.html#patterns","x":"Pattern Group Reads Threshold spams_clicks rhythm Swings before the attack has recharged. 0.60 crit_jumper rhythm Jumps in to land critical hits. 0.50 wtap_pressure rhythm Re-sprints between hits. 0.60 predictable_strafe_left movement Strafes to its left in melee. 0.60 predictable_strafe_right movement Strafes to its right in melee. 0.60 chases_retreat movement Chases a foe that steps back. 0.60 shield_turtle defense Keeps the shield raised most of the time. 0.50 shield_late defense Raises the shield too late. 0.60 overextends_after_block defense Strikes right after blocking. 0.60 no_shield defense Fights without a shield. 0.80 fails_answer_block tells Fails to block a telegraphed attack. 0.60 fails_answer_dodge tells Fails to dodge a telegraphed attack. 0.60 fails_answer_back_off tells Fails to back away from a telegraphed attack. 0.60 fails_answer_break_sight tells Fails to break line of sight in time. 0.60 fails_answer_interrupt tells Fails to interrupt a telegraphed attack. 0.60 fails_dodge_projectile tells Is often hit by projectiles. 0.60 weak_to_area tells Is often caught by area attacks. 0.60 heals_at_low_hp resources Heals when health is low. 0.60 pearls_when_low resources Escapes with an ender pearl when hurt. 0.50 retreats_when_low resources Retreats when health is low. 0.60 relies_on_totem resources Has survived with a totem. 0.50 kites_at_range distance Keeps its distance and shoots. 0.60 seeks_high_ground distance Climbs out of melee reach. 0.60 mace_diver distance Dives from above with a mace. 0.50 fixed_cadence rhythm An entity hits on a fixed interval. No t","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"How a pattern is detected","u":"patterns.html#detection","x":"Every enemy's actions are turned into a short stream: idle, strike, strike_early, crit_strike, sprint_strike, shield_up, shield_down, strafe_left, strafe_right, step_in, step_out, jump, sprint_reset, draw, release and consume. Movement is sampled every patterns.sampleTicks, and sideways motion of patterns.strafeBlocks or more counts as a strafe. At most patterns.maxReadsPerTick movement reads run per tick across the server; the others wait for a later tick. Each pattern has its own detector and threshold. It needs at least patterns.minTrials chances to show, must clear its threshold for patterns.persistUpdates updates in a row to become active, and turns off when its evidence falls patterns.exitMargin below the threshold. Old evidence fades with patterns.evidenceForgetting, and when the enemy suddenly changes style the evidence is reset. In simulation, with the shipped forgetting of 0.98, a habit shown 80 % of the time was detected in 92.5 % of runs (median 24 chances), a 70 % habit in 41.8 %, and false positives stayed at 0.1 %.","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Modes","u":"patterns.html#modes","x":"Mode What it does off No observation. observe Detects and records patterns; decisions stay unchanged. The shipped default. bias observe, plus the local engine leans toward the counter of an active pattern. full bias, plus short pattern phrases reach Jev. patterns.mode sets the ceiling; a profile's Patterns.Mode can only lower it (a higher value warns is above Patterns.Mode and uses the minimum). Watch out bias and full need a verdict bias and full change how the mob fights, so they stay at observe until an evaluation verdict for these exact pattern settings is loaded. bias needs a passing simulator verdict; full also needs a passing bench verdict, and with only the first it falls back to bias with a warning. Verdict files come from the offline evaluation tools and are loaded with /thepredict eval verdict import <file> (see Commands & permissions). Until then, /thepredict status names the cause UNVERIFIED_PATTERN_MODE. Changing the patterns.* keys changes the settings' fingerprint, so an older verdict no longer applies.","k":"section","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Patterns","u":"patterns.html","x":"A pattern is a habit of one enemy: spamming clicks, strafing the same way, keeping the shield up, drinking a potion every time health drops. ThePredict watches each enemy of an encounter separately, notices when a habit is real, and can lean the mob's next moves toward the counter. Everything is read from what the mob could witness: observed movement and combat events (hits, criticals, shield up and down, bow draws, eating and drinking). ThePredict never reads a player's raw keyboard input. MythicMobs' own input and HasItem conditions are yours to use in your skills; ThePredict does not read them.","k":"page","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"spams_clicks","u":"patterns.html#pattern-spams_clicks","x":"Swings before the attack has recharged.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"crit_jumper","u":"patterns.html#pattern-crit_jumper","x":"Jumps in to land critical hits.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"wtap_pressure","u":"patterns.html#pattern-wtap_pressure","x":"Re-sprints between hits.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"predictable_strafe_left","u":"patterns.html#pattern-predictable_strafe_left","x":"Strafes to its left in melee.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"predictable_strafe_right","u":"patterns.html#pattern-predictable_strafe_right","x":"Strafes to its right in melee.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"chases_retreat","u":"patterns.html#pattern-chases_retreat","x":"Chases a foe that steps back.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"shield_turtle","u":"patterns.html#pattern-shield_turtle","x":"Keeps the shield raised most of the time.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"shield_late","u":"patterns.html#pattern-shield_late","x":"Raises the shield too late.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"overextends_after_block","u":"patterns.html#pattern-overextends_after_block","x":"Strikes right after blocking.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"no_shield","u":"patterns.html#pattern-no_shield","x":"Fights without a shield.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"fails_answer_block","u":"patterns.html#pattern-fails_answer_block","x":"Fails to block a telegraphed attack.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"fails_answer_dodge","u":"patterns.html#pattern-fails_answer_dodge","x":"Fails to dodge a telegraphed attack.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"fails_answer_back_off","u":"patterns.html#pattern-fails_answer_back_off","x":"Fails to back away from a telegraphed attack.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"fails_answer_break_sight","u":"patterns.html#pattern-fails_answer_break_sight","x":"Fails to break line of sight in time.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"fails_answer_interrupt","u":"patterns.html#pattern-fails_answer_interrupt","x":"Fails to interrupt a telegraphed attack.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"fails_dodge_projectile","u":"patterns.html#pattern-fails_dodge_projectile","x":"Is often hit by projectiles.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"weak_to_area","u":"patterns.html#pattern-weak_to_area","x":"Is often caught by area attacks.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"heals_at_low_hp","u":"patterns.html#pattern-heals_at_low_hp","x":"Heals when health is low.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"pearls_when_low","u":"patterns.html#pattern-pearls_when_low","x":"Escapes with an ender pearl when hurt.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"retreats_when_low","u":"patterns.html#pattern-retreats_when_low","x":"Retreats when health is low.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"relies_on_totem","u":"patterns.html#pattern-relies_on_totem","x":"Has survived with a totem.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"kites_at_range","u":"patterns.html#pattern-kites_at_range","x":"Keeps its distance and shoots.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"seeks_high_ground","u":"patterns.html#pattern-seeks_high_ground","x":"Climbs out of melee reach.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"mace_diver","u":"patterns.html#pattern-mace_diver","x":"Dives from above with a mace.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"fixed_cadence","u":"patterns.html#pattern-fixed_cadence","x":"An entity hits on a fixed interval. No threshold and no phrase.","k":"pattern","p":"Patterns"},{"t":"Latency","u":"jev.html#latency","x":"Measured from the development machine: a decision request took 179 ms at p50, 228 ms at p95 and 328 ms at p99 (1 200 calls, no timeouts); the model check took about 141 ms. Your server's numbers are in /thepredict status under Latency: roundtrip is the time to Jev and back, prepare the encoding on the server thread, tick_work ThePredict's work per tick.","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"Confidence threshold","u":"jev.html#confidence","x":"Answers below decision.minimumConfidence (0.45) are discarded and the mob keeps its plan or plays locally. 0.45 was chosen on a labeled set of combat scenarios: with full detail it kept most scenarios with about 90 % acceptable answers and no forbidden ones. It is a modest sample and will be revisited with server data. Raise Timing.MinimumConfidence for a boss whose mistakes are expensive: it will drop more doubtful answers and play locally more often. Lowering it without your own evidence is not recommended.","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"Costs and capacity","u":"jev.html#costs","x":"Price. At the time this release was tested, Jev cost 0.042 USD per million input tokens, and output was free. TypeSafe can change prices; check their models page before relying on these numbers. /thepredict status estimates the hourly cost from the tokens of the last minute: Input tokens: <t>/600000 in 60 s; estimated cost <c> USD per hour. One mob. An isolated mob in continuous combat sends about 60 requests a minute (one per heartbeat). Mobs that share an encounter share requests: three mobs on the same player send 60 requests a minute in total, not 180, and each adds its own question but no new state. Caps. Every request fits budgets you control. When a budget is spent, mobs fall back to local play (NO_BUDGET) without errors. Cap Default Notes decision.maxRequestsPerMinute 600 Half the account limit (1 200 per minute). Cannot exceed 1 200. decision.maxRequestsPerMinutePerWorld 300 Usually the cap that binds on a one-world server: about 5 isolated mobs. decision.maxInputTokensPerMinute 600000 Binds first with many mobs across worlds: about 5 isolated mobs with full. At the cap, about 1.5 USD per hour. decision.maxInFlightRequests / decision.maxInFlightRequestsPerWorld 8 / 4 Requests waiting at once. To fit more mobs, raising the token cap alone is not enough: raise the request caps too, never beyond the account's 1 200 requests per minute (about 20 isolated mobs). To spend less, lower decision.maxInputTokensPerMinute, use compact, or the standard cadence (see How a fight runs). Before reserving budget, ThePredict prepares the exact request and reserves tokens for its real","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"Question detail","u":"jev.html#question-detail","x":"decision.questionDetail (or a profile's Timing.QuestionDetail) sets how much each option says, and so what each request costs. Measured with the real account on the production request (one mob, one player, one contingency, seven options): Detail Tokens per request Cost per hour of one mob in continuous combat compact ≈ 953 ≈ 0.14 USD standard ≈ 1 701 ≈ 0.26 USD full (default) ≈ 1 884 ≈ 0.28 USD full + fit checks ≈ 2 950 ≈ 0.45 USD full is the default because it kept the most acceptable answers at the default confidence threshold; compact costs about half and is available per profile. What each level sends is shown in Profiles, tactics & contexts.","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"What Jev receives","u":"jev.html#what-is-sent","x":"One request per encounter: a short summary of the fight in English (bands such as MELEE or CRITICAL, facts such as RAISING_SHIELD), the profile's objective, and one question per mob listing its candidate tactics as plain-English options. Players are player_1, player_2…; other entities are entity_1… with their species. Names, UUIDs, coordinates, Display names, MythicMobs IDs and factions never travel. No numbers from your skills and no choice IDs are sent; skills are described with fixed phrases built from their Intention line. Requests have a size guard: a request whose state plus longest question would pass the model's limit is not sent; that encounter plays locally and the service is not paused.","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"Checking the service","u":"jev.html#check","x":"With a key, the start checks the service with GET /v1/models, which spends no tokens, and reports in the console: Console Checking Jev without spending tokens; the result follows in the console. Jev check: READY (credential valid; model unverified until first inference). Decisions are enabled. The check reads the key and the model list; it does not verify an inference or its quality. /thepredict check runs the same check on demand without blocking the server. The current state is the State: line of /thepredict status: State Meaning What to do UNCONFIGURED No key is configured. Set the TYPESAFE_API_KEY environment variable (or jev.apiKey) and restart. Meanwhile mobs fight with their local planner, at no cost. INVALID_CONFIGURATION config.yml is invalid; the console names the file, the path and the reason. Fix the file and restart. ThePredict stays inactive; MythicMobs keeps working. CHECKING The service is being checked (at startup, or after a pause). Wait for the result in the console or in /thepredict status. READY The service accepts requests. Nothing. PAUSED Requests are paused after a rate limit (429), an overload (529), network or service errors, two timeouts in a row, three invalid answers in a row, or a rejected request (60 s). Wait: ThePredict retries with a growing pause (1 to 60 s), then a single trial request. If it repeats, check roundtrip latency and the limits. INVALID_CREDENTIALS The key was rejected (401). Check the key in your TypeSafe account, set it and restart: the key is read only at startup. INVALID_MODEL The configured model does not exist. Use the te","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"Connection settings","u":"jev.html#settings","x":"Key Default Notes jev.baseUrl https://api.typesafe.ai https required; plain http only for a loopback host. jev.model jev-1.13.0 The model tested with this release. jev.provider typesafe Keep the default. jev.timeoutMillis 800 ms Must stay below profileDefaults.maximumIntentDurationTicks × 50. jev.connectTimeoutMillis 1500 ms jev.maxResponseBytes 262144 jev.maxStateChars 12000 Largest combat state sent; at most 45 000.","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"The key","u":"jev.html#key","x":"Recommended: put the key in the environment variable TYPESAFE_API_KEY of the server process. It wins over jev.apiKey. Alternative: jev.apiKey in config.yml, if you cannot set a variable. jev.apiKeyEnvironment renames the variable (empty means only jev.apiKey is used). Write the variable's name there, never the key. Restart the server after setting or changing the key. It is read only at startup; /thepredict check re-checks with the key already loaded and does not read a new one. start.sh (example)Shell export TYPESAFE_API_KEY=\"<your key here>\" java -jar paper.jar --nogui Important Keep the key private Never paste the key in chats, screenshots, reports or command arguments. ThePredict never prints it: not in the console, not in /thepredict status, not in migration reports, not in records. If you share a config.yml, blank jev.apiKey first. A key pasted into jev.model by mistake is refused at load without showing its value.","k":"section","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"Jev connection","u":"jev.html","x":"Jev is the decision model of TypeSafe. It answers choice questions with calibrated probabilities and never generates text or runs anything. ThePredict uses it as the final pick among the candidate tactics its own engine prepares. ThePredict is an independent addon: naming Jev does not imply TypeSafe's endorsement. Jev is optional. Without a key, nothing leaves your server and every bound mob fights with its profile's local planner (level LOCAL), at no cost.","k":"page","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"UNCONFIGURED","u":"jev.html#ServiceState-UNCONFIGURED","x":"No key is configured.","k":"value","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"INVALID_CONFIGURATION","u":"jev.html#ServiceState-INVALID_CONFIGURATION","x":"config.yml is invalid; the console names the file, the path and the reason.","k":"value","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"CHECKING","u":"jev.html#ServiceState-CHECKING","x":"The service is being checked (at startup, or after a pause).","k":"value","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"READY","u":"jev.html#ServiceState-READY","x":"The service accepts requests.","k":"value","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"PAUSED","u":"jev.html#ServiceState-PAUSED","x":"Requests are paused after a rate limit (429), an overload (529), network or service errors, two timeouts in a row, three invalid answers in a row, or a rejected request (60 s).","k":"value","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"INVALID_CREDENTIALS","u":"jev.html#ServiceState-INVALID_CREDENTIALS","x":"The key was rejected (401).","k":"value","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"INVALID_MODEL","u":"jev.html#ServiceState-INVALID_MODEL","x":"The configured model does not exist.","k":"value","p":"Jev connection"},{"t":"Permissions","u":"commands.html#permissions","x":"Permission Default Grants thepredict.admin op The /thepredict command itself (a player without it can use no subcommand), plus status, check, inspect, intention suggest, zone, records stats and learn status. thepredict.records op /thepredict records except stats: export, prune, verify, backup, flush, cache and tag. thepredict.eval op /thepredict eval: status, difficulty, report and verdicts. pressure also needs thepredict.debug. thepredict.learn op /thepredict learn build, export, import, rollback and disable (status also accepts thepredict.admin). thepredict.autoconfig op /thepredict autoconfig: status, import, show, apply and revert. thepredict.debug false /thepredict debug (set, release and list local intents; never sends a request to Jev) and /thepredict duel. Not even operators have it by default; the console always does. Every subcommand also needs thepredict.admin, the permission of the command itself. thepredict.admin alone is enough for records stats and learn status. To give the debug tools to operators without a permissions plugin, create permissions.yml in the server root: permissions.ymlYAML thepredict.verifier: description: Grants ThePredict debug tools to operators on the verification server default: op children: thepredict.debug: true","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"duel","u":"commands.html#duel","x":"/thepredict duel records, in real time, a fight between two factions of mobs. It is off until you start it and costs nothing while idle. It needs thepredict.debug (without it: You need the thepredict.debug permission to record duels). Console /thepredict duel start <label> <factionA> <factionB> [radius] [skills=A,B] /thepredict duel start <label> <factionA> <factionB> <world> <x> <y> <z> [radius] [skills=A,B] /thepredict duel status /thepredict duel stop The first form is for players: the arena is centred on you, in your world. The console must use the second form with a loaded world and coordinates. label matches [a-z0-9-]{1,40}. factionA is the red side and factionB the blue one; they must differ. The radius defaults to 24 blocks, at most 64. skills= lists the skills that count as casts; by default, the MythicMobs skill choices of the bound profiles whose Entities.Allow names one of the two factions. start answers Duel recording '<label>' started: red = <A>, blue = <B>, radius <r>, folder <folder>; stop writes summary.md and says how many rounds and dropped rows there were. What the recorder writes is described in Storage & records.","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"debug","u":"commands.html#debug","x":"Debug tools need thepredict.debug, which not even operators have by default. Without it, debug answers You need the thepredict.debug permission to use debug tools and neither debug nor duel shows up in tab completion. The console can always use them. debug intent <nearest|uuid> <tactic> [ticks] sets a LOCAL intent with one tactic of the mob's profile, for 1 to 6000 ticks (without [ticks], the profile's intent length: 40 ticks by default). It never sends a request to Jev. It refuses, with the reason, a tactic the profile does not declare or that was not eligible at the last capture (a context that does not allow it, a skill on cooldown, no target, or FLANK without a raised shield). debug release <nearest|uuid> drops the mob to level 4; the fallback chain decides again within 2 ticks. debug goals <nearest|uuid> prints the full UUID and generation, one line per goal (running while it runs) and the movement progress.","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"learn and autoconfig","u":"commands.html#learn-autoconfig","x":"/thepredict learn manages learning data and learned values; learn status prints one line, the rest is queued on the storage thread. See Learning & training. /thepredict autoconfig imports, shows, applies and reverts profile overlays. See Profile overlays.","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"zone","u":"commands.html#zone","x":"/thepredict zone prints one fixed line: No ready zone. Effective mode is the minimum of zone.mode and Zone.Mode. Permission: thepredict.admin. In this release neither zone nor inspect shows a mob's zone. See Zones & terrain.","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"eval","u":"commands.html#eval","x":"Changing soon eval reads and tunes the target-time difficulty, which is about to be redefined as intelligence levels. It works as described here in the current build. eval difficulty <nearest|uuid> shows two lines for one mob: preset <name> entropy <true|false> and r <ticks> c <seconds> pressure <rung>, where r is the current reaction delay, c the Entropy adaptation time and pressure the rung, bench at full power. A mob without a session answers no session. eval status shows the same block for the nearest bound mob or, without one, the configured default preset at full power. eval pressure <nearest|uuid> <0-8|auto> forces a pressure rung for testing; auto gives control back to the controller. It also needs thepredict.debug and is not stored. eval verdict import <file> validates an evaluation verdict file and copies it into records/eval/verdicts/ (and the aggregates database). Modes waiting for a verdict, such as patterns.mode: bias, are re-offered at once, without a restart. <file> is a path inside the plugin folder, plugins/ThePredict/: relative to it (never to the folder the server starts from), or absolute inside it. A path with .. is refused with path; an absolute path outside the folder, or a link that leads out of it, with path: must stay inside the plugin folder. Nothing is imported then. eval verdict list shows the loaded verdicts, one line each, at most 8 lines. Before the first load it answers pending: the verdicts have not loaded yet; with none, no verdict loaded. eval report answers eval report is not available on the server in this release.","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"records","u":"commands.html#records","x":"records stats answers at once with one line: <state> [cause] records <level> dropped <n> inFlight <n> failed <n> sqlite <version>. Every other records subcommand needs thepredict.records, is queued on the storage thread and answers queued; the result arrives later in your chat or console. Only one command of each kind runs at a time (A records command of that kind is already running.), and without a storage writer they answer Records <action> needs the storage writer. export outcomes [profile] writes records/exports/outcomes-all.csv (or outcomes-<profile>.csv). It reads the aggregates database. export events <from> <to> [types] takes UTC days as yyyy-MM-dd and writes records/exports/events-<from>-<to>.jsonl, optionally only some line types. It stops at 512 MiB and says capped. prune [days] deletes record days older than days; today is never deleted. verify runs SQLite's integrity check and answers ok or the first problem. backup writes a copy into records/backups/ and keeps storage.backupsKept copies. tag <tag> labels every following record line with [a-z0-9-]{1,40}; tag clear stops. See Storage & records for what the records hold.","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"intention suggest","u":"commands.html#intention-suggest","x":"/thepredict intention suggest [profile] prints, for each bound choice, the Intention line its skill should carry, in canonical order, plus what the line cannot express (for example a reach, which belongs in targetwithin). An untyped choice prints untyped; no Intention line. Without a profile ID it covers every bound profile. It never writes a MythicMobs file: copy the lines yourself (see Skills & intents).","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"inspect","u":"commands.html#inspect","x":"/thepredict inspect <nearest|uuid> explains one bound mob in at most fourteen lines: Line Shows Mob <id> generation <n> Which mob and which session. Session MythicMobs ID, profile, state, level and encounter. Intent Current tactic, movement, choice, confidence, ticks left, whether its skill was tried, [debug] for a forced intent. Without one: none; level 4 runs the base AI of the goal set. Next options Alternatives and contingencies of the last answer. Why Last fallback reason, last cast result and the low-confidence and no-progress streaks. Perception Health band, target distance and trend, reachable, visible, flankable, active contexts, eligible tactics, skills out of reach. Skills Each choice's delivery, reach, radius, wind-up, line of sight, cooldown class and origin (origin=skill when the Intention line was used), or untyped. Target The target by alias (player_1, or entity_1 (zombie)), perceived participants and combat time. Events The latest combat events. Goals installed for revision <n> or not installed (MythicMobs keeps its AI), and the goal set. Movement Progress of the current movement. Threat The native threat table and what ThePredict added. Outcomes The last 8 closed outcome windows, newest last. Aggregate With the aggregates database: windows=… effect=… stored for the current tactic in a similar situation. Add a detail word for one subsystem: tick (the per-tick reading of the target), stance, telegraph, group or patterns, in any case. There is no zone detail. A mob without a session answers <id> has no session: it is not a bound mob with Predictor: true and a","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"check","u":"commands.html#check","x":"/thepredict check asks for a fresh service check without blocking the server. It answers Jev check started; the result arrives here without blocking the server. and later Jev check: <STATE> (<detail>). with the next step. The check calls GET /v1/models, which spends no tokens and does not test an inference. It uses the key read at startup: after changing the key, restart the server instead. If checks are already queued it answers Other checks are already waiting; see /thepredict status.","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"status","u":"commands.html#status","x":"/thepredict status answers in fixed sections, always in the same order: Environment, Service, Catalog, Sessions, Encounters, Budget, Consumption, Latency (p50, p95, p99 of the last two minutes), Errors, Counters and Effectiveness, plus Storage when storage is running and a Patterns line. The whole answer never passes 48 lines: when there are more, the last one says <n> more status lines are not shown. It never shows the key and never names a player. The lines you will read most: Line What it tells you Versions: Java 25 (minimum 25), Minecraft 26.2 (minimum 26.2), MythicMobs … What ThePredict detected at startup. State: Jev <STATE> (<detail>) The service state (see Troubleshooting & status); , trial while one test request runs after a pause. Model: configured jev-1.13.0; last answer <model> The model you set and the one that last answered. Pause: ends in <n> s Only while the service is paused. Profiles: <STATE> (revision N, <r> profiles read, <a> active, <e> errors, <w> warnings) The profile catalog. INVALID adds the first error; SETUP_PENDING says what setup still needs. Migration: none pending / Migration pending: review … Whether an old configuration waits to be moved by hand. Bound mobs: <n> active, <m> suspended; levels JEV …, ALTERNATIVE …, LOCAL …, BASE …; debug intents <d> Mobs ThePredict controls, by fallback level. Server: <x>/600 requests in 60 s, <y>/8 in flight and Your world: … Request budget used, server-wide and in your world. Input tokens: <t>/600000 in 60 s; estimated cost <c> USD per hour (…) Token use and an hourly cost estimate at the published price. ca","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"All subcommands","u":"commands.html#all","x":"Command Permission What it does /thepredict [status] thepredict.admin Health report in fixed sections (see status). /thepredict check thepredict.admin Checks the Jev service again with the key loaded at startup. Spends no tokens. /thepredict inspect <nearest|uuid> [detail] thepredict.admin Explains one bound mob: level, intent, why, perception, skills, goals, threat, outcomes. /thepredict intention suggest [profile] thepredict.admin Prints the canonical Intention line for each bound choice. Writes nothing. /thepredict zone thepredict.admin One fixed diagnostics line about zones. /thepredict records stats thepredict.admin Storage state in one line. /thepredict records export outcomes [profile] thepredict.records Writes the outcome statistics as CSV into records/exports/. /thepredict records export events <from> <to> [types] thepredict.records Copies the JSONL events of a day range into records/exports/. /thepredict records prune [days] thepredict.records Deletes record days older than days (default 14). /thepredict records verify thepredict.records Integrity check of the aggregates database. /thepredict records backup thepredict.records Backs up the aggregates database now. /thepredict records flush thepredict.records Writes the pending aggregates now. /thepredict records cache clear thepredict.records Empties the answer cache. /thepredict records tag <tag> / tag clear thepredict.records Labels the next record lines (for example a test session), or stops labelling. /thepredict eval status thepredict.eval Difficulty state of the nearest bound mob, or the configured defaults. ","k":"section","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"Commands & permissions","u":"commands.html","x":"There is one command, /thepredict, and /thepredict alone means /thepredict status. The command itself needs thepredict.admin, so a player without it can run no subcommand at all; the other permissions add to it. The console may run everything. Tab completion hides debug and duel from players without thepredict.debug.","k":"page","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"thepredict.admin","u":"commands.html#perm-thepredict-admin","x":"The /thepredict command itself (a player without it can use no subcommand), plus status, check, inspect, intention suggest, zone, records stats and learn status.","k":"permission","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"thepredict.records","u":"commands.html#perm-thepredict-records","x":"/thepredict records except stats: export, prune, verify, backup, flush, cache and tag.","k":"permission","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"thepredict.eval","u":"commands.html#perm-thepredict-eval","x":"/thepredict eval: status, difficulty, report and verdicts. pressure also needs thepredict.debug.","k":"permission","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"thepredict.learn","u":"commands.html#perm-thepredict-learn","x":"/thepredict learn build, export, import, rollback and disable (status also accepts thepredict.admin).","k":"permission","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"thepredict.autoconfig","u":"commands.html#perm-thepredict-autoconfig","x":"/thepredict autoconfig: status, import, show, apply and revert.","k":"permission","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"thepredict.debug","u":"commands.html#perm-thepredict-debug","x":"/thepredict debug (set, release and list local intents; never sends a request to Jev) and /thepredict duel. Not even operators have it by default; the console always does.","k":"permission","p":"Commands & permissions"},{"t":"Duel recorder","u":"storage.html#duel-recorder","x":"/thepredict duel records everything two factions of mobs decide and do, in real time (see Commands & permissions for the command). It is off until you start it and costs nothing while idle. What it follows. Up to 8 living duellists of the two factions inside the radius, sampled every 5 ticks. A round starts when each side has a duellist and ends when one side has none: a death gives the round to the other side; a removal (a timeout skill, /mm mobs kill) is a draw. A side is tp when its mobs have a bound profile and classic otherwise. Where. plugins/ThePredict/duels/<label>-<UTC yyyyMMdd-HHmmss>/. Files. decisions.jsonl (planned, body, result, acceptance and local lines, joined by encounter and sequence; local uses sequence −1), samples.csv, casts.csv, damage.csv, intents.csv, defense.csv, retreats.csv, threat.csv, outcomes.csv, rounds.csv and summary.md (wins with a confidence interval, time to kill, damage, hits and misses per skill, retreats, guards, time per control level, effect per tactic, requests, tokens and cost). Limits. 4 hours, 500 rounds, 128 MB per file and 512 MB per recording. At a limit the recording stops itself, writes summary.md with stopped_by: <limit>, tells the player who started it if they are online and logs Duel recording '<label>' stopped: <limit> reached. Writer. One thread, ThePredict-DuelWriter, alive only while recording, with a queue of 8 192 rows. A full queue drops rows and counts them (rows dropped in duel status and in summary.md). At shutdown the recording stops, waiting 2 seconds at most. Cost. With a key, duel status shows the requests ","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Scenario recording","u":"storage.html#scenario-recording","x":"debug.recordScenarios saves every decision Jev answered as an anonymized scenario, for calibration work. Keep it off on a live server; it is read at startup like the rest of config.yml. One file per decision: plugins/ThePredict/scenarios/scenario-<UTC start>-<nonce>-<nnnn>.json, with the exact body sent (aliases only), the questions, the answer, the tokens and empty labels. Never the key. At most 1 000 files per start. At the limit, one line: Scenario recording reached its limit of 1000 files; later decisions are not recorded. Its own thread with a queue of 64. When the queue is full the decision is dropped, counted and reported once: Scenario recording dropped a decision: its queue of 64 is full. About 4.5 KB per file in a one-against-one fight and 51 KB in the worst case (16 mobs against 16 players): up to about 51 MB per start. With recording on, closing the plugin can take about 2 seconds while the queue drains; whatever is left is dropped and counted.","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"What stays private","u":"storage.html#private","x":"Local files may contain the UUIDs of mobs and worlds, and the duel files contain the UUIDs of the duellists. They help debugging and never leave the machine. Jev only ever receives aliases: player_1, entity_1 and so on, plus an entity's species. Never names, Display names, MythicMobs IDs, factions, UUIDs or coordinates. No file ever holds the key or an Authorization header. config_sha256 is computed without jev.apiKey.","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Reading the data offline","u":"storage.html#offline","x":"Stop the server first, then use any JSON or SQLite tool. For example: Shell # every outcome window of the kept days (closed files are gzipped) gzip -dcf plugins/ThePredict/records/events/*/events-*.jsonl* | jq -c 'select(.type == \"outcome\")' # the best and worst tactics per profile sqlite3 plugins/ThePredict/aggregates.db \\ \"SELECT profile, tactic, level, windows, effect_mean FROM outcome_stats ORDER BY profile, effect_mean DESC LIMIT 20\" /thepredict records export outcomes writes the same statistics as CSV into records/exports/ while the server runs.","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Status and commands","u":"storage.html#status","x":"When storage is running, /thepredict status adds a Storage block: Console State: READY records decisions dropped 0 inFlight 0 failed 0 Store: sqlite 3.49.1 synchronous 1 journal wal State shows the aggregates state (READY, STARTING, DISABLED, READ_ONLY, DEGRADED or FAILED) and its cause, the records level, dropped events, batches in flight and failed batches. Store shows the SQLite version and the settings read back from the database (synchronous 1 is normal, 2 is full), plus paused when events are paused for size, network for a network drive and failure … when the records failed. /thepredict records stats prints the same in one line with only thepredict.admin. The other records commands (export, prune, verify, backup, flush, cache, tag) need thepredict.records; see Commands & permissions.","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Aggregates database","u":"storage.html#aggregates","x":"aggregates.db is a SQLite database of running statistics (outcomes per profile, tactic and level, and the data the other features keep). With storage.aggregates off, only the JSONL is written. Driver. ThePredict uses the sqlite-jdbc driver that Paper already ships and does not bundle its own. It needs SQLite 3.45 or newer. Without a usable driver, aggregates turn off (DRIVER_MISSING) and the JSONL records continue. MySQL. mysql is reserved: writing it is a configuration error. Backups. Every 24 hours a copy goes to records/backups/, keeping the newest 7. /thepredict records backup makes one now. Recovery. At startup the database is checked with SQLite's quick_check. A broken file is renamed, never deleted, and the newest backup that passes the check takes its place; without one, aggregates stay FAILED. Flushes. Pending statistics are written every 100 ticks; /thepredict records flush forces one. Important Keep it off network drives SQLite's write-ahead log is not safe on NFS, CIFS/SMB or sshfs. When the records folder looks like one, the Store line of /thepredict status ends with network. Put plugins/ThePredict/ on a local disk.","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Fight records","u":"storage.html#records","x":"The records are append-only JSONL: one JSON object per line, without spaces, written by one background thread (ThePredict-Storage). Every line carries v, type, run, t_ms, t_nanos, tick and tag, then its own fields. records.level What is written off No records. decisions (default) Decisions (planned, result, acceptance, local), outcome windows, tells and the other fight summaries. full Also casts, threat changes, reactions, micro-movements and stances. records.bodies decides what happens to the request bodies: none, hash (default, only a hash), dedup (each distinct body once) or all. Rotation. A file rotates at 64 MiB or after 60 minutes. A closed file is gzipped, and the original is deleted only once the .gz closed correctly. Retention. 14 days and 2048 MiB by default. The current day is never deleted; if today alone passes the size cap, events pause and the aggregates keep working. Runs. Each start with records begins with a run_start line: plugin version, model, question detail, config_sha256, records level, body policy and answer cache. A clean stop writes run_stop with clean: true. After a crash the storage state shows the cause DIRTY_SHUTDOWN; run /thepredict records verify. Tags. /thepredict records tag <tag> writes a label into every following line, handy to mark a test session; tag clear stops. Note Size A planning estimate, not measured on a server: about 47 MB per hour before compression with five bosses fighting, at decisions level with hashed bodies. full writes much more.","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Where things live","u":"storage.html#where","x":"What Where Your configuration plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.yml and AIConfig/Profiles/ (see Install & requirements) Fight records (JSONL) plugins/ThePredict/records/events/<UTC day>/events-<run>-<n>.jsonl, gzipped to .jsonl.gz once closed Request bodies, when kept bodies-<run>-<n>.jsonl in the same day folder Backups, exports and the lock records/backups/, records/exports/, records/.lock Evaluation verdicts records/eval/verdicts/<fingerprint>-<stage>.json Aggregates database plugins/ThePredict/aggregates.db, beside records/, not inside it Scenario recordings plugins/ThePredict/scenarios/ Duel recordings plugins/ThePredict/duels/ Migration proposals plugins/ThePredict/migration/ Learning artifacts plugins/ThePredict/learn/ Profile overlays plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/ Example boss plugins/ThePredict/examples/ The records folder is records.directory (relative to plugins/ThePredict/) and the database file is storage.file. If config.yml is invalid, ThePredict stays inactive and opens neither: no records/ and no aggregates.db are created.","k":"section","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Storage & records","u":"storage.html","x":"Everything on this page stays on your machine. ThePredict writes it from background threads, so a slow disk never delays a fight, and nothing here is ever sent to Jev.","k":"page","p":"Storage & records"},{"t":"Commands","u":"learning.html#commands","x":"Command Permission What it does /thepredict learn or learn status thepredict.learn or thepredict.admin One line: learn <state> artifact <sha or none> verdict <verdict or none> collect <learning.collect> scope <learning.scope>. /thepredict learn build [profile] thepredict.learn Builds a value file from the collected data, for every profile or one, and marks it active. /thepredict learn export <sha256> <file> thepredict.learn Copies a value file to learn/export/<file>. /thepredict learn import <file> thepredict.learn Reads learn/export/<file> or learn/import/<file> and stores it under learn/artifacts/, waiting for a verdict. /thepredict learn rollback thepredict.learn Points learn/active.json back at the previous value file. /thepredict learn disable value|calibration|all thepredict.learn Clears the active value file, the calibration, or both. Every command except status answers queued, runs on the ThePredict-Storage thread and reports its result when it finishes. File names cannot contain a path or ... Without the storage writer, the command answers Learn <action> needs the storage writer.; a second command of the same kind while one runs answers A learn command of that kind is already running. All the keys are in the config.yml reference.","k":"section","p":"Learning & training"},{"t":"Advanced switches","u":"learning.html#advanced","x":"Key What it does Leave it learning.voiSkip Skips a question to Jev when learned data says the local answer almost surely matches. shadow only measures. It relies on learned values and its own evaluation verdict. \"off\" learning.jevHint In shadow, computes a hint for Jev and stores it in the records (planned.jev_hint); it is never sent, so the request stays the same as with off. \"off\" learning.groupPlans Reserved. \"off\" Note Keys not read yet learning.maxContextKeysPerProfile, learning.maxOpenWindowsPerSession, learning.calibration.minDecisions and learning.calibration.driftReferenceWindows are accepted and validated, but this build does not read them (a session always keeps at most 32 open windows). A value other than the shipped one logs a warning at startup.","k":"section","p":"Learning & training"},{"t":"Calibration","u":"learning.html#calibration","x":"Jev returns a confidence with each answer. decision.confidenceGate decides what the decision.minimumConfidence threshold compares: raw (the default): Jev's confidence as it comes. calibrated: a calibrated probability, from a calibration file at plugins/ThePredict/learn/active.tplc. The file is used only when a passing evaluation verdict for it is loaded; otherwise the calibration is the identity and nothing changes. The server itself does not write this file. With calibrated, decision.minimumCalibratedConfidence at parity accepts exactly what the raw threshold of 0.45 accepts; a number from 0.50 to 0.99 sets the calibrated floor yourself.","k":"section","p":"Learning & training"},{"t":"Learned values","u":"learning.html#values","x":"/thepredict learn build turns the collected outcomes into a value file: a table of how well each tactic did in each situation, written to plugins/ThePredict/learn/artifacts/<sha256>.tplv and marked active in learn/active.json. Only sources listed in learning.trainingSources train it, a situation needs learning.minWindowsForValue windows before its value counts, and spreads below learning.minValueSpreadMillis change nothing. Watch out Not used in fights yet In this build the server does not load value files into fights: /thepredict learn status reports learn none, and decision.candidateScoring set to learned has nothing to act on. Building, exporting and importing files works, so you can collect and keep them for a later release. learning.scope (bench or all) is shown by learn status and has no other effect for the same reason. Keep learning.allowUnverified at false: with true, a mode or learned file without an evaluation verdict may activate, and every start warns with the path of learn/active.json.","k":"section","p":"Learning & training"},{"t":"Training mobs","u":"learning.html#training","x":"A mob explores (tries a tactic other than its best one now and then) only where exploration is allowed: Against players, only a mob whose MythicMobs file has both Predictor: true and PredictorTraining: true. There is no command, timer or global switch; remove the key to stop it. In mob-against-mob duels, only with learning.exploreInDuels set to true. plugins/MythicMobs/Mobs/TrainingDummyBoss.yml (excerpt)YAML TrainingDummyBoss: Type: ZOMBIE Predictor: true PredictorTraining: true With probability learning.exploration.epsilon, a decision explores: the mob does not ask Jev that time and draws its tactic among the candidates, usually still the best one but sometimes another. Explored adoptions never pass learning.exploration.maxShare of the total, and an answer from Jev that was already accepted is never replaced.","k":"section","p":"Learning & training"},{"t":"What happens by default","u":"learning.html#default","x":"With learning.collect at true, every tactic a mob adopts opens an outcome window that closes when the intent ends: damage dealt and taken (and damage avoided, for a retreat or a defensive skill), whether the movement reached its goal, kills. Each window is stored with the situation it happened in: distance, health, kind of target, terrain, group. When the fight ends, its final result is shared back over the windows, between the mob's own result (learning.creditShare) and its group's (learning.groupCreditShare), fading over earlier windows (learning.creditDecayPerWindow). The results are aggregated per profile and situation in the local database (see Storage & records), kept for learning.weeksKept with a half-life of learning.halfLifeDays. Turn learning.collect off if you do not want the data at all.","k":"section","p":"Learning & training"},{"t":"Learning & training","u":"learning.html","x":"ThePredict keeps score of its own decisions: after each tactic it adopts, it records what that tactic achieved. This page covers what that collection does out of the box, how a mob can be allowed to experiment, and the commands that turn the collected data into a learned file. Note Nothing changes by default With the shipped settings, learning only collects. It never changes a decision, never changes what is sent to Jev, and players see nothing.","k":"page","p":"Learning & training"},{"t":"On every reload","u":"overlays.html#reload","x":"At startup, on every /mm reload and after each apply or revert, ThePredict reads up to 256 files of at most 64 KiB from autoconfig/active/ and applies each one to its own profile. A key from the overlay wins over the same key of the author's profile. When a file cannot be applied, the author's profile is used and the console warns, naming the file: Warning Cause OVERLAY_UNMATCHED No profile with that ID. OVERLAY_DUPLICATE An earlier file already holds the overlay of that profile. OVERLAY_STALE The author changed the profile after the overlay was built. OVERLAY_INVALID A key does not apply. OVERLAY_UNREADABLE The file is unreadable or larger than 64 KiB. An overlay whose Timing.TickLayer is above decision.tickLayer.mode still applies, lowered to the global mode, and the console warns, for example autoconfig/active/thepredict_guardian.txt: thepredict_guardian: Timing.TickLayer is above the global reactions; using reactions. When the author edits the profile, its fingerprint changes, the overlay goes stale and the author's version rules again until you write a new proposal. Note No automatic search yet The autoconfig.* keys size an offline search for good overlays. That search does not run on the server in this release: proposals are written by hand.","k":"section","p":"Profile overlays"},{"t":"When apply refuses","u":"overlays.html#refusals","x":"apply checks everything a reload would check and writes nothing when it refuses: Refusal Cause OVERLAY_RAISES_GLOBAL A key raises a global mode (Zone.Mode, Group.Mode or Patterns.Mode above zone.mode, group.mode or patterns.mode), or sets Zone.Mode or Group.Mode to off. OVERLAY_INVALID A mode is not a mode, base= is missing, a line has no =, or a key cannot be applied to the profile (for example Zone.Radius=100; the reason is given). OVERLAY_UNREADABLE The file is larger than 64 KiB. OVERLAY_UNMATCHED No profile read now has that ID. OVERLAY_STALE base= is not the fingerprint of the profile read now; the message gives the current one.","k":"section","p":"Profile overlays"},{"t":"Commands","u":"overlays.html#commands","x":"All of them need the permission thepredict.autoconfig. The <path> must contain plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/ and no ..; anything else answers Autoconfig writes only under plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/. Command What it does /thepredict autoconfig or autoconfig status Answers autoApply=off. /thepredict autoconfig import <path> Copies the proposal into autoconfig/inbox/. It changes nothing in fights. /thepredict autoconfig apply <path> Checks the proposal and writes autoconfig/active/<file name>: first profile= and base=, then the keys that are not pinned. Then it reloads the profile catalog, and live mobs switch to the new profile as after /mm reload. /thepredict autoconfig show <path> Shows the active copy of that proposal, or none. /thepredict autoconfig revert <path> Deletes the active copy and reloads the catalog: the author's profile rules again. The file commands answer queued and report the result when the storage thread finishes. Without the storage writer they answer Autoconfig <action> needs the storage writer. Console /thepredict autoconfig apply plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/thepredict_guardian.txt /thepredict autoconfig show plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/thepredict_guardian.txt /thepredict autoconfig revert plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/thepredict_guardian.txt To change the overlay of a profile, revert the old one first, then apply the new proposal.","k":"section","p":"Profile overlays"},{"t":"Keys an overlay can set","u":"overlays.html#keys","x":"Key Notes Timing.Cadence reactive or standard. Timing.TickLayer casts, reactions or full. Above decision.tickLayer.mode it is lowered to the global mode, like a profile's, with a warning. Timing.Reactions all, survival or none. Timing.ReactiveInterval 4 to 20 ticks. Zone.Mode Can only lower zone.mode, and cannot be off. Zone.Radius 8 to 64 blocks. Group.Mode Can only lower group.mode, and cannot be off. Patterns.Mode Can only lower patterns.mode. Decision.Pruning, Decision.MaxOptions, Decision.CandidateScoring, Decision.Diversity Accepted, but these profile keys have no effect in fights yet (see the Profile reference). Other keys are ignored. Mode values are read without case, so Zone.Mode=OFF is refused like off.","k":"section","p":"Profile overlays"},{"t":"The proposal file","u":"overlays.html#proposal","x":"A proposal is a plain text file you write under plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/, one key=value per line. Lines starting with # are comments. plugins/ThePredict/autoconfig/thepredict_guardian.txtText # Calmer guardian on the survival server profile=thepredict_guardian base=<fingerprint of the author's profile> Timing.Cadence=standard Zone.Mode=guard Zone.Radius=32 Line Meaning profile=<id> The profile ID the overlay belongs to. Without it, the file name without its extension is used. base=<fingerprint> Fingerprint of the author's profile the proposal was written for. Required by apply. pin=<key> Leaves that key out: the author's value is kept. <key>=<value> A profile key and its new value. To get the fingerprint, leave base= out and run apply once: the refusal OVERLAY_STALE prints the fingerprint of the profile as it is now (... (base <fingerprint>)). Copy it into the file and apply again.","k":"section","p":"Profile overlays"},{"t":"Profile overlays","u":"overlays.html","x":"An overlay lets an administrator retune a profile on one server (calmer cadence, a lower zone mode, a smaller zone) without editing the author's file. ThePredict never writes the author's profile: the profile a mob uses becomes the author's profile plus the overlay, and removing the overlay brings the author's version back. Each overlay belongs to exactly one profile. Nothing is ever applied on its own: autoconfig.autoApply only accepts \"off\".","k":"page","p":"Profile overlays"},{"t":"Decision log","u":"troubleshooting.html#decision-log","x":"With decision.logDecisions set to true (and a restart), the console prints every decision, fallback, cast result, threat change and closed outcome window, at most 20 lines every 10 seconds. No player names, only aliases: Console Mob <uuid> fell back: NO_PROGRESS Threat +1.50 ALLY_ASSISTED for player_2 sent to the table of mob <uuid> Threat -2.00 UNREACHABLE for player_1 sent to the table of mob <uuid> Outcome JEV keep_distance_and_shoot dealt=0.12 taken=0.03 reached=yes casts=1 hits=1 Local output may show the full UUID of the mob; player names never appear. When you report a bug, include the status and inspect output, these console lines, the profile and the mob and skill files, and your versions. Never include the key: ThePredict never prints it, so nothing you copy from its output contains it.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Common symptoms","u":"troubleshooting.html#symptoms","x":"The mob ignores ThePredict. Check, in order: Predictor: true in the mob file; a profile whose MythicID matches the mob ID exactly (case-sensitive); no profile error in the console; inspect says Goals: installed for revision <n>. Species with a Brain (piglins, wardens, villagers…) only accept Movement: NONE, and slimes, magma cubes, ghasts, phantoms and bats keep their own AI (Goals: not installed (MythicMobs keeps its AI)). It fights, but always at LOCAL. Normal without a key. With a key, read State in status and the Why line of inspect: SERVICE_BLOCKED, NO_BUDGET and LOW_CONFIDENCE are the usual causes. A skill spams. With the default CastMode: any_ready, every skill with a valid Intention line fires as soon as it is ready. A skill without a native Cooldown is ready all the time. Give it a Cooldown (or Charges); ThePredict adds no floor of its own. Double damage. The mob's own trigger lines (~onAttack, ~onTimer) keep running while ThePredict controls it. Gate them with predictorcontrol false so they only fire when ThePredict is not in control. The boss hits less than its classic version. While ThePredict controls a mob, its base melee goal does not hit. Put the melee damage in a skill of a tactic, or add a Kind: VANILLA_MELEE choice (one vanilla hit every 20 ticks at most). A predictor* condition is always false. The control conditions (predictorcontrol, predictormove, predictortactic, predictorrole, predictorplan, predictortoken, predictorzone, predictorpattern) are false at BASE and once the intent expires; predictorstance is the exception. predictorzone only has data wi","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Effectiveness","u":"troubleshooting.html#effectiveness","x":"Each time a mob adopts a new intent at level JEV, ALTERNATIVE or LOCAL (never on a renewal), ThePredict opens an outcome window. It closes when the intent ends or after 60 ticks, whichever comes first, and records: damage dealt and taken, as fractions of the victim's max health; casts, and confirmed hits (the target took damage within 20 ticks of a damaging cast); whether the movement reached its goal (APPROACH got to melee, KEEP_DISTANCE ended at range, RETREAT ended farther than it started, FLANK cast while flanking; HOLD and NONE have no goal); whether the mob or its target died. Where What to read status, Effectiveness: outcomes: level=JEV windows=3 dealt=0.12 taken=0.03 reach=0.67 hit_rate=0.50 effect=0.21 One line per level. dealt and taken are means per window, reach the share of windows that reached their goal, hit_rate confirmed hits per cast, effect the mean of dealt − taken + 0.25·reached + target died − mob died. Without data: outcomes: no closed window yet. status: contingencies: asked=4 fired=2 effective=1 Contingencies sent, fired in combat, and fired with a positive window. inspect: Outcomes: JEV keep_distance_and_shoot dealt=0.12 taken=0.03 reached=yes casts=1 hits=1; … The mob's last 8 windows, newest last, with mob died or target died when it happened. Console with decision.logDecisions: Outcome JEV keep_distance_and_shoot dealt=0.12 … One line per closed window. The effect index is a comparison tool, not a verdict: use it to compare levels or two versions of the same profile.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Profile problems","u":"troubleshooting.html#profile-problems","x":"An error excludes that profile (the others keep loading); a warning keeps it. Errors and warnings are logged at load and after every /mm reload, and Profiles: in status counts them. Message What to do guardian_ai.MythicID: unknown mob 'guardian'; IDs are case-sensitive, did you mean 'Guardian'? Copy the exact MythicMobs ID. The same goes for unknown skill '…'. <Mob>.Predictor: is true but no valid AI profile targets this mob The mob opted in but its profile is missing or has an error. <Mob>.Predictor: must be true or false Same rule for PredictorTraining, PredictorEntropy; PredictorDifficulty must name a preset. <Mob>.PredictorTraining: requires Predictor: true Training only applies to a bound mob. mob '<Mob>' has 2 profiles (a, b); all of them are excluded One profile per mob. … is not a known field A typo or a key from another section. Keys are case-sensitive. … is a schema 1 field; review the migration proposal under migration/ An old-format profile. See Install & requirements. … uses a reserved tactic name ('none' or the prefix 'debug_') / (prefix 'tell_' or 'stance_') Rename the tactic. Tactics.<id>.Choice: is required for Movement FLANK FLANK needs a skill to strike with. Tactics.<id>.Movement: species PIGLIN uses a Brain; only Movement: NONE is allowed Brain-driven species keep their own movement. See Movement & goals. MythicMobs rejected the condition '…'; context '…' is disabled Only that context is off. Fix the condition line. no plugin resolved the condition '…'; context '…' is disabled A condition from a plugin that is not installed. … has the same Priority 50 a","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"discards","u":"troubleshooting.html#discards","x":"Why an answer that arrived was not applied. Value Meaning STALE_SEQUENCE A newer request of the same encounter was already sent; the older answer is dropped. SESSION_CHANGED The mob's session changed while the request was in flight (it was reloaded, respawned or moved to another encounter). SESSION_INACTIVE The mob's session is not active, or a debug intent holds it. CATALOG_CHANGED Profiles or MythicMobs were reloaded while the request was in flight. MODEL_CHANGED A model other than the configured one answered. TOO_OLD The answer arrived after it could still be applied (see decision.maxDecisionAgeMillis). TARGET_CHANGED The mob changed target; the answer was about the old one. PROBE_UNAVAILABLE The mob could not be read when the answer arrived. SITUATION_CHANGED A reactive answer no longer matched the live situation. GROUP_EPOCH_CHANGED The group plan was captured under another group membership; the leader's question is kept.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"outcomes","u":"troubleshooting.html#cast-outcomes","x":"Result of trying to cast the skill of an intent. Value Meaning CAST The skill was cast. DEFERRED_INVULNERABLE The target is in its invulnerability frames; the cast is retried in a later tick. SKIPPED_SHIELD The target blocks with a shield and the skill cannot ignore it. REJECTED_BY_MYTHICMOBS MythicMobs refused the skill (a failed chance, a cancelled event, no charges left). NOT_ELIGIBLE The skill is not ready yet (cooldown, reach, conditions); retried in a later tick. EXPIRED The intent expired before the skill could be cast.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"dispatch","u":"troubleshooting.html#dispatch","x":"What happened to an encounter that was due for a decision. Value Meaning SENT A request was sent. EMPTY_CAPTURE No member of the encounter could be read. NO_QUESTIONS No mob qualified for a question (an active session with installed goals, no debug intent, a perceived target and two distinct eligible tactics), and there is no group plan question. SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE The service is not ready, is paused, or is running its single trial request. NO_BUDGET A request, token or in-flight limit refused the prepared request; the mobs play locally. NOTHING_TO_ASK While preparing, no question kept two options that read differently: nothing is sent or reserved and the mobs play locally. PREPARE_FAILED The request could not be encoded (for example, over the size guard). It counts as INVALID_REQUEST, nothing is sent, that encounter plays locally and the service is not paused, so other encounters keep asking. CLIENT_ERROR The client failed to accept the request (a bug); counted as INVALID_REQUEST. CACHE_HIT An identical earlier answer was reused (only with decision.answerCache on).","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"failures","u":"troubleshooting.html#failures","x":"Why a request to Jev failed. Value Meaning AUTHENTICATION The key was rejected (401). MODEL_UNAVAILABLE The model does not exist. INVALID_REQUEST The request was rejected, or was too large to prepare. RATE_LIMITED The account's rate limit was hit (429). OVERLOADED The service is overloaded (529). SERVICE_ERROR The service answered with an error status (a 5xx other than 529, or an unexpected status). NETWORK The connection failed. TIMEOUT No answer arrived within jev.timeoutMillis. INVALID_RESPONSE The answer could not be understood.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Other counters","u":"troubleshooting.html#counters","x":"The Counters section of status groups running totals. Each group lists only non-zero values, or none. totals also counts options_merged (options not sent because they read like another option) and the contingencies asked, fired and effective.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Fallback reasons","u":"troubleshooting.html#fallback-reasons","x":"When a mob drops to a lower control level, the reason shows in inspect (Why: last fallback …), in status (fallbacks and Recent fallbacks) and, with decision.logDecisions, as Mob <uuid> fell back: <REASON>. Value Meaning What to do SERVICE_PAUSED The service is paused (429, 529, timeout, network) or still being checked. Wait out the pause; check latency and limits if it repeats. SERVICE_BLOCKED The service cannot be used without a configuration change: UNCONFIGURED, INVALID_CONFIGURATION, INVALID_CREDENTIALS or INVALID_MODEL. Read State in /thepredict status, fix the key or the model and restart. NO_BUDGET The request, token or in-flight budget is spent (server, world or encounter). Review decision.maxRequestsPerMinute, decision.maxInputTokensPerMinute and the load. Mobs without budget fight locally, without errors. LOW_CONFIDENCE Several answers in a row stayed below the minimum confidence. Review the profile: contexts, tactic names and descriptions. INVALID_RESPONSE The answer had no applicable tactic. Make sure the profile offers eligible tactics; report it with the log if it repeats. EXPIRED The intent expired without a replacement. Normal now and then. If frequent, compare roundtrip latency with profileDefaults.maximumIntentDurationTicks. NO_PROGRESS The movement made no progress for two decisions (target on a pillar, behind a wall, in water). Check the terrain, the arena and the mob's species. RETREAT_LIMIT The encounter already has as many simultaneous retreats as it allows (one per three members, at least one). Nothing; it is coordination between mobs. SESSION_INVALI","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Service states","u":"troubleshooting.html#service-states","x":"The State line of /thepredict status and the answer of /thepredict check. Value Meaning What to do UNCONFIGURED No key is configured. Set the TYPESAFE_API_KEY environment variable (or jev.apiKey) and restart. Meanwhile mobs fight with their local planner, at no cost. INVALID_CONFIGURATION config.yml is invalid; the console names the file, the path and the reason. Fix the file and restart. ThePredict stays inactive; MythicMobs keeps working. CHECKING The service is being checked (at startup, or after a pause). Wait for the result in the console or in /thepredict status. READY The service accepts requests. Nothing. PAUSED Requests are paused after a rate limit (429), an overload (529), network or service errors, two timeouts in a row, three invalid answers in a row, or a rejected request (60 s). Wait: ThePredict retries with a growing pause (1 to 60 s), then a single trial request. If it repeats, check roundtrip latency and the limits. INVALID_CREDENTIALS The key was rejected (401). Check the key in your TypeSafe account, set it and restart: the key is read only at startup. INVALID_MODEL The configured model does not exist. Use the tested model ID jev-1.13.0 and restart. With INVALID_CREDENTIALS (a 401 or 403) or INVALID_MODEL, ThePredict sends nothing until a restart or a /thepredict check; mobs fight locally meanwhile. The key itself is read only at startup.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Startup messages","u":"troubleshooting.html#startup","x":"ThePredict reports a fresh installation as information, never as an error. Each line ends with the next step. Console line What it means Startup prerequisite failed: Java <n> is unsupported; ThePredict requires Java 25 or newer The plugin disables itself. Run the server on Java 25. Startup prerequisite failed: Minecraft <v> is unsupported; this Paper build requires 26.2 or newer Use Paper 26.2. Startup prerequisite failed: MythicMobs <v> is unsupported; minimum version is 5.13.1 Update MythicMobs Premium. MythicMobs must be installed and enabled means it is missing or failed. Created setup files: … First start: the missing setup files were created. Existing files are never replaced. Invalid configuration: <file>: <path>: <reason>. ThePredict stays inactive and /thepredict status still works. Next: fix plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.yml and restart the server, then run /thepredict status. config.yml has an unknown key, an old-schema key or a value out of range. MythicMobs keeps working; storage is not opened. Jev not configured: set TYPESAFE_API_KEY or jev.apiKey. MythicMobs works normally. Next: set the key and restart the server, then run /thepredict status. No key. Bound mobs fight with their local planner, at no cost. No profiles: copy examples/ or create a .yml file in plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/. Next: read plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/README.txt. No profile yet. <n> profiles read, but no mob targeted by a profile has Predictor: true. Next: set Predictor: true on the MythicMobs mob and run /mm reload. Profiles load, but no mob has opted in. Profil","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"First checks","u":"troubleshooting.html#first-checks","x":"/thepredict status. Read State (the Jev service), Profiles (the catalog), Bound mobs (who ThePredict controls, by level) and Recent failures / Recent fallbacks. /thepredict inspect nearest next to the mob. Session says whether it is bound, Intent what it is doing, Why the last fallback and cast result, Goals whether its movement goals are installed. The console. Every profile problem names the file and the path: <file>: <profile>.<path>: <message>. For a live decision log, set decision.logDecisions to true and restart. Reload or restart? Profiles, mob and skill files: /mm reload. config.yml and the key: restart the server, there is no reload command. After /minecraft:reload (datapack tags), run /mm reload too.","k":"section","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"UNCONFIGURED","u":"troubleshooting.html#ServiceState-UNCONFIGURED","x":"No key is configured.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"INVALID_CONFIGURATION","u":"troubleshooting.html#ServiceState-INVALID_CONFIGURATION","x":"config.yml is invalid; the console names the file, the path and the reason.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"CHECKING","u":"troubleshooting.html#ServiceState-CHECKING","x":"The service is being checked (at startup, or after a pause).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"READY","u":"troubleshooting.html#ServiceState-READY","x":"The service accepts requests.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"PAUSED","u":"troubleshooting.html#ServiceState-PAUSED","x":"Requests are paused after a rate limit (429), an overload (529), network or service errors, two timeouts in a row, three invalid answers in a row, or a rejected request (60 s).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"INVALID_CREDENTIALS","u":"troubleshooting.html#ServiceState-INVALID_CREDENTIALS","x":"The key was rejected (401).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"INVALID_MODEL","u":"troubleshooting.html#ServiceState-INVALID_MODEL","x":"The configured model does not exist.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SERVICE_PAUSED","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-SERVICE_PAUSED","x":"The service is paused (429, 529, timeout, network) or still being checked.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SERVICE_BLOCKED","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-SERVICE_BLOCKED","x":"The service cannot be used without a configuration change: UNCONFIGURED, INVALID_CONFIGURATION, INVALID_CREDENTIALS or INVALID_MODEL.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"NO_BUDGET","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-NO_BUDGET","x":"The request, token or in-flight budget is spent (server, world or encounter).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"LOW_CONFIDENCE","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-LOW_CONFIDENCE","x":"Several answers in a row stayed below the minimum confidence.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"INVALID_RESPONSE","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-INVALID_RESPONSE","x":"The answer had no applicable tactic.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"EXPIRED","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-EXPIRED","x":"The intent expired without a replacement.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"NO_PROGRESS","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-NO_PROGRESS","x":"The movement made no progress for two decisions (target on a pillar, behind a wall, in water).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"RETREAT_LIMIT","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-RETREAT_LIMIT","x":"The encounter already has as many simultaneous retreats as it allows (one per three members, at least one).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SESSION_INVALID","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-SESSION_INVALID","x":"The mob was reloaded, died or changed world.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"INTERNAL_ERROR","u":"troubleshooting.html#FallbackReason-INTERNAL_ERROR","x":"An exception inside ThePredict; the console says how many sessions fell back to the base AI.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"AUTHENTICATION","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-AUTHENTICATION","x":"The key was rejected (401).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"MODEL_UNAVAILABLE","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-MODEL_UNAVAILABLE","x":"The model does not exist.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"INVALID_REQUEST","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-INVALID_REQUEST","x":"The request was rejected, or was too large to prepare.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"RATE_LIMITED","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-RATE_LIMITED","x":"The account's rate limit was hit (429).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"OVERLOADED","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-OVERLOADED","x":"The service is overloaded (529).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SERVICE_ERROR","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-SERVICE_ERROR","x":"The service answered with an error status (a 5xx other than 529, or an unexpected status).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"NETWORK","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-NETWORK","x":"The connection failed.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"TIMEOUT","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-TIMEOUT","x":"No answer arrived within jev.timeoutMillis.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"INVALID_RESPONSE","u":"troubleshooting.html#FailureKind-INVALID_RESPONSE","x":"The answer could not be understood.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SENT","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-SENT","x":"A request was sent.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"EMPTY_CAPTURE","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-EMPTY_CAPTURE","x":"No member of the encounter could be read.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"NO_QUESTIONS","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-NO_QUESTIONS","x":"No mob qualified for a question (an active session with installed goals, no debug intent, a perceived target and two distinct eligible tactics), and there is no group plan question.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE","x":"The service is not ready, is paused, or is running its single trial request.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"NO_BUDGET","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-NO_BUDGET","x":"A request, token or in-flight limit refused the prepared request; the mobs play locally.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"NOTHING_TO_ASK","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-NOTHING_TO_ASK","x":"While preparing, no question kept two options that read differently: nothing is sent or reserved and the mobs play locally.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"PREPARE_FAILED","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-PREPARE_FAILED","x":"The request could not be encoded (for example, over the size guard). It counts as INVALID_REQUEST, nothing is sent, that encounter plays locally and the service is not paused, so other encounters keep","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"CLIENT_ERROR","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-CLIENT_ERROR","x":"The client failed to accept the request (a bug); counted as INVALID_REQUEST.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"CACHE_HIT","u":"troubleshooting.html#DispatchOutcome-CACHE_HIT","x":"An identical earlier answer was reused (only with decision.answerCache on).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"CAST","u":"troubleshooting.html#ExecutionOutcome-CAST","x":"The skill was cast.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"DEFERRED_INVULNERABLE","u":"troubleshooting.html#ExecutionOutcome-DEFERRED_INVULNERABLE","x":"The target is in its invulnerability frames; the cast is retried in a later tick.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SKIPPED_SHIELD","u":"troubleshooting.html#ExecutionOutcome-SKIPPED_SHIELD","x":"The target blocks with a shield and the skill cannot ignore it.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"REJECTED_BY_MYTHICMOBS","u":"troubleshooting.html#ExecutionOutcome-REJECTED_BY_MYTHICMOBS","x":"MythicMobs refused the skill (a failed chance, a cancelled event, no charges left).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"NOT_ELIGIBLE","u":"troubleshooting.html#ExecutionOutcome-NOT_ELIGIBLE","x":"The skill is not ready yet (cooldown, reach, conditions); retried in a later tick.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"EXPIRED","u":"troubleshooting.html#ExecutionOutcome-EXPIRED","x":"The intent expired before the skill could be cast.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"STALE_SEQUENCE","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-STALE_SEQUENCE","x":"A newer request of the same encounter was already sent; the older answer is dropped.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SESSION_CHANGED","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-SESSION_CHANGED","x":"The mob's session changed while the request was in flight (it was reloaded, respawned or moved to another encounter).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SESSION_INACTIVE","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-SESSION_INACTIVE","x":"The mob's session is not active, or a debug intent holds it.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"CATALOG_CHANGED","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-CATALOG_CHANGED","x":"Profiles or MythicMobs were reloaded while the request was in flight.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"MODEL_CHANGED","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-MODEL_CHANGED","x":"A model other than the configured one answered.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"TOO_OLD","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-TOO_OLD","x":"The answer arrived after it could still be applied (see decision.maxDecisionAgeMillis).","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"TARGET_CHANGED","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-TARGET_CHANGED","x":"The mob changed target; the answer was about the old one.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"PROBE_UNAVAILABLE","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-PROBE_UNAVAILABLE","x":"The mob could not be read when the answer arrived.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"SITUATION_CHANGED","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-SITUATION_CHANGED","x":"A reactive answer no longer matched the live situation.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"GROUP_EPOCH_CHANGED","u":"troubleshooting.html#DiscardReason-GROUP_EPOCH_CHANGED","x":"The group plan was captured under another group membership; the leader's question is kept.","k":"value","p":"Troubleshooting & status"},{"t":"Decision","u":"profile-reference.html#decision","x":"The four keys are parsed and validated (for example MaxOptions must be 0 or 2 to 8) and kept for overlays, but this build keeps using the global decision.* values in fights. A value other than inherit (or 0) logs a warning when the profile loads.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Patterns","u":"profile-reference.html#patterns","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group","u":"profile-reference.html#group","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Zone","u":"profile-reference.html#zone","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise","u":"profile-reference.html#poise","x":"Profile only, with no global keys. Without this section the mob has no poise and cannot be staggered. The defaults below apply to keys left out of a Poise section.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph","u":"profile-reference.html#telegraph","x":"Changing soon Tells and telegraphing will be redefined in an upcoming release. Without this section the profile inherits telegraph.* from config.yml.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances","u":"profile-reference.html#stances","x":"Without this section the profile inherits stance.* from config.yml. See Stances, tells & poise.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty","u":"profile-reference.html#difficulty","x":"Changing soon Difficulty is about to be redefined as levels of intelligence and aggression. This section documents how the current build works.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Entities","u":"profile-reference.html#participants-entities","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Participants","u":"profile-reference.html#participants","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Reactions","u":"profile-reference.html#reactions","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing","u":"profile-reference.html#timing","x":"The heartbeat, the decision intervals and the contingencies are global (decision.* and profileDefaults.*); a profile cannot change them.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Threat","u":"profile-reference.html#threat","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Health","u":"profile-reference.html#health","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Arena","u":"profile-reference.html#movement-arena","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Approach","u":"profile-reference.html#movement-approach","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Retreat","u":"profile-reference.html#movement-retreat","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Band","u":"profile-reference.html#movement-band","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement","u":"profile-reference.html#movement","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Contexts","u":"profile-reference.html#contexts","x":"Contexts.<id> — up to 16 contexts. The ID follows the choice ID rules. idle, attacking_phase, tracking_enemy and low_health_phase are shortcut contexts computed by ThePredict and take no Conditions (see Profiles, tactics & contexts).","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Tactics","u":"profile-reference.html#tactics","x":"Tactics.<id> — 1 to 255 tactics. The ID is the option name Jev reads: [a-z][a-z0-9_]{2,39} (3 to 40 characters, starting with a letter). none and the prefixes debug_, tell_ and stance_ are reserved.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choice telegraph","u":"profile-reference.html#choice-telegraph","x":"Changing soon Tells will be redefined in an upcoming release.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Purpose (administrator override)","u":"profile-reference.html#purpose","x":"Choices.<id>.Purpose replaces the skill's Intention line for that choice. It is internal data for an administrator who must tune one mob; authors should write the Intention line instead (see Skills & intents).","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices","u":"profile-reference.html#choices","x":"Choices.<id> — one entry per skill (or vanilla hit) the tactics can use. The ID is yours: [a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}, local to the profile, never sent to Jev.","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Profile root","u":"profile-reference.html#root","x":"","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Mob file keys","u":"profile-reference.html#mob-file","x":"These keys go in the MythicMobs mob file (plugins/MythicMobs/Mobs/*.yml), next to Type and Health, not in the profile. A wrong value is a catalog error that names the mob, and the mob stays unbound. plugins/MythicMobs/Mobs/MyBoss.ymlYAML MyBoss: Type: ZOMBIE Health: 200 Predictor: true PredictorDifficulty: Difícil PredictorEntropy: false","k":"section","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Profile reference","u":"profile-reference.html","x":"A profile file is a .yml or .yaml file in plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/Profiles/ that starts with schemaVersion: 2 and holds one or more profiles. Each profile is keyed by its ID (snake_case is recommended). For the concepts behind these keys, start with Profiles, tactics & contexts. Tip Strict by design An unknown key is an error that names the file and the path (is not a known field), and a profile with an error is skipped while the others keep loading. Values a profile does not set come from profileDefaults in config.yml, and no profile can widen the global decision.* limits. Note off and on need no quotes YAML reads a bare off or on as a boolean; every mode key of a profile reads it back as off or on, so Native: off and Native: \"off\" mean the same. Note Keys with no effect yet A few keys are accepted and validated but not used by this build. They are marked no effect yet below; when a profile gives one of them a value other than its default, the profile still loads and the console logs <file>: <profile>.<path>: has no effect in this build. A profile that uses most sections AIConfig/Profiles/guardian_full.ymlYAML schemaVersion: 2 guardian_full: MythicID: ThePredictGuardian TypeOfMythicID: MOB Type: NORMAL Objective: Protect the altar and punish players who attack it from range Choices: melee: { MythicID: ThePredictGuardianMelee, TypeOfMythicID: SKILL, RequiresTarget: true } ranged: { MythicID: ThePredictGuardianRanged } defense: { MythicID: ThePredictGuardianDefense, RequiresTarget: false } punch: { Kind: VANILLA_MELEE } Tactics: press_and_strike: { Movement: APPROACH, Ch","k":"page","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Predictor","u":"profile-reference.html#mob.Predictor","x":" In the MythicMobs mob file. Turns ThePredict on for this mob. The mob also needs a valid profile whose MythicID names it. Any value other than true or false is a catalog error (<Mob>.Predictor: must be true or false). With false, or withou","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"PredictorTraining","u":"profile-reference.html#mob.PredictorTraining","x":" In the mob file. With true (and Predictor: true), this mob may also explore other tactics against players, to collect learning data (see Learning & training). Players do not see it. Remove the key to turn it off; there is no command or glo","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"PredictorDifficulty","u":"profile-reference.html#mob.PredictorDifficulty","x":" In the mob file, with Predictor: true. Difficulty preset of this mob: the target length of a whole fight against players. Another value is a catalog error and the mob stays unbound. See Difficulty. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"PredictorEntropy","u":"profile-reference.html#mob.PredictorEntropy","x":" In the mob file, with Predictor: true. Opt-in lethal mode: the mob always plays at full pressure and its reaction, adaptation and replanning times shrink during the fight down to the preset's floor. It never reads hidden player input. See ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"MythicID","u":"profile-reference.html#MythicID","x":" Exact MythicMobs mob ID this profile controls. IDs are case-sensitive; when the case is the only difference, the error suggests the right spelling (unknown mob 'guardian'; IDs are case-sensitive, did you mean 'Guardian'?). Two profiles for","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"TypeOfMythicID","u":"profile-reference.html#TypeOfMythicID","x":" Kept for compatibility with old profiles. Only MOB. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Type","u":"profile-reference.html#Type","x":" Profile mode. Only NORMAL in this release. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Objective","u":"profile-reference.html#Objective","x":" What the mob tries to achieve, in short, clear English. It reaches Jev with every question. The catalog warns, without blocking, when the text may not be English. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices","x":" The skills (or the vanilla hit) the tactics can use, keyed by a choice ID of your own ([a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}). Choice IDs never reach Jev. See Choices.<id>.* below. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Tactics","u":"profile-reference.html#Tactics","x":" What Jev or the local planner can choose. The tactic ID is the option name Jev reads, so make it describe the action in English. See Tactics.<id>.*. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Contexts","u":"profile-reference.html#Contexts","x":" Situations that limit which tactics are eligible, written with MythicMobs conditions or as shortcut contexts. See Contexts.<id>.*. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement","x":" Distances and speeds of the movements. Values it does not set come from profileDefaults. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Health","u":"profile-reference.html#Health","x":" Health thresholds of the CRITICAL and WOUNDED bands. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Threat","u":"profile-reference.html#Threat","x":" Weights of the enriched threat ThePredict adds to the MythicMobs threat table. See Targets, participants & threat. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"BaseAI","u":"profile-reference.html#BaseAI","x":" Lines in MythicMobs AIGoalSelectors syntax: what the mob does at level 4 (BASE), when ThePredict does not control it. A clear line is dropped. If a line names a goal MythicMobs does not know, the installation is refused and the mob keeps i","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing","x":" Confidence, switch margin, question detail, casting and the per-tick layer of this profile. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Reactions","u":"profile-reference.html#Reactions","x":" Which reaction bands run before the tactic's own skill. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Participants","u":"profile-reference.html#Participants","x":" Which players and other entities the mobs of this profile may perceive, target and fight. Without it, the global participants section applies. See Targets, participants & threat. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty","x":" Tuning of the target-time controller for this profile. See Difficulty. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances","x":" Stance sharing and timing for this profile. See Stances, tells & poise. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph","u":"profile-reference.html#Telegraph","x":" Tell enforcement and feints for this profile. See Stances, tells & poise. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise","x":" Poise and stagger. Without this section the mob has no poise and cannot be staggered. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Zone","u":"profile-reference.html#Zone","x":" Terrain reading for this profile. See Zones & terrain. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group","u":"profile-reference.html#Group","x":" Group coordination for this profile. See Groups. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Patterns","u":"profile-reference.html#Patterns","x":" Enemy pattern reading for this profile. See Patterns. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Decision","u":"profile-reference.html#Decision","x":" Per-profile overrides of pruning, option cap, candidate scoring and diversity. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Kind","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Kind","x":"MYTHIC_SKILL casts a MythicMobs skill. VANILLA_MELEE deals a vanilla hit (never farther than Movement.MeleeReach, at most one hit every 20 ticks, like vanilla) and takes no MythicID.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.MythicID","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.MythicID","x":" Exact MythicMobs skill ID (case-sensitive). The skill should declare an Intention line (see Skills & intents). Must be absent for VANILLA_MELEE. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.TypeOfMythicID","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.TypeOfMythicID","x":" Kept for compatibility. Only SKILL. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.RequiresTarget","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.RequiresTarget","x":" Whether the choice needs a target. A self-heal or a self-buff is usually false. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.CD","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.CD","x":" Extra cooldown per mob, for compatibility only. Prefer the skill's native Cooldown (and Charges), which ThePredict reads and respects. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose","x":"Administrator override, not for authors. A full typed purpose that replaces the skill's Intention line for this choice (the binder warns Choices.<id>.Purpose overrides the Intention of skill '<S>'). It is the only form that takes numbers (R","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Telegraph","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Telegraph","x":" Overrides what ThePredict deduces about this skill's tell: Danger, Answer and RecoveryTicks. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Displacement","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Displacement","x":" Overrides how ThePredict reads the skill's push (it reads damage knockback, throw, leap, explosions and pulls). A skill with nested skills, projectiles or auras is assumed to KNOCKBACK; set Displacement: NONE if it does not push. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.TargetsAllies","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.TargetsAllies","x":" Overrides whether ThePredict thinks the skill can reach allies (it reads targeters such as @MobsInRadius, @Parent or @Children). Matters for the SUPPORT group role. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.Roles","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.Roles","x":" What the skill is for. The first role is the primary one. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.Delivery","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.Delivery","x":" How the skill reaches its target. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.Reach","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.Reach","x":" Reach of the skill. Required with MELEE and CONE; not allowed with SELF and AREA_AROUND_SELF. A reach beyond Movement.RangedReach warns that Jev reads it as beyond ranged reach. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.Radius","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.Radius","x":" Area radius. Required with AREA_AROUND_SELF and AREA_AT_TARGET; not allowed otherwise. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.WindUp","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.WindUp","x":" Wind-up before the hit lands. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.Damage","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.Damage","x":" Damage tier. Required when Roles has DAMAGE or FINISHER, and then it cannot be NONE. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.BestWhen","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.BestWhen","x":" Situations where the skill works best. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.Risks","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.Risks","x":" What can go wrong with it. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Purpose.IgnoresShield","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Purpose.IgnoresShield","x":" The skill goes through shields. Cannot be combined with the BLOCKED_BY_SHIELD risk. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Telegraph.Danger","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Telegraph.Danger","x":" Danger class of the hit, instead of the one ThePredict deduces from the skill. MEDIUM and above are enforced against players. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Telegraph.Answer","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Telegraph.Answer","x":" What the target should do to avoid the hit. It wins over the skill's ANSWER_* primitive and over the answer deduced from the delivery, and decides which PREDICTOR_TELL_* signal is sent. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Choices.<id>.Telegraph.RecoveryTicks","u":"profile-reference.html#Choices.Telegraph.RecoveryTicks","x":" Recovery after the hit, instead of the one read from the skill's trailing delay lines. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Tactics.<id>.Movement","u":"profile-reference.html#Tactics.Movement","x":" How the mob moves while the tactic runs (see Movement & goals). FLANK requires a Choice. Species with a Brain only accept NONE. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Tactics.<id>.Choice","u":"profile-reference.html#Tactics.Choice","x":" ID of the choice this tactic casts. A tactic without a choice only moves. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Tactics.<id>.Description","u":"profile-reference.html#Tactics.Description","x":" What the tactic does, in English, for Jev. With standard and full detail it is sent whole; with compact only an excerpt is used, when needed to tell two options apart. Put the essential first. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Tactics.<id>.Priority","u":"profile-reference.html#Tactics.Priority","x":" Order of the local planner: among the eligible tactics, the highest priority wins. Also decides which options are kept when a question is over the option cap. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Tactics.<id>.Stance","u":"profile-reference.html#Tactics.Stance","x":" Base stance while this tactic runs, instead of the one Stances.ByMovement gives its movement. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Contexts.<id>.Conditions","u":"profile-reference.html#Contexts.Conditions","x":" MythicMobs condition lines, at least one; all must hold. Only entity conditions work here (they are evaluated on the mob itself, outside any skill). Not allowed in the shortcut contexts idle, attacking_phase, tracking_enemy and low_health_","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Contexts.<id>.Priority","u":"profile-reference.html#Contexts.Priority","x":" When several contexts are active, the highest priority decides. With equal priorities, the one declared first wins and the catalog warns. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Contexts.<id>.Tactics","u":"profile-reference.html#Contexts.Tactics","x":" Tactics eligible while this context is active, at least one, no repeats. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Contexts.<id>.DirectTactic","u":"profile-reference.html#Contexts.DirectTactic","x":" Optional. Must be listed in Tactics. In local mode this tactic is picked directly while the context is active. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Band","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Band","x":" The keep-distance band: Inner and Outer. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Retreat","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Retreat","x":"Distance and Speed of RETREAT.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Approach","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Approach","x":"Speed of APPROACH, KEEP_DISTANCE and the walk back to the arena.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Arena","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Arena","x":" An optional arena around the spawn point. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.MeleeReach","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.MeleeReach","x":" Melee distance: the MELEE band, where APPROACH stops, and the reach of melee skills. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.RangedReach","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.RangedReach","x":" Up to this distance the target is in the RANGED band; farther, BEYOND. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Band.Inner","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Band.Inner","x":" Inner edge of KEEP_DISTANCE: closer than this, the mob backs away. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Band.Outer","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Band.Outer","x":" Outer edge of KEEP_DISTANCE: farther than this, the mob closes in. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Retreat.Distance","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Retreat.Distance","x":" Distance a retreat tries to open. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Retreat.Speed","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Retreat.Speed","x":" Speed while retreating. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Approach.Speed","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Approach.Speed","x":" Speed while approaching, keeping distance and returning to the arena. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Movement.Arena.Radius","u":"profile-reference.html#Movement.Arena.Radius","x":" When set, the mob walks back to its spawn point whenever it gets farther than this radius. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Health.Critical","u":"profile-reference.html#Health.Critical","x":" At or below this ratio of health (health plus absorption over max health) the band is CRITICAL, for the mob and for players. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Health.Wounded","u":"profile-reference.html#Health.Wounded","x":" At or below this ratio (and above Critical) the band is WOUNDED; above it, HEALTHY. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Threat.AssistsOthers","u":"profile-reference.html#Threat.AssistsOthers","x":" When a player heals or buffs other participants with a splash or lingering potion: weight × participants reached, added to that player in the table of every active member of the encounter. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Threat.RangedHarass","u":"profile-reference.html#Threat.RangedHarass","x":" Multiplies the final damage of each projectile from a player who is not the mob's target, in that mob's table. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Threat.BlockedHits","u":"profile-reference.html#Threat.BlockedHits","x":" Points per hit of the mob that the player blocks with a shield, in that mob's table. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Threat.UnreachableDecayPerSecond","u":"profile-reference.html#Threat.UnreachableDecayPerSecond","x":" Points per second the target loses while the mob cannot reach it on foot (after two decisions following a path that does not reach it). Ignored, with a warning, when the mob has ThreatTable.DecayUnreachable: true, so threat is not removed ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Threat.MaxPerWindow","u":"profile-reference.html#Threat.MaxPerWindow","x":" Cap of points added per mob table, player and fact in each 100-tick window. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.MinimumConfidence","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.MinimumConfidence","x":" Answers from Jev below this confidence are discarded. Raise it for a boss whose mistakes are expensive: more doubtful answers are dropped and the mob plays locally more often. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.SwitchMargin","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.SwitchMargin","x":" To switch tactic, the new one must beat the current one by this probability margin. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.QuestionDetail","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.QuestionDetail","x":" How much each option of this profile tells Jev, and its cost (see Jev connection). Never widens the global token limits. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.FitChecks","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.FitChecks","x":" Adds a yes/no \"does this option fit now?\" question per option, which can veto an option or rescue a low-confidence answer. Sent only with QuestionDetail: full (with another level it is ignored and the load warns). An error while decision.f","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.CastMode","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.CastMode","x":"any_ready: every skill with a valid Intention line fires on the first tick it is ready, besides the tactic's choice. intent_only: only the tactic's choice fires. The profile wins over the global value.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.ReadyHorizon","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.ReadyHorizon","x":" Ticks ahead a skill still counts as available for the question. Only the question uses it, never the local planner. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.TickLayer","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.TickLayer","x":" Per-tick layer of this profile. Asking for more than the global mode warns and uses the global one; an overlay that asks for more is lowered the same way. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.Reactions","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.Reactions","x":" Which reaction bands are evaluated (see How a fight runs). ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.ReactionDelay","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.ReactionDelay","x":" A reaction's trigger must hold this long before the reaction fires. Against players, the difficulty preset's reaction floor also applies. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.Cadence","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.Cadence","x":"reactive keeps the intent short (Timing.IntentHorizon) and extends it while nothing changes; it asks more often and costs more. standard is the saving mode: intents last the usual time.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.ReactiveInterval","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.ReactiveInterval","x":" Shortest gap between two reactive questions. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Timing.IntentHorizon","u":"profile-reference.html#Timing.IntentHorizon","x":" Length of a reactive intent. Ignored, with a warning, under Cadence: standard. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Reactions.Ahead","u":"profile-reference.html#Reactions.Ahead","x":" Reaction bands tried before the tactic's own skill. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Participants.PlayerGameModes","u":"profile-reference.html#Participants.PlayerGameModes","x":" Must be a subset of the global list; a mode outside it is an error. []: the mobs of this profile never perceive or attack players. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Participants.Entities","u":"profile-reference.html#Participants.Entities","x":" Non-player entities: Allow, Deny, PerceiveNonTargets. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Participants.Entities.Allow","u":"profile-reference.html#Participants.Entities.Allow","x":" Selectors added to participants.entities.allow. Ignored with a warning when participants.entities.profilesMayAllow is false. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Participants.Entities.Deny","u":"profile-reference.html#Participants.Entities.Deny","x":" Selectors added to participants.entities.deny; they never take part. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Participants.Entities.PerceiveNonTargets","u":"profile-reference.html#Participants.Entities.PerceiveNonTargets","x":"true (only allowed while the global key is true): the mobs also perceive allowed entities nearby, not only their target.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.Mode","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.Mode","x":" How this profile's mobs choose their pressure (see difficulty.defaultMode). ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.TargetSeconds","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.TargetSeconds","x":" Target length of a whole fight against players, instead of the preset's. A world override with a preset beats it. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.Tolerance","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.Tolerance","x":" Band around the target time inside which the in-fight controller does not react. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.MinRung","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.MinRung","x":" Lowest pressure rung the controller may use. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.MaxRung","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.MaxRung","x":" Highest pressure rung the controller may use. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.StartRung","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.StartRung","x":" Rung at the start of a fight. auto uses what the mob learned from earlier fights. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.InFight","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.InFight","x":" Whether the in-fight controller may move the rung during the fight. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.Learn","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.Learn","x":" Whether the between-fights learning may move the starting rung. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Difficulty.NativeLevel","u":"profile-reference.html#Difficulty.NativeLevel","x":" With spawn (and difficulty.nativeLevelAllowed true), five fights in a row at an extreme may move the MythicMobs level of the next spawn by ±1. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.Native","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.Native","x":" How the stance is shared with MythicMobs (see stance.nativeMode). ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.MinDwellTicks","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.MinDwellTicks","x":" Shortest time a base stance holds before it changes. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.HysteresisCycles","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.HysteresisCycles","x":" Reactive cycles in a row (2 ticks each) a new base stance must be asked for before it applies. The survival reaction EVADE_CRITICAL skips this wait and MinDwellTicks. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.Casts","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.Casts","x":" Base stance → roles that CastMode: any_ready may fire in that stance (DAMAGE, DEFENSE, ...). The tactic's own choice is never filtered. An unknown role is an error. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.ByMovement","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.ByMovement","x":" Base stance of each movement, for tactics without their own Tactics.<id>.Stance. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.EnragedContexts","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.EnragedContexts","x":" Contexts of this profile that enrage the mob while they are active: predictorstance{s=enraged} is true, and the mob receives PREDICTOR_STANCE_ENRAGED on entering and PREDICTOR_STANCE_CALM on leaving. An unknown context is an error. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.EnragedNative","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.EnragedNative","x":" Exact values of the mob's own MythicMobs stance that also enrage it. Only with Native: hybrid or write; with read or off the load warns. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Stances.Describe","u":"profile-reference.html#Stances.Describe","x":" Meant to add a stance phrase to the option text Jev reads for tactics with Stance:. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph.AgainstPlayers","u":"profile-reference.html#Telegraph.AgainstPlayers","x":" Enforce tell minimums against players (see telegraph.againstPlayers). ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph.Commitment","u":"profile-reference.html#Telegraph.Commitment","x":" Chance that a tell is real. With 100 there are no feints; lower values let the mob feint. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph.EntropyCommitment","u":"profile-reference.html#Telegraph.EntropyCommitment","x":" The same chance while Entropy is on. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph.AgainstEntities","u":"profile-reference.html#Telegraph.AgainstEntities","x":" Enforce tell minimums against non-player targets. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph.ShortWindUp","u":"profile-reference.html#Telegraph.ShortWindUp","x":" What happens when a skill's wind-up is shorter than its minimum against a player: lead sends the tell first and casts when the minimum is met; immediate casts at once with the author's wind-up (the binder warns, and status counts those hit","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Telegraph.DefaultRecoveryTicks","u":"profile-reference.html#Telegraph.DefaultRecoveryTicks","x":" Recovery after a skill with RISK_LEAVES_CASTER_EXPOSED or RISK_ROOTS_CASTER when neither the choice nor the skill gives one. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise.Max","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise.Max","x":" Share of max health that must be dealt to break poise. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise.RegenDelayTicks","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise.RegenDelayTicks","x":" Without damage for this long, poise starts to recover. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise.RegenPerSecond","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise.RegenPerSecond","x":" Share recovered every second after the delay. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise.WindUpMultiplier","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise.WindUpMultiplier","x":" Damage taken during a wind-up counts this much more. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise.BlockedHitPoise","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise.BlockedHitPoise","x":" Poise the mob loses when the target blocks one of its HEAVY or SEVERE hits with a shield. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise.StaggerTicks","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise.StaggerTicks","x":" Length of a stagger: the mob casts nothing, does not react and ThePredict does not move it. A break during a wind-up interrupts it. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Poise.ImmunityTicks","u":"profile-reference.html#Poise.ImmunityTicks","x":" After a stagger, poise does not fill for this long. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Zone.Mode","u":"profile-reference.html#Zone.Mode","x":" Zone mode of this profile. It can only lower zone.mode; a higher value warns and uses the global one. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Zone.Radius","u":"profile-reference.html#Zone.Radius","x":" Radius read around the fight. With an arena, the zone uses the arena radius plus 4 (capped by zone.maxRadiusBlocks). ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Zone.Facts","u":"profile-reference.html#Zone.Facts","x":" Whether terrain facts are published (to Jev, predictorzone and <caster.predictor.zone>) when the effective mode is full. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Zone.HazardPush","u":"profile-reference.html#Zone.HazardPush","x":" With exploit, the mob may push a non-player target into a hazard (lava, void, a deadly drop). It never does so against a player. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.Mode","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.Mode","x":" Group mode of this profile. It can only lower group.mode; a higher value warns and uses the global one. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.Squad","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.Squad","x":" Squad name ([a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}). When choosing a leader, a bigger squad wins ties of LeaderPriority. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.LeaderPriority","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.LeaderPriority","x":" Leader election: the member with the highest priority leads, then the one with the biggest squad, then the healthiest. Without any priority or squad in the encounter there is no leader. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.Weight","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.Weight","x":" How much of a player's attacker cap this mob takes (a big boss can count as 2 or more). ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.Roles","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.Roles","x":" Roles the group may give this mob. reserve is always possible. Each named role must be one the profile can fill, or the load fails. Roles only exist while the group follows a plan (see Groups). ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.OnLeaderDeath","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.OnLeaderDeath","x":"succeed elects a new leader. break breaks the group for group.brokenTicks.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.AgainstEntities","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.AgainstEntities","x":"free: the group's fairness limits only record against non-player targets. fair: they apply against entities too.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.Questions","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.Questions","x":" Read from the leader's profile in full mode: which questions the encounter's request carries. plan_and_leader: the group plan question and the leader's own question. plan_only: only the plan question. leader_only: only the leader's questio","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Group.PlanQuestion","u":"profile-reference.html#Group.PlanQuestion","x":" Meant to choose when the group plan question is attached: only when the group changes, or on every heartbeat. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Patterns.Mode","u":"profile-reference.html#Patterns.Mode","x":" Pattern mode of this profile. It can only lower patterns.mode; a higher value warns is above Patterns.Mode and uses the minimum. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Patterns.AgainstEntities","u":"profile-reference.html#Patterns.AgainstEntities","x":"free: against non-player targets the exploitation quota does not apply. fair: it applies against entities too.","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Patterns.Facts","u":"profile-reference.html#Patterns.Facts","x":" In full mode, whether short pattern phrases reach Jev. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Decision.Pruning","u":"profile-reference.html#Decision.Pruning","x":" Per-profile pruning; inherit keeps decision.pruning. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Decision.MaxOptions","u":"profile-reference.html#Decision.MaxOptions","x":" Per-profile option cap; 0 keeps decision.maxOptionsPerQuestion. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Decision.CandidateScoring","u":"profile-reference.html#Decision.CandidateScoring","x":" Per-profile candidate scoring; inherit keeps decision.candidateScoring. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"Decision.Diversity","u":"profile-reference.html#Decision.Diversity","x":" Per-profile candidate diversity; inherit keeps the global behavior. ","k":"key","p":"Profile reference"},{"t":"autoconfig","u":"config-reference.html#autoconfig","x":"Limits of the overlay workflow. See Profile overlays.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.voi","u":"config-reference.html#learning-voi","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.calibration","u":"config-reference.html#learning-calibration","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.exploration","u":"config-reference.html#learning-exploration","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning","u":"config-reference.html#learning","x":"Outcome collection and calibration. See Learning & training.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns","u":"config-reference.html#patterns","x":"Enemy habits. See Patterns.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group","u":"config-reference.html#group","x":"Several mobs in one encounter. See Groups.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone","u":"config-reference.html#zone","x":"Terrain reading. See Zones & terrain.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"stance","u":"config-reference.html#stance","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.answerTicks","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph-answerTicks","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.minTicks","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph-minTicks","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph","x":"Changing soon Tells and telegraphing will be redefined in an upcoming release. This section documents how the current build works. ThePredict never adds particles or sounds: a tell is a set of signals your own skills can react to. See Stances, tells & poise.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage","u":"config-reference.html#storage","x":"The SQLite aggregates database, written beside the records folder. See Storage & records.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"Presets","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty-presets","x":"Each preset under difficulty.presets.<name> holds four numbers. The names are facil, normal, dificil, caos and vacio. Mob file name config.yml key Target fight length Reaction floor (ticks) Entropy floor (ticks) Entropy start Fácil facil 45 min 5 4 7 s Normal normal 30 min 5 3 5 s Difícil dificil 15 min 3 0 3.5 s Caos caos 10 min 1 0 1.5 s Vacío vacio 5 min 0 0 0 s #facil #normal #dificil #caos #vacio","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty","x":"Changing soon Difficulty is about to be redefined as levels of intelligence and aggression instead of a target fight length. This section documents how the current build works.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records","u":"config-reference.html#records","x":"Local JSONL records of each fight. See Storage & records.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants.entities","u":"config-reference.html#participants-entities","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants","u":"config-reference.html#participants","x":"Optional. Without it, or with the shipped values, mobs only perceive, target and fight players in SURVIVAL or ADVENTURE. See Targets, participants & threat.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults","x":"Values every profile inherits unless it sets its own. The cross-checks keep the timings consistent: decision.encounterHeartbeatTicks ≥ minimumDecisionIntervalTicks, maximumIntentDurationTicks ≥ minimumDecisionIntervalTicks, jev.timeoutMillis < maximumIntentDurationTicks × 50 and decision.maxDecisionAgeMillis ≥ jev.timeoutMillis.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"debug","u":"config-reference.html#debug","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer","u":"config-reference.html#decision-tickLayer","x":"The per-tick layer: reactions and micro-movements between two decisions. See How a fight runs.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision","u":"config-reference.html#decision","x":"Global limits that no profile can widen, plus the defaults profiles inherit for confidence, question detail and casting.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev","u":"config-reference.html#jev","x":"How ThePredict reaches Jev. See Jev connection for the key, the service check and the costs.","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"Root","u":"config-reference.html#root","x":"","k":"section","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"config.yml reference","u":"config-reference.html","x":"The master file lives at plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/config.yml. ThePredict creates it on the first start and never overwrites it. Every value in the shipped file is the default, and units are in the key names (Millis, Ticks, Blocks, Micros). Watch out Read once, at startup config.yml and the Jev key are read only when the server starts. After a change, restart the server. /mm reload re-reads the profiles, not this file. An unknown key, a key from the old schema or a value out of range keeps ThePredict inactive and names the file, the path and the reason; MythicMobs keeps working. How to read the entries below: Default is the value in the shipped file, Range comes from the plugin's validation, and keys a profile can override link to the Profile reference. Keys marked changing soon will be redefined in an upcoming release; keys marked no effect yet are accepted and validated but this build does not read them, and most of them log AIConfig/config.yml: <key>: has no effect in this build at startup when set to anything other than the shipped value. Note Sections not covered here The shipped file also holds a few sections for experimental features that stay off or record-only by default. They are not covered by this documentation: leave them as shipped. Section Keys What it controls jev 9 How ThePredict reaches Jev: endpoint, model, key and timeouts. decision 47 Global decision limits and behavior: request budget, confidence, questions, casting and the tick layer. A profile never widens these limits. records 10 Local JSONL event records: level, body policy, rotation and retentio","k":"page","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"schemaVersion","u":"config-reference.html#schemaVersion","x":" Schema of the file. Required, and only 2 is accepted. A file without it that holds schema 1 keys (such as provider) is treated as an old configuration: ThePredict loads nothing from it and writes a migration proposal instead. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.baseUrl","u":"config-reference.html#jev.baseUrl","x":" TypeSafe Jev endpoint. https is required; plain http is accepted only for a loopback host (localhost, 127.0.0.1 or ::1). No user, query or fragment. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.model","u":"config-reference.html#jev.model","x":" Versioned Jev model ID, 1 to 64 letters, digits, ., _ or -. Only jev-1.13.0 is tested with this release. If a key is pasted here by mistake, the file is refused at load without showing the value. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.apiKeyEnvironment","u":"config-reference.html#jev.apiKeyEnvironment","x":" Name of the environment variable that holds the key (an empty value means only jev.apiKey is used). The variable wins over jev.apiKey when both are set. Write the variable's name here, never the key itself. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.apiKey","u":"config-reference.html#jev.apiKey","x":" Key stored in the file. Leave it empty and use the environment variable instead whenever you can. ThePredict never prints it: not in the console, not in /thepredict status, not in migration reports. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.provider","u":"config-reference.html#jev.provider","x":" Who answers the requests. Keep the default, typesafe, which reads the key from jev.apiKeyEnvironment or jev.apiKey. Other values are experimental and not covered by this documentation. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.timeoutMillis","u":"config-reference.html#jev.timeoutMillis","x":" How long one decision request may take. It must stay below profileDefaults.maximumIntentDurationTicks × 50 (2000 ms with the defaults), so an answer can arrive before the current intent expires. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.connectTimeoutMillis","u":"config-reference.html#jev.connectTimeoutMillis","x":" How long opening the connection may take. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.maxResponseBytes","u":"config-reference.html#jev.maxResponseBytes","x":" Largest response body ThePredict accepts. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"jev.maxStateChars","u":"config-reference.html#jev.maxStateChars","x":" Largest encoded combat state sent in one request. The client refuses to send a request whose state plus its longest question would pass 32 000 estimated tokens (48 000 characters at 1.5 characters per token); the cap of 45 000 leaves room ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxRequestsPerMinute","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxRequestsPerMinute","x":" Server-wide cap on requests to Jev. The default is half of the account limit published by TypeSafe (1 200 per minute). Mobs over budget fight with their local planner, without errors. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxRequestsPerMinutePerWorld","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxRequestsPerMinutePerWorld","x":" Cap per world. It cannot exceed decision.maxRequestsPerMinute. With one world, this is usually the limit that binds first. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxInFlightRequests","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxInFlightRequests","x":" Requests that may wait for an answer at the same time, server-wide. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxInFlightRequestsPerWorld","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxInFlightRequestsPerWorld","x":" Requests in flight per world. Cannot exceed decision.maxInFlightRequests. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxInputTokensPerMinute","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxInputTokensPerMinute","x":" Local cap on input tokens sent per minute. With many mobs in many worlds this is the limit that binds, and it bounds the cost: at the cap, 600 000 tokens per minute is about 1.5 USD per hour of continuous combat at the published price. Low","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.encounterHeartbeatTicks","u":"config-reference.html#decision.encounterHeartbeatTicks","x":" Routine decision rhythm of an encounter: one request per encounter at most this often, or sooner when something relevant happens. Must be at least profileDefaults.minimumDecisionIntervalTicks. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.contingenciesPerMob","u":"config-reference.html#decision.contingenciesPerMob","x":" Extra \"what if\" questions per mob in each request (for example \"if your health becomes critical\"). The answer is kept and used at once if that situation happens. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.minimumConfidence","u":"config-reference.html#decision.minimumConfidence","x":" Default confidence an answer needs to be adopted (profiles can set Timing.MinimumConfidence). Answers below it are discarded and the mob keeps its current plan or plays locally. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tacticSwitchMargin","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tacticSwitchMargin","x":" Default probability margin a new tactic needs over the current one before the mob switches (profiles can set Timing.SwitchMargin). Prevents flip-flopping between two close options. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxInstallsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxInstallsPerTick","x":" Movement goal installations per tick, when bound mobs spawn or reload. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxEncounterEvaluationsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxEncounterEvaluationsPerTick","x":" Encounters that may prepare a request in one tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxProbesPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxProbesPerTick","x":" Cheap per-mob checks per tick. Lower it if the tick_work latency in /thepredict status nears 2 ms at p95. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxCompletionsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxCompletionsPerTick","x":" Answers applied per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxSignalsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxSignalsPerTick","x":"predictordecide requests handled per tick.","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxTickWorkMicros","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxTickWorkMicros","x":" Work budget of ThePredict inside one server tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.lowConfidenceStreakForLocal","u":"config-reference.html#decision.lowConfidenceStreakForLocal","x":" Low-confidence answers in a row before the mob drops to its local planner (fallback reason LOW_CONFIDENCE). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.searchRadiusBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#decision.searchRadiusBlocks","x":" Safety cap on how far a mob perceives participants. Each mob uses its MythicMobs Options.FollowRange, never more than this. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.logDecisions","u":"config-reference.html#decision.logDecisions","x":" Logs every decision, fallback, cast result, threat change and closed outcome window to the console (at most 20 lines every 10 seconds). Useful while tuning a boss; noisy on a live server. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxOptionsPerQuestion","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxOptionsPerQuestion","x":" Most options in one question to Jev, after identical tactics are merged. The mob's current tactic is never cut, so the switch margin can still compare against it. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.questionDetail","u":"config-reference.html#decision.questionDetail","x":" How much each option tells Jev, and so how much it costs. full adds what favors or hurts each option right now; compact is a short text and costs about half. Profiles can choose their own with Timing.QuestionDetail. No level ever widens th","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.fitChecks","u":"config-reference.html#decision.fitChecks","x":" Default of Timing.FitChecks: one extra yes/no \"does this option fit now?\" question per option, in the same request. Sent only with full detail. Costs tokens. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.fitChecksAllowed","u":"config-reference.html#decision.fitChecksAllowed","x":"false forbids fit checks everywhere: a profile with Timing.FitChecks: true then fails to load.","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.fitVeto","u":"config-reference.html#decision.fitVeto","x":" Fit below this value vetoes an option. Must be lower than decision.fitRescue. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.fitRescue","u":"config-reference.html#decision.fitRescue","x":" Fit at or above this value lets a single option rescue a low-confidence answer. Must be higher than decision.fitVeto. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.castMode","u":"config-reference.html#decision.castMode","x":" Which skills fire as soon as they are ready. any_ready: every skill with a valid Intention line fires on the first tick it is ready (on its own cooldown), besides the tactic's choice. intent_only: only the chosen tactic's skill fires. A pr","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.castThread","u":"config-reference.html#decision.castThread","x":" Thread a cast runs on. same_tick runs the skill's delay on the server thread, so delay 10 waits exactly 10 server ticks. mythic_default keeps the MythicMobs default. Global only. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.untypedCast","u":"config-reference.html#decision.untypedCast","x":" What a skill without a valid Intention line may do. tactic_only: it fires only as the choice of its own tactic. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.readyHorizonTicks","u":"config-reference.html#decision.readyHorizonTicks","x":" How many ticks ahead a skill still counts as available when ThePredict builds a question. 0 keeps the question to skills that are ready now. The local planner never reads it. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.pruning","u":"config-reference.html#decision.pruning","x":"off keeps the question order as is. safe drops options that cannot work right now and orders the rest by the local score. Quote \"off\": YAML reads a bare off as a boolean, which ThePredict also accepts here.","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.candidateScoring","u":"config-reference.html#decision.candidateScoring","x":" How the local engine ranks candidate tactics. priority uses the tactic Priority and its situational tie-breaks; utility multiplies that score by the enemy-pattern factor, so a counter to a detected pattern can rise; learned multiplies it b","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.confidenceGate","u":"config-reference.html#decision.confidenceGate","x":" Whether decision.minimumConfidence compares Jev's raw confidence or a calibrated probability. The default, raw, keeps the threshold as is. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.minimumCalibratedConfidence","u":"config-reference.html#decision.minimumCalibratedConfidence","x":" Threshold used with confidenceGate: calibrated. parity accepts exactly what the raw threshold accepts. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.candidateDiversity","u":"config-reference.html#decision.candidateDiversity","x":" Meant to show each movement's best option first, so similar tactics do not crowd out different ones. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.answerCache","u":"config-reference.html#decision.answerCache","x":" Reuse of an identical earlier answer. shadow only measures; on reuses exact answers once its evaluation gate passes, which this release does not reach. Keep it \"off\". ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.answerCacheTtlTicks","u":"config-reference.html#decision.answerCacheTtlTicks","x":" How long a cached answer stays valid. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.answerCacheEntries","u":"config-reference.html#decision.answerCacheEntries","x":" Most cached answers (there is also a cap of 8 000 000 characters). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.answerCacheRevalidateRatio","u":"config-reference.html#decision.answerCacheRevalidateRatio","x":" Share of cache hits that are also sent to Jev to check the cache. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxDecisionAgeMillis","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxDecisionAgeMillis","x":" Oldest answer that may still be applied. Not in the shipped file; add it only to override the default. Must be at least jev.timeoutMillis. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.maxReadyChecksPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.maxReadyChecksPerTick","x":"Obsolete. An old file that still has it starts with an INFO line and nothing changes; the live cap is decision.tickLayer.maxSessionsPerTick. You can delete it.","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.mode","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.mode","x":" What the per-tick layer does. casts: only fires ready skills. reactions: also reacts within ticks (dodge pressure, punish a drinking target, finish a low target). full: also runs short micro-movements (circle, step in, back off). off is an","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.maxSessionsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.maxSessionsPerTick","x":" Mobs the tick layer visits per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.maxMicros","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.maxMicros","x":" Time budget of the tick layer inside one tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.guardMspt","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.guardMspt","x":" MSPT guard. When the previous server tick ran late, or the average tick time passes this value, the tick layer drops to a lighter step for the next tick (casting is never delayed). 0 turns the guard off. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.microMinHoldTicks","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.microMinHoldTicks","x":" Shortest time one micro-movement holds before another may replace it (full only). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.waypointRefreshTicks","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.waypointRefreshTicks","x":" How often an orbit waypoint is refreshed (full only). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.maxWaypointPathsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.maxWaypointPathsPerTick","x":" Short paths computed per tick for micro-movements. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"decision.tickLayer.maxWaypointPathMicrosPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#decision.tickLayer.maxWaypointPathMicrosPerTick","x":" Time budget for those paths per tick. One path may pass the budget; the next one waits. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"debug.recordScenarios","u":"config-reference.html#debug.recordScenarios","x":" Saves every decision Jev answered as an anonymized scenario file under plugins/ThePredict/scenarios/ (at most 1 000 files per start). For calibration work; keep it off on a live server. See Storage & records. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"debug.seed","u":"config-reference.html#debug.seed","x":" Base seed of ThePredict's deterministic random numbers. The same seed and the same tick give the same number. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.observationIntervalTicks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.observationIntervalTicks","x":" How often each mob runs its cheap checks (reach, conditions, ready skills). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.minimumDecisionIntervalTicks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.minimumDecisionIntervalTicks","x":" Shortest time an adopted tactic is kept before another may replace it. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.maximumIntentDurationTicks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.maximumIntentDurationTicks","x":" How long an intent stays valid without being renewed. Must be at least profileDefaults.minimumDecisionIntervalTicks. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.criticalHealthRatio","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.criticalHealthRatio","x":" Health ratio (health plus absorption over max health) at or below which a creature is CRITICAL. Applies to mobs and players. Profiles: Health.Critical. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.woundedHealthRatio","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.woundedHealthRatio","x":" At or below this ratio (and above critical) a creature is WOUNDED; above it, HEALTHY. Profiles: Health.Wounded. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.meleeReachBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.meleeReachBlocks","x":" Melee distance: the MELEE band, where APPROACH stops, and the reach of melee skills. Profiles: Movement.MeleeReach. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.bandInnerBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.bandInnerBlocks","x":" Inner edge of the KEEP_DISTANCE band. Profiles: Movement.Band.Inner. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.bandOuterBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.bandOuterBlocks","x":" Outer edge of the KEEP_DISTANCE band. Profiles: Movement.Band.Outer. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.rangedReachBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.rangedReachBlocks","x":" Up to this distance the target is in the RANGED band; farther, BEYOND. Profiles: Movement.RangedReach. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.retreatDistanceBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.retreatDistanceBlocks","x":" Distance a RETREAT tries to open. Profiles: Movement.Retreat.Distance. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.retreatSpeed","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.retreatSpeed","x":" Speed multiplier while retreating. Profiles: Movement.Retreat.Speed. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"profileDefaults.approachSpeed","u":"config-reference.html#profileDefaults.approachSpeed","x":" Speed multiplier while approaching, keeping distance and walking back to the arena. Profiles: Movement.Approach.Speed. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants.playerGameModes","u":"config-reference.html#participants.playerGameModes","x":" Players in these game modes can be perceived, targeted and fought. [] means no player at all. A profile can only narrow this list (Participants.PlayerGameModes). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants.entities.allow","u":"config-reference.html#participants.entities.allow","x":" Selectors of non-player living entities that may take part (see Targets, participants & threat). Empty means none, the default behavior. Profiles add their own with Participants.Entities.Allow. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants.entities.deny","u":"config-reference.html#participants.entities.deny","x":" Selectors that never take part, even when a profile allows them. Profiles add their own. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants.entities.profilesMayAllow","u":"config-reference.html#participants.entities.profilesMayAllow","x":" With false, the Allow lists of profiles are ignored with a load warning and only this file's list counts. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants.entities.perceiveNonTargets","u":"config-reference.html#participants.entities.perceiveNonTargets","x":" With false, a mob perceives only its own target among non-player entities, at no extra cost. With true, each mob also perceives allowed entities nearby (one nearby-entity query per mob). A profile can turn it on only while this is true. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"participants.entities.maxCandidatesPerMember","u":"config-reference.html#participants.entities.maxCandidatesPerMember","x":" With perceiveNonTargets, the nearest non-target entities each mob reads per capture. The cap of 16 participants per encounter covers players and entities together. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.level","u":"config-reference.html#records.level","x":" How much of each fight is written to the JSONL records. decisions writes decisions and tells; full also writes casts, threat, reactions, micro-movements and stances. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.bodies","u":"config-reference.html#records.bodies","x":" How request bodies are kept in the records: not at all, as a hash, deduplicated, or in full. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.directory","u":"config-reference.html#records.directory","x":" Records folder, relative to plugins/ThePredict/. An absolute path or one with .. is rejected. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.queueCapacity","u":"config-reference.html#records.queueCapacity","x":" Events that may wait for the writer thread. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.segmentMegabytes","u":"config-reference.html#records.segmentMegabytes","x":" A record file rotates when it reaches this size. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.segmentMinutes","u":"config-reference.html#records.segmentMinutes","x":" A record file rotates when it reaches this age. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.compressClosedSegments","u":"config-reference.html#records.compressClosedSegments","x":" Gzips each closed segment; the original is deleted only after the .gz closes correctly. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.retentionDays","u":"config-reference.html#records.retentionDays","x":" Days of records kept. The current day is never deleted. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.maxTotalMegabytes","u":"config-reference.html#records.maxTotalMegabytes","x":" Size cap of the records folder. If the current day alone passes it, events pause and the aggregates keep working. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"records.patternSummaryBinary","u":"config-reference.html#records.patternSummaryBinary","x":" Adds a compact binary copy (summary_b64) to each pattern summary line in the records. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.defaultMode","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.defaultMode","x":" How a mob chooses its pressure when its profile does not say. player: a controller aims the whole fight at the preset's target length. bench: full power, no controller. auto: player against players and bench against other entities. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.defaultPreset","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.defaultPreset","x":" Preset of a mob whose file has no PredictorDifficulty. Case and accents are ignored. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.adjustIntervalTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.adjustIntervalTicks","x":" How often the in-fight controller may move the pressure rung (spread across sessions). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.toleranceRatio","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.toleranceRatio","x":" Band around the target time inside which the in-fight controller does not react. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.deadbandRatio","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.deadbandRatio","x":" Band inside which the between-fights learning does not move the starting rung. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.learningGain","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.learningGain","x":" How fast the between-fights learning moves the starting rung (clipped to 0.33 by the ladder). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.projectedTtkCapRatio","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.projectedTtkCapRatio","x":" Cap of a projected time-to-kill, as a multiple of the target time. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.dampingReversals","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.dampingReversals","x":" Sign changes in the last ten fights that halve the learning gain. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.estimatorHalfLifeTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.estimatorHalfLifeTicks","x":" Half-life of the damage-rate estimate, for a 45-second target; it scales with the target time. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.minEvidenceTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.minEvidenceTicks","x":" Fight time before the estimate counts. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.disengageTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.disengageTicks","x":" A fight closes after this long without the mob dealing damage. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.maxTrackedFights","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.maxTrackedFights","x":" Fight clocks kept per mob. The one quiet for longest is dropped, never the current target's. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.nativeLevelAllowed","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.nativeLevelAllowed","x":" With true, a profile with Difficulty.NativeLevel: spawn may move the MythicMobs level of the next spawn by ±1 (within the mob's level ±2). Never during a fight. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.worlds","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.worlds","x":" Per-world overrides, keyed by world name: difficulty.worlds.<world>.preset (a preset name) and difficulty.worlds.<world>.entropy (true or false). A world override beats the mob file. Players never choose the difficulty. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.facil.targetMinutes","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.facil.targetMinutes","x":" Target length of a whole fight against players for the Fácil preset. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.facil.reactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.facil.reactionFloorTicks","x":" Shortest reaction delay against players for Fácil. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.facil.entropyReactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.facil.entropyReactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor reached while PredictorEntropy is on. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.facil.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.facil.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","x":" With Entropy, the adaptation time at the start of the fight; it shrinks toward zero as the fight goes on. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.normal.targetMinutes","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.normal.targetMinutes","x":" Target fight length for Normal. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.normal.reactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.normal.reactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor against players for Normal. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.normal.entropyReactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.normal.entropyReactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor with Entropy for Normal. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.normal.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.normal.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","x":" Entropy adaptation at the start of the fight for Normal. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.dificil.targetMinutes","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.dificil.targetMinutes","x":" Target fight length for Difícil. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.dificil.reactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.dificil.reactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor against players for Difícil. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.dificil.entropyReactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.dificil.entropyReactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor with Entropy for Difícil. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.dificil.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.dificil.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","x":" Entropy adaptation at the start of the fight for Difícil. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.caos.targetMinutes","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.caos.targetMinutes","x":" Target fight length for Caos. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.caos.reactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.caos.reactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor against players for Caos. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.caos.entropyReactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.caos.entropyReactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor with Entropy for Caos. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.caos.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.caos.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","x":" Entropy adaptation at the start of the fight for Caos. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.vacio.targetMinutes","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.vacio.targetMinutes","x":" Target fight length for Vacío. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.vacio.reactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.vacio.reactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor against players for Vacío. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.vacio.entropyReactionFloorTicks","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.vacio.entropyReactionFloorTicks","x":" Reaction floor with Entropy for Vacío. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"difficulty.presets.vacio.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","u":"config-reference.html#difficulty.presets.vacio.entropyAdaptStartSeconds","x":" Entropy adaptation at the start of the fight for Vacío. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.aggregates","u":"config-reference.html#storage.aggregates","x":" The aggregates database. mysql is reserved and refused at load. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.file","u":"config-reference.html#storage.file","x":" Database file name, written beside the records folder (not inside it). A plain file name, no slashes. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.synchronous","u":"config-reference.html#storage.synchronous","x":" SQLite synchronous setting. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.busyTimeoutMillis","u":"config-reference.html#storage.busyTimeoutMillis","x":" SQLite busy timeout. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.flushIntervalTicks","u":"config-reference.html#storage.flushIntervalTicks","x":" How often pending aggregates are written. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.maxPendingKeys","u":"config-reference.html#storage.maxPendingKeys","x":" Aggregate keys that may wait for the next flush. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.backupEveryHours","u":"config-reference.html#storage.backupEveryHours","x":" Database backup interval. 0 turns backups off. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"storage.backupsKept","u":"config-reference.html#storage.backupsKept","x":" Backups kept; older ones are deleted. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.againstPlayers","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.againstPlayers","x":" With enforce, every MEDIUM, HEAVY or SEVERE hit against a player is announced for at least its minimum (the danger minimum, plus the answer time, plus the delivery margin) through the tell signals. While Entropy is on, minimums do not appl","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.againstEntities","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.againstEntities","x":" The same, against non-player targets. Profiles: Telegraph.AgainstEntities. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.deliveryMarginTicks","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.deliveryMarginTicks","x":" Margin added to every enforced tell for signal delivery. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.maxReleasesPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.maxReleasesPerTick","x":" Tells released in one tick, server-wide. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.whiffRecoveryTicks","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.whiffRecoveryTicks","x":" Recovery after a whiffed, lost or rejected tell. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.whiffCooldownTicks","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.whiffCooldownTicks","x":" Cooldown of that skill after a whiff or a feint. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.resultWindowTicks","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.resultWindowTicks","x":" Ticks watched after the impact to read whether the hit landed (40 for projectiles). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.minTicks.light","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.minTicks.light","x":" Minimum tell of a LIGHT hit. Light hits are not enforced. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.minTicks.medium","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.minTicks.medium","x":" Minimum tell of a MEDIUM hit. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.minTicks.heavy","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.minTicks.heavy","x":" Minimum tell of a HEAVY hit. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.minTicks.severe","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.minTicks.severe","x":" Minimum tell of a SEVERE hit. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.answerTicks.block","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.answerTicks.block","x":" Extra ticks added when the expected answer is to block. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.answerTicks.dodge","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.answerTicks.dodge","x":" Extra ticks when the answer is a sidestep. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.answerTicks.backOff","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.answerTicks.backOff","x":" Extra ticks when the answer is to leave reach. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.answerTicks.breakSight","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.answerTicks.breakSight","x":" Extra ticks when the answer is to break line of sight. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"telegraph.answerTicks.interrupt","u":"config-reference.html#telegraph.answerTicks.interrupt","x":" Extra ticks when the answer is to interrupt the wind-up. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"stance.nativeMode","u":"config-reference.html#stance.nativeMode","x":" How ThePredict shares the stance with MythicMobs. hybrid writes the variable predictor_stance and reads the mob's own stance, never calling setStance. read only reads. write calls setStance. off neither reads nor writes. Profiles: Stances.","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"stance.minDwellTicks","u":"config-reference.html#stance.minDwellTicks","x":" Shortest time a base stance holds before it changes. Profiles: Stances.MinDwellTicks. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"stance.hysteresisCycles","u":"config-reference.html#stance.hysteresisCycles","x":" Reactive cycles in a row (2 ticks each) a new base stance must be asked for before it applies. Profiles: Stances.HysteresisCycles. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.mode","u":"config-reference.html#zone.mode","x":" How far terrain reading may change a fight. off: no zone is built. observe: the zone is built and, against players, the push policy and tell feasibility apply. guard: the mob also refuses unsafe ground. full: terrain facts also reach Jev, ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.defaultRadiusBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.defaultRadiusBlocks","x":" Radius of the zone read around a fight when the profile sets none. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxRadiusBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxRadiusBlocks","x":" Largest zone radius, including an arena (whose zone is the arena radius plus 4). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.bandBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.bandBlocks","x":" Vertical half-band read above and below. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxZones","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxZones","x":" Encounters that may hold a zone map at the same time. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxSnapshotsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxSnapshotsPerTick","x":" Chunk snapshots taken on the server thread per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxConcurrentBuilds","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxConcurrentBuilds","x":" Zone builds queued to the zone thread. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxDropScanBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxDropScanBlocks","x":" How far down a drop is followed. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxMicrosPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxMicrosPerTick","x":" Time budget of the zone step per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxColumnReadsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxColumnReadsPerTick","x":" Live column reads per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.minColumnRefreshTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.minColumnRefreshTicks","x":" Shortest gap between two reads of the same column. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxDirtyQueue","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxDirtyQueue","x":" Changed columns that may wait for a patch. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.dirtyRebuildThreshold","u":"config-reference.html#zone.dirtyRebuildThreshold","x":" Changed columns that force a full rebuild instead of patches. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.verifyIntervalTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.verifyIntervalTicks","x":" How often a busy zone is fully re-checked. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.idleDropTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.idleDropTicks","x":" An idle zone map is dropped after this long. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxQueriesPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxQueriesPerTick","x":" Terrain queries answered per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.knockbackDepthBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.knockbackDepthBlocks","x":" How far a knockback is assumed to carry when ThePredict checks where a push would land. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.strongPushDepthBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.strongPushDepthBlocks","x":" How far a strong push (throw, leap, explosion) is assumed to carry. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxSafeDropBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxSafeDropBlocks","x":" The biggest drop that is still safe. An edge is a drop bigger than this (4 blocks or more with the default). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.factPeriodTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.factPeriodTicks","x":" How often terrain facts are sampled. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.factOnTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.factOnTicks","x":" A fact must hold this long before it turns on. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.factOffTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.factOffTicks","x":" A fact must be gone this long before it turns off. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.maxFactsPerMob","u":"config-reference.html#zone.maxFactsPerMob","x":" Terrain facts sent to Jev for one mob. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.pushDeferTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.pushDeferTicks","x":" How long one deferral of a dangerous push lasts. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.pushDeferMaxTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.pushDeferMaxTicks","x":" A deferred push is skipped after this long. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.pushAttributionTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.pushAttributionTicks","x":" How long a push stays attributed to the mob that caused it. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.answerRetryTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.answerRetryTicks","x":" Retry interval while the terrain makes a tell's answer impossible (for example, no room to back off). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"zone.answerMaxWaitTicks","u":"config-reference.html#zone.answerMaxWaitTicks","x":" A tell whose answer stays impossible is dropped after this long. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.mode","u":"config-reference.html#group.mode","x":" How far mobs of one encounter coordinate. off: no group step. fair: attack tokens and impact spacing per player. coordinate: also a plan, roles and positions, but in this build a plan is only adopted with the group plan question, so it beh","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxSquads","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxSquads","x":" Squads kept in one encounter, in order: declared squad names first, then each member whose summons are in the encounter, which heads a squad with them. Members of any further squad join the remainder, like a mob without a squad. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.brokenTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.brokenTicks","x":" How long a group stays broken after its leader dies with OnLeaderDeath: break. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.arbitrationPeriodTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.arbitrationPeriodTicks","x":" How often roles and tokens are re-arbitrated. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.replanPeriodTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.replanPeriodTicks","x":" How often roles are reassigned while the group has a plan; a change of members also triggers it. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxReplansPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxReplansPerTick","x":" Group replans per world per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxMicrosPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxMicrosPerTick","x":" Time budget of the group step per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxMeleeAttackersPerPlayer","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxMeleeAttackersPerPlayer","x":" Melee attack weight that may press one player at once (each member uses its Group.Weight). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxRangedAttackersPerPlayer","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxRangedAttackersPerPlayer","x":" Ranged attack weight that may shoot one player at once. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.minImpactGapTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.minImpactGapTicks","x":" Shortest gap between two impacts on the same player. The floor of 4 is fixed. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.tokenIdleTimeoutTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.tokenIdleTimeoutTicks","x":" An attack token that is not used returns after this long. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.stealMarginMillis","u":"config-reference.html#group.stealMarginMillis","x":" Score advantage a member needs to take a token from another. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.idleWarnTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.idleWarnTicks","x":" A member left without a token this long is reported. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.roleSwitchMarginMillis","u":"config-reference.html#group.roleSwitchMarginMillis","x":" Cost of changing a member's role, so roles do not flicker. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.exitSectorDegrees","u":"config-reference.html#group.exitSectorDegrees","x":" Sector behind the player that the group leaves open. The floor of 60 is fixed. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.lkpForgetTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.lkpForgetTicks","x":" While no member sees its target, the group can offer the search_last_known plan if a member saw it at most this long ago. Only matters when the group plan question is asked (full). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxMediumTellsPerPlayer","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxMediumTellsPerPlayer","x":" Open MEDIUM tells on one player at once. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.bigImpactSpacingTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.bigImpactSpacingTicks","x":" Spacing around a HEAVY or SEVERE impact on the same player. The floor of 8 is fixed. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.leaderReserveTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.leaderReserveTicks","x":" How early the leader's impact slot is reserved. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.projectileFlightMarginTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.projectileFlightMarginTicks","x":" Widening of a projectile's impact window to cover flight time. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxPlanCandidates","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxPlanCandidates","x":" Most plans offered in one group plan question: at most one per family (attack, protect, retreat, search), with the local plan first. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.minPlanTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.minPlanTicks","x":" Shortest time a chosen plan holds. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.planHorizonTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.planHorizonTicks","x":" A plan expires after this long. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.assignmentThreatMargin","u":"config-reference.html#group.assignmentThreatMargin","x":" Threat added toward the target a group assigns to a member. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.factOnTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.factOnTicks","x":" A group fact must hold this long before it turns on. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.factOffTicks","u":"config-reference.html#group.factOffTicks","x":" A group fact must be gone this long before it turns off. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"group.maxFacts","u":"config-reference.html#group.maxFacts","x":" Group facts sent to Jev. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.mode","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.mode","x":" How far enemy-pattern reading may affect a fight. observe: detect and publish, decisions unchanged. bias: the local engine leans toward counters. full: also short phrases to Jev. bias and full stay at observe until an evaluation verdict is","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.hearingBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.hearingBlocks","x":" Meant as the range at which a mob hears enemy actions it cannot see. Today an action only counts when a member sees it. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.sampleTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.sampleTicks","x":" How often each watched enemy's movement is sampled. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxWatchedPerEncounter","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxWatchedPerEncounter","x":" Enemies read per encounter at every sample. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxReadsPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxReadsPerTick","x":" Movement reads of enemies per tick, across the whole server. A read that does not fit waits for a later tick and counts PATTERN_READS_DEFERRED in the totals line of /thepredict status. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.strafeBlocks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.strafeBlocks","x":" Sideways movement that counts as a strafe. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.airSwings","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.airSwings","x":" Whether swings at the air feed the patterns. Keep observe until it is verified on a server. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.mergeTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.mergeTicks","x":" Window that merges repeats of the same strafe or step. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.idleTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.idleTicks","x":" Inactivity that counts as an idle beat. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxTokensPerSecond","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxTokensPerSecond","x":" Most enemy actions recorded per second. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.order2Contexts","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.order2Contexts","x":" Rows of the second-order predictor (what follows two actions). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.forgetting","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.forgetting","x":" Forgetting factor of the action predictor (closer to 1 remembers longer). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.evidenceForgetting","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.evidenceForgetting","x":" Forgetting factor of the pattern evidence. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.confidenceQuantile","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.confidenceQuantile","x":" Tail probability a pattern's evidence must clear. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.minTrials","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.minTrials","x":" Observations before a pattern can activate. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.persistUpdates","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.persistUpdates","x":" Consecutive passing updates needed to activate. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.exitMargin","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.exitMargin","x":" Gap below the threshold that deactivates a pattern. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.changepointH","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.changepointH","x":" Change detector threshold: when the enemy's style changes, old evidence is dropped. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.forecastMinAccuracy","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.forecastMinAccuracy","x":" Running accuracy the forecast needs before <caster.predictor.forecast> shows it. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.histogramBinTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.histogramBinTicks","x":" Bin width of the reaction-time histogram. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxMicrosPerTick","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxMicrosPerTick","x":" Time budget of the pattern step per tick. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxExploitShare","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxExploitShare","x":" Largest share of casts in a window of patterns.exploitWindowTicks that a detected pattern may motivate against a player (bias and full). The pressure rung can lower it further. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxCounterDelayTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxCounterDelayTicks","x":" Longest delay a counter may wait for its moment. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.exploitWindowTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.exploitWindowTicks","x":" Window over which the exploit share is measured. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.restAfterSuccesses","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.restAfterSuccesses","x":" Successful counters in a row that open a rest. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.restTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.restTicks","x":" Length of that rest. When it ends, the pattern comes back active if the habit still holds (a new activation, with its signal in bias and full); otherwise it turns inactive. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxExploitedPatterns","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxExploitedPatterns","x":" Patterns exploited at the same time. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.factOnTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.factOnTicks","x":" A pattern fact must hold this long before it reaches Jev (full). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.factOffTicks","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.factOffTicks","x":" A pattern fact must be gone this long before it is dropped. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxFactsPerParticipant","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxFactsPerParticipant","x":" Pattern facts sent for one enemy. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"patterns.maxFactsPerRequest","u":"config-reference.html#patterns.maxFactsPerRequest","x":" Pattern facts in one whole request to Jev. Enemies are filled in order, each up to patterns.maxFactsPerParticipant, until this cap is used up. Only full sends pattern facts. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.allowUnverified","u":"config-reference.html#learning.allowUnverified","x":" With true, a mode or learned artifact without an evaluation verdict may activate, and every start warns with the path of learn/active.json. Keep false. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.collect","u":"config-reference.html#learning.collect","x":" Records outcome windows for learning. It never changes a decision or what is sent to Jev. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.scope","u":"config-reference.html#learning.scope","x":" Where learned values may act: bench (mob against mob and simulations) or all (also against players, which needs a passing evaluation verdict). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.baseScoring","u":"config-reference.html#learning.baseScoring","x":" Base score a learned value multiplies. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.trainingSources","u":"config-reference.html#learning.trainingSources","x":" Fight sources that train learned values. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.contextVersion","u":"config-reference.html#learning.contextVersion","x":" Version of the learning context. Only 2. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.maxContextKeysPerProfile","u":"config-reference.html#learning.maxContextKeysPerProfile","x":" Situation keys kept per profile; past the cap, fine keys fold into coarser ones. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.maxOpenWindowsPerSession","u":"config-reference.html#learning.maxOpenWindowsPerSession","x":" Outcome windows open at once per mob. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.creditShare","u":"config-reference.html#learning.creditShare","x":" Weight of the mob's own result in an outcome. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.groupCreditShare","u":"config-reference.html#learning.groupCreditShare","x":" Weight of the group's result. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.creditDecayPerWindow","u":"config-reference.html#learning.creditDecayPerWindow","x":" How fast credit fades over later windows. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.minWindowsForValue","u":"config-reference.html#learning.minWindowsForValue","x":" Windows a situation needs before its learned value is used. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.halfLifeDays","u":"config-reference.html#learning.halfLifeDays","x":" Half-life of old outcomes. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.weeksKept","u":"config-reference.html#learning.weeksKept","x":" Weeks of learning data kept. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.maxEntries","u":"config-reference.html#learning.maxEntries","x":" Size cap of the learning table. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.minValueSpreadMillis","u":"config-reference.html#learning.minValueSpreadMillis","x":" Below this spread between options, the learned factor is 1 (it changes nothing). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.buildChunkRows","u":"config-reference.html#learning.buildChunkRows","x":" Rows read per slice while building an artifact. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.exploreInDuels","u":"config-reference.html#learning.exploreInDuels","x":" With true, mob-against-mob duels may explore other tactics. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.voiSkip","u":"config-reference.html#learning.voiSkip","x":" Skipping a question to Jev when the local answer is very likely the same. shadow only measures; on waits for its evaluation gate. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.jevHint","u":"config-reference.html#learning.jevHint","x":" In shadow, a hint for Jev is computed and stored in the records but never sent; the request is the same as with off. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.groupPlans","u":"config-reference.html#learning.groupPlans","x":" Reserved. Only \"off\". ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.exploration.policy","u":"config-reference.html#learning.exploration.policy","x":" Exploration policy. Only epsilon. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.exploration.epsilon","u":"config-reference.html#learning.exploration.epsilon","x":" Probability of exploring another tactic, where exploration is allowed (see PredictorTraining). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.exploration.maxShare","u":"config-reference.html#learning.exploration.maxShare","x":" Largest share of adoptions that may be explorations. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.calibration.minDecisions","u":"config-reference.html#learning.calibration.minDecisions","x":" Labelled decisions needed before confidence calibration. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.calibration.priorStrength","u":"config-reference.html#learning.calibration.priorStrength","x":" Strength of the calibration prior. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.calibration.driftReferenceWindows","u":"config-reference.html#learning.calibration.driftReferenceWindows","x":" Reference windows of the calibration drift detector. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.voi.minWindows","u":"config-reference.html#learning.voi.minWindows","x":" Windows a situation needs before a skip is considered. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.voi.minAgreement","u":"config-reference.html#learning.voi.minAgreement","x":" Lower bound of agreement with Jev needed to skip. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.voi.maxExpectedGain","u":"config-reference.html#learning.voi.maxExpectedGain","x":" Largest expected gain of asking that still allows a skip. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"learning.voi.maxConsecutiveSkips","u":"config-reference.html#learning.voi.maxConsecutiveSkips","x":" Skips in a row before a question is sent anyway. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"autoconfig.initialConfigs","u":"config-reference.html#autoconfig.initialConfigs","x":" Size of the first round of an offline configuration search (includes the current one and the defaults). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"autoconfig.initialPairs","u":"config-reference.html#autoconfig.initialPairs","x":" Fight pairs in the first round. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"autoconfig.eta","u":"config-reference.html#autoconfig.eta","x":" Reduction factor between rounds. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"autoconfig.maxPairs","u":"config-reference.html#autoconfig.maxPairs","x":" Most fight pairs in a search. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"autoconfig.maxMinutes","u":"config-reference.html#autoconfig.maxMinutes","x":" Longest search time. ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"autoconfig.autoApply","u":"config-reference.html#autoconfig.autoApply","x":" Only \"off\": nothing is ever applied automatically. Overlays are applied by hand with /thepredict autoconfig apply (see Profile overlays). ","k":"key","p":"config.yml reference"},{"t":"How do I report a bug?","u":"faq.html#bug","x":"Send the output of /thepredict status and /thepredict inspect nearest, the console lines around the problem (turn on decision.logDecisions for the decision log), the profile, the mob and skill files, and your Java, Paper and MythicMobs versions. Never share your key or any file that holds it. ThePredict never prints the key, so its own output is safe to share. See Troubleshooting & status.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Does it work with Folia?","u":"faq.html#folia","x":"No. ThePredict needs Paper 26.2, Java 25 and MythicMobs Premium 5.13.1 or newer.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Is it fair to players?","u":"faq.html#fair","x":"Changing soon Today a fight against players runs under fairness rules: minimum tell lengths before heavy hits, attack tokens and spacing between hits when several mobs gang up, no lethal pushes, limits on exploiting a player's habits, and a difficulty controller that aims the fight at a target length. These rules are about to be redefined as intelligence levels. See Difficulty, Stances, tells & poise and Groups for how each works in the current build.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Does it see through walls?","u":"faq.html#perception","x":"No. A mob only considers participants within its FollowRange (capped by decision.searchRadiusBlocks), sees a player's shield, drawn bow, held item and effects only with a line of sight and only if the player is not invisible, and Jev receives distance bands and aliases (player_1), never coordinates, names or UUIDs. See Targets, participants & threat.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Does it read players' keyboard input?","u":"faq.html#input","x":"No. A player's tendency (strafing, backing off, chasing) is read from their observed movement, never from raw input. MythicMobs' own input condition is your choice in your skills; ThePredict does not read it. See Patterns.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Do I have to write in English?","u":"faq.html#english","x":"Objective, tactic IDs and Description reach Jev, which reads English best. The catalog warns, without blocking, when a text looks like another language. Choice and context IDs never leave the server.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Do I need to restart after a change?","u":"faq.html#restart","x":"For config.yml and the key, yes: they are read only at startup. Profiles, mobs and skills only need /mm reload.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"How do I turn it off for one mob?","u":"faq.html#disable","x":"Set Predictor: false in the mob file (or remove its profile) and run /mm reload. ThePredict releases the mob and MythicMobs puts its own goals back. To remove ThePredict entirely, take the JAR out and restart. See Install & requirements.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Why does my boss hit less than the classic version?","u":"faq.html#melee","x":"While ThePredict controls a mob, its base melee goal does not hit; ThePredict adds no automatic vanilla hits. Put the melee damage in a skill of a tactic, or add a Kind: VANILLA_MELEE choice, which hits at most once every 20 ticks like vanilla. Tune that skill's Cooldown and damage when you compare with a classic boss.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"How do I make a skill fire only during one tactic?","u":"faq.html#one-tactic","x":"With the default CastMode: any_ready, every skill with a valid Intention line fires as soon as it is ready. To tie a skill to its tactic, pick one: add - predictortactic{t=<tactic>} true to the skill's Conditions (ThePredict checks them before casting and waits while they fail); leave the skill without an Intention line: an untyped skill only fires as the choice of its own tactic; set Timing.CastMode to intent_only for the whole profile.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Can mobs fight other mobs?","u":"faq.html#mob-vs-mob","x":"Yes. Allow other living entities as participants (participants.entities.allow or the profile's Participants.Entities.Allow), give the mob a native target selector such as nearestOtherFactionMonsters, and use MythicMobs factions or scoreboard teams to set the sides. /thepredict duel records such fights. See Targets, participants & threat.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"What about flying or swimming mobs?","u":"faq.html#flyers","x":"Not recommended yet. Flyers and swimmers that are regular creatures do get movement goals, but their movement has not been tested.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Which mobs work?","u":"faq.html#mobs","x":"Any MythicMobs mob with Predictor: true and a profile whose MythicID names it. This release targets ground mobs. Species with a Brain (piglins, hoglins, wardens, villagers, breezes, frogs, goats and a few more) keep their own movement and only accept Movement: NONE tactics, so ThePredict still picks and casts their skills. Slimes, magma cubes, ghasts, phantoms and bats keep their MythicMobs AI entirely. See Movement & goals.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Can players see it?","u":"faq.html#players","x":"Players only see the mob fight differently. ThePredict sends them no messages and they have no command. Whatever they see or hear on a decision comes from your skills, for example a line on ~onSignal:PREDICTOR_RETREAT_AND_DEFEND.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Does ThePredict change my skills or add effects?","u":"faq.html#effects","x":"No. It never edits MythicMobs files and never adds particles, sounds, glow or animations. It decides when and how your skills come out, and it publishes signals (PREDICTOR_*), conditions and placeholders your own skills can react to. Every visual or sound the player sees comes from your skills. Even /thepredict intention suggest only prints lines for you to copy.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"What does it cost?","u":"faq.html#cost","x":"Only Jev's input tokens are billed; the output is free. At the price published when this release was tested (0.042 USD per million input tokens, which TypeSafe may change), a lone mob in continuous combat measured about 1 884 tokens per request with the default full detail: about 0.28 USD per hour at one request per heartbeat, or 0.14 USD with compact. The default reactive cadence asks more often, up to about 0.95 USD per mob and hour in the worst case. decision.maxInputTokensPerMinute caps the total (the shipped cap is about 1.5 USD per hour at most); mobs over budget simply play locally. /thepredict status shows a live hourly estimate.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Do I need a TypeSafe key?","u":"faq.html#key","x":"No. Without a key ThePredict never contacts any service: bound mobs fight with the local planner of their profile, at no cost, and MythicMobs works as usual. With a key in the TYPESAFE_API_KEY environment variable, Jev picks among the tactics your profile offers. See Jev connection.","k":"section","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"FAQ","u":"faq.html","x":"ThePredict 0.0.1 is a release candidate: these pages describe this build, checked against its source code, but it has not been verified on a live server yet. If your server behaves differently, report it (see the last question).","k":"page","p":"FAQ"},{"t":"Known limits","u":"changelog.html#v0-0-1-limits","x":"In-game behavior and host capacity are pending verification on a live server. Ground mobs only; species with a Brain only accept Movement: NONE; skills already started (delays, projectiles) are not cancelled. A stuck local mob repeats its PREDICTOR_<TACTIC> signal. Context conditions that need skill data (trigger, skill target, metadata) are always false. While ThePredict controls a mob, its base melee goal does not hit: put melee damage in a skill. Folia is not supported.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Migration from schema 1","u":"changelog.html#v0-0-1-migration","x":"There is no migration command, and ThePredict never changes your files. When it finds schema 1 files it loads nothing from them and writes a proposal (config.yml.proposed, the proposed profiles and report.md). Limits with an equivalent are carried over (for example decision.maxConcurrentRequests becomes decision.maxInFlightRequests), each choice becomes a tactic without movement, each Operation becomes the matching shortcut context and DirectChoice becomes DirectTactic. Apply it by hand, set TYPESAFE_API_KEY, start, run /thepredict status, and then add movements to the converted tactics.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Removed","u":"changelog.html#v0-0-1-removed","x":"The old provider based on OpenRouter and its provider section. The migrator only recognizes it to propose a migration; an old key is never copied.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Changed","u":"changelog.html#v0-0-1-changed","x":"config.yml and profiles use the strict schema 2: an unknown key is an error with the file and path. Defaults: decision.questionDetail: full and decision.minimumConfidence: 0.45, chosen from a labelled benchmark. A tactic's skill fires on its own Cooldown: every 2 ticks ThePredict checks whether it is ready again. Tune each skill's Cooldown to control spam. A vanilla hit keeps the vanilla rhythm of one hit every 20 ticks. The example skills and template use healthpercent{p=<30%}: health{h=…} compares absolute health and fails with % in MythicMobs 5.13.1. If you copied the example before, change those lines. Requests are prepared on the server thread before any budget is reserved; a request with nothing left to ask is not sent. A request that cannot be prepared only affects its own encounter and never pauses the service. The budget reserves tokens by the real size of each prepared request.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Added","u":"changelog.html#v0-0-1-added","x":"Direct Jev client (TypeSafe System One): a free service check (GET /v1/models) and one request per encounter with contingencies, an English combat summary with player aliases, and a size guard. Movement ownership. Movement goals generated from the profile and installed through the MythicMobs AI API, plus the Paper goals thepredict:hold, thepredict:flank and thepredict:owner. Sessions and encounters per mob, a per-tick coordinator with request, token and work budgets, and growing pauses when the service fails. Tactical execution with the four-level fallback chain (JEV, ALTERNATIVE, LOCAL, BASE), a re-check of reach and conditions before every skill, invulnerability frames, shields and flanking. MythicMobs vocabulary: predictorcontrol, predictormove, predictortactic, the predictordecide mechanic, <caster.predictor.*> placeholders and PREDICTOR_<TACTIC> signals. Enriched threat on top of the MythicMobs threat table: assists, blocked hits, ranged harassment and unreachable targets. Commands status, check, inspect and debug intent|release|goals, with thepredict.admin and thepredict.debug (off by default). Example boss ThePredictGuardian and a profile template, created on the first start without replacing anything. Skill purposes: what each skill is for, its reach and its risks, the cooldown class read from the native Cooldown, and a warning for tactics whose movement can never cast their skill. Better questions to Jev: identical tactics are merged (with a warning), at most 8 options per question with the current tactic always kept, three detail levels (compact, standard, full), ","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"0.0.1 · 2026-09-29 · candidate","u":"changelog.html#v0-0-1","x":"The first candidate: built and covered by automated tests, with the Jev client checked against the real TypeSafe account. Hosted acceptance on a Paper server is still pending.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Migration notes","u":"changelog.html#unreleased-migration","x":"If the old location (plugins/ThePredict/config.yml or plugins/ThePredict/AI/) has content and AIConfig/ has none, ThePredict loads nothing, enables no request and writes a proposal under plugins/ThePredict/migration/. Copy the .proposed files into plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/ by hand. If both locations have content, AIConfig/ wins and the old files are ignored. Nothing is ever moved or deleted. To move a profile from Purpose to Intention: run /thepredict intention suggest <profile>, copy each line into its skill, /mm reload, check that inspect shows origin=skill, then remove Purpose. Note Coming next The difficulty presets, Entropy, tells, the push policy toward players and the group fairness rules listed above will be redefined in an upcoming release, which replaces target-time difficulty with intelligence levels. The pages that describe them carry a changing soon mark.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Changed","u":"changelog.html#unreleased-changed","x":"A skill without a valid Intention line (and without an administrator Purpose) is untyped: it fires only as the choice of its own tactic. PredictValues no longer produce a purpose; they are kept as history. Purpose in a profile choice stays as an administrator override and wins over the skill's line. ThePredict no longer reads raw player input: a player's tendency comes from observed movement. decision.tickLayer.mode: off is an error; use casts. The shipped config.yml no longer has the obsolete decision.maxReadyChecksPerTick. An older file that still has it starts with an INFO line and nothing changes. /thepredict learn status shows collect and scope from the loaded config.yml. The ThePredict-Zone thread starts with the first zone build and stops after a second without work. Pattern summaries are written to the records. Performance improvements in hot paths.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Added","u":"changelog.html#unreleased-added","x":"Configuration in the MythicMobs folder. config.yml and the profiles now live in plugins/MythicMobs/AIConfig/ (config.yml and Profiles/). The first start creates the folder only when it is missing and never overwrites a file. Generated data stays in plugins/ThePredict/. See Install & requirements. The Intention line. Each MythicMobs skill says what it is for in one line (Intention: DAMAGE, MELEE, DAMAGE_MEDIUM, WHEN_TARGET_IN_MELEE). Vocabulary v2 has 43 primitives, including five ANSWER_* primitives for tells. Reach, radius, wind-up, cooldown and charges are still read from the native skill, not from the line. See Skills & intents. Skills fire on their own cooldown. With the new default decision.castMode: any_ready, every skill with a valid Intention line fires on the first tick it is ready, at the pace of its native Cooldown and Charges. intent_only keeps the 0.0.1 behavior (only the tactic's skill). Profiles choose with Timing.CastMode. /thepredict intention suggest [profile] prints the canonical Intention line of every bound choice. It never writes MythicMobs files. Per-tick layer. Between two decisions the mob reacts within ticks (evade at critical health, punish a drinking target, respect a raised shield, finish a low target) and, with full, runs short micro-movements. New: decision.tickLayer.*, the reactive cadence per profile (standard is the saving mode), debug.seed and /thepredict inspect <mob> tick. See How a fight runs. Records and aggregates. Append-only JSONL records in plugins/ThePredict/records/ (14 days, 2 GB by default) and a SQLite aggregates.db beside the","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Fixed (2026-10-17)","u":"changelog.html#unreleased-fixed","x":"PREDICTOR_PATTERN_<PATTERN> is now sent: once each time a pattern becomes active, to each mob of the encounter whose target is that enemy and that has a handler, and only in the bias and full pattern modes. See Patterns. A pattern's rest now ends after patterns.restTicks: the pattern comes back active if the habit still holds, which counts as a new activation and sends its signal again, or turns inactive otherwise. Before, a rested pattern stayed resting. The pattern statistics now count as activations only the moments a pattern becomes active. Group.Questions now decides which questions go to Jev in full: plan_and_leader and leader_only ask only the leader, plan_only sends only the group plan question, and members is unchanged. The other members keep playing locally. For five members, a plan_and_leader request went from about 22 400 to about 7 000 characters. See Groups. The search_last_known plan is offered when no member sees its target and one saw it at most group.lkpForgetTicks ago. Plan candidates are one per family, with the local plan first. An overlay's Timing.TickLayer above decision.tickLayer.mode is lowered to the global mode with a warning, like a profile's. The ANSWER_* primitive of an Intention line sets the answer of the skill's tell when the choice declares no Telegraph.Answer. patterns.maxExploitShare, patterns.maxReadsPerTick, patterns.maxFactsPerRequest, group.maxSquads, group.lkpForgetTicks and the profile key Group.Roles now take effect. Stances.Native, Difficulty.NativeLevel, Decision.Pruning and Decision.Diversity accept a bare off or on. eval verdic","k":"section","p":"Changelog"},{"t":"Unreleased · release candidate rc1 (2026-10-12) and later local changes","u":"changelog.html#unreleased","x":"No new version number or JAR yet: these changes sit on top of 0.0.1 and have not been verified on a live server.","k":"section","p":"Changelog"}];
